1
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:06,770
(Day 4, morning)

2
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,140
It's a strange question.

3
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:13,550
(Dormitory for Red)

4
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,220
"Decipher."

5
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,120
"Decipher the code."

6
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,160
What did it say "decipher?"

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,930
What are we supposed to decipher?

8
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:28,530
The lock is locked.
It must be unlocked with a key.

9
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:31,170
How is that possible?

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,300
It's certainly the tulip mania.

11
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,300
We're supposed to decipher something
with this.

12
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:36,970
What could that be?

13
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:43,950
After issuing around 400 diamonds today,

14
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:45,950
it'll be best if White starts a war.

15
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:51,650
Could someone from Team White
suggest going to war?

16
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,490
It would be hard to bring it up.

17
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,260
- Right. If there are many members,
- Right.

18
00:00:56,290 --> 00:00:59,460
- you have to sound and behave nicely.
- Right.

19
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,000
- The nice person has a better say.
- Right.

20
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,230
Their deal fell apart.

21
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:07,340
There will be a few in Team White
that feel annoyed.

22
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:12,340
Team Blue is away.

23
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,810
Are they talking with another team?
Shall we head out?

24
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:18,710
You wouldn't answer
no matter how many times we called.

25
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:21,320
- There was nobody inside.
- We met with them first.

26
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:22,620
We're pushovers right now.

27
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:24,190
Look at today's deals.

28
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:26,390
Based on the first deal of the day,

29
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,690
the pushover is identified.

30
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:29,290
Those two teams are making a deal.

31
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:32,730
I believe that we have to show
our presence in this situation.

32
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,400
Then,

33
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:37,330
the ones who feel mad
can start to have a better say.

34
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,200
- You're right about that.
- The White members...

35
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,370
- aren't fools.
- Right.

36
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,740
They pretend to be good-natured,

37
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:46,510
but I think they're hiding
an important piece of information.

38
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,780
This is what I think.

39
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,150
Let's say we are to go to war today.

40
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:56,880
By reason...

41
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,590
By reason,
we have to go against Team Blue.

42
00:01:58,590 --> 00:01:59,620
- Right.
- That's how it is.

43
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,920
We were asked to ally with them
on the first day.

44
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,060
We made a smooth deal with them as well.

45
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:04,560
They kept their mouths shut
the very next day...

46
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,060
and teamed up with Team Red...

47
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,600
after coming to us first on the first day.

48
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,330
On top of that, we trusted them...

49
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:12,370
- and paid them in advance.
- We even sold our credits.

50
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:14,170
- But they dishonored our deal?
- I know.

51
00:02:14,270 --> 00:02:16,370
- If that's the case,
- That's insane if you think about it.

52
00:02:16,370 --> 00:02:19,040
- that's so unprofessional.
- It's making me feel mad.

53
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:22,010
That's why we have a reason
to strike them first.

54
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:23,040
- Right.
- Right.

55
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:25,610
Anyway, we think it's better for us...

56
00:02:25,610 --> 00:02:27,080
- to ally with Team Blue.
- They're easy to deal with.

57
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,280
Is it solely because
they're easy to deal with...

58
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,650
or is it because
we can get a lot from them?

59
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:30,920
- We can get a lot from them as well.
- They're easy to deal with...

60
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,020
and we can get a lot from them.

61
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,960
We can also help them
with their skill development.

62
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:35,320
It's because they aren't a threat to us.

63
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:38,160
We can't help Team Red
with their skill development.

64
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,290
- They're dealing with a nuclear weapon.
- Right.

65
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,760
It's okay for us to help Team Blue.

66
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,630
The goal of war is to eliminate
our actual threat.

67
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:46,430
Our actual threat is Team Red.

68
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,800
If they produce a lot of credits,
they can reduce our lives.

69
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,970
They can do that right away.

70
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:51,910
- Right.
- That's their skill.

71
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:54,580
Right. So it's right for us
to eliminate our threat.

72
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:56,110
- That's a strategic approach.
- Right.

73
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,980
That's what war is for.

74
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,650
I thought that we had to strike Team Blue.

75
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:04,020
The goal of this war is to secure lives.

76
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,290
For us to secure lives,

77
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,660
we must strike Team Blue,

78
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:10,060
which has the most lives.

79
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:14,230
But during the morning meeting,

80
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,400
the idea we ended up with
was to ally with Team Blue...

81
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,530
and strike Team Red.

82
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:21,100
If I didn't feel persuaded by that idea,

83
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,740
I thought about striking Team Blue.

84
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:27,140
Lives are what we need the most.

85
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:31,010
If we have a good talk with Team Blue,
the team that has lives,

86
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:34,150
I thought that war could be avoided today.

87
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:35,750
I believe that...

88
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:38,620
war is something that doesn't benefit us.

89
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:40,590
It should happen only when...

90
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:43,120
another country tries to invade us.

91
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:46,330
We can be in a war
from a defensive stance,

92
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:50,800
but I believe trying to steal
for each other isn't ideal.

93
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,000
I want to head in a direction
in which all of us help each other.

94
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,770
- So that's...
- Right.

95
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,340
I think we're going to
go out after eating.

96
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,810
Day Four has begun.

97
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:04,550
Team leaders can now be changed.

98
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:09,480
Discuss whether to
reappoint the current leader.

99
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:12,490
The supermarket has reopened today.

100
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:13,850
- Yes!
- Yes!

101
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:15,360
We can finally eat.

102
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,490
After productive activities are over,
the supermarket can be used...

103
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:21,660
- starting from lunchtime.
- Right. We can't use it in the morning.

104
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,330
- This concludes the announcement...
- Good thing I had a banana.

105
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,570
from Community Center.

106
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,970
I think it'll be good for us
to talk about our leader situation.

107
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:30,000
I mentioned yesterday
about the leader holding information...

108
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,240
- and feeling pressure.
- Right.

109
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,540
I said that it would be good for a change
of leaders to prevent those things.

110
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:36,980
But we learned a lesson from Team Blue.

111
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:38,250
- A constant leadership change...
- Right.

112
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:40,680
or a bad takeover will put a team
in so much danger.

113
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,820
- Right.
- We unfortunately witnessed that.

114
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,020
Well,

115
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,990
we've been given certain roles...

116
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,620
- and have adjusted to them.
- Right.

117
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,560
If we force ourselves with a change,

118
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:52,230
the other team at the negotiation table
will also be confused.

119
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:54,430
It will confuse us as well, to be honest.

120
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,900
- But it will bring this effect.
- That will be the flow.

121
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,500
- If we change our leader today,
- Right.

122
00:04:58,070 --> 00:05:00,030
the other teams will feel
a greater threat of war.

123
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:01,970
- It will be easier to be with Team Blue.
- Why?

124
00:05:01,970 --> 00:05:03,670
- I also think...
- Do you think I'll start a war?

125
00:05:03,670 --> 00:05:05,910
- a change is needed.
- Right. That's your image.

126
00:05:05,910 --> 00:05:07,110
- That's why I think...
- Right.

127
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:09,280
- there's no need for a change today.
- Right.

128
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,780
When she made negotiations
with the other team,

129
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:15,350
she calmly persuaded them step by step.

130
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:18,090
If I were a Team Blue member,
I wouldn't have traded with our team.

131
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,760
- But she got them to sit with us.
- Right.

132
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,460
- And...
- That's Luna's strength.

133
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:23,960
- Right. That's her strength.
- Right.

134
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:26,430
I said this next to her on purpose.

135
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:27,600
"We can go to war,"

136
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,930
"and you can become our target."

137
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:33,230
- She was 7, and I was 3 to them.
- Right.

138
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:34,640
She became the good cop,
and I became the bad cop.

139
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:36,670
- And the pacifist joined in.
- Right.

140
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,040
After creating this situation,

141
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,740
- if I suddenly show up as a leader...
- Then, they will all get ready.

142
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,280
- "They're preparing for war."
- Right.

143
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,910
I'm a pacifist as well!

144
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:46,110
- Anyway, that ended up becoming my image.
- Right.

145
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:48,350
The leadership change might be seen...

146
00:05:48,350 --> 00:05:49,450
- as a signal.
- Right.

147
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:50,850
- Right.
- So Leia...

148
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,450
should use this as leverage.

149
00:05:52,450 --> 00:05:55,020
"If this carries on,"

150
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,190
"the hardliners of our team
will gain more power."

151
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,230
And naturally,

152
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:01,500
- I'm a good person!
- we can use this as an advantage.

153
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,700
- We've gained another weapon.
- Right.

154
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,500
So we'll carry on with our leader.

155
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,100
- We can stay if we do that.
- Right.

156
00:06:08,470 --> 00:06:10,240
For the benefit of our team,

157
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,110
- the one who leads our team...
- Right.

158
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:13,770
is quite important.

159
00:06:14,110 --> 00:06:16,980
We should discuss
who should be our leader.

160
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,180
Right now...

161
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:22,380
Do you want to be the leader? Or...

162
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:25,150
I do want to be the leader.

163
00:06:25,150 --> 00:06:26,850
I've tried talking
with the others yesterday.

164
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:29,620
There's a certain right...

165
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,460
- that a leader has.
- Actually,

166
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,560
when considering the role of a leader,

167
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:36,730
the main focus is making negotiations
with the other teams.

168
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,530
Up until now,

169
00:06:38,530 --> 00:06:41,340
I've done all of the negotiating...

170
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:44,740
and uncomfortable talks
with the other teams.

171
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,340
I was wondering if I could...

172
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:49,780
continue to take that role...

173
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:53,850
and represent our team.

174
00:06:54,550 --> 00:06:55,580
Right.

175
00:06:57,550 --> 00:07:00,020
Pitou naturally showed her desire...

176
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:03,090
of wanting to become the leader
since yesterday.

177
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:06,390
But to be honest,

178
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:08,030
I feel quite anxious about Pitou.

179
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:10,700
It felt like she kept trying to
threaten my position.

180
00:07:11,030 --> 00:07:14,370
"I should stop her from becoming
the leader."

181
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:15,870
This was the thought I got.

182
00:07:15,870 --> 00:07:18,240
That was why I went with,
"I want to be the leader."

183
00:07:18,670 --> 00:07:21,440
I thought that Genie
shouldn't be our leader.

184
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:23,110
Ultimately,

185
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:26,280
the fact that the leader
could affect our lives...

186
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,950
wasn't shared with us on the first day.

187
00:07:28,150 --> 00:07:29,680
I felt a chill down my spine.

188
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,450
I thought,
"The leader could get us killed."

189
00:07:32,050 --> 00:07:35,390
She was someone I felt anxious about,

190
00:07:35,390 --> 00:07:37,260
and I had to let her handle
this mission...

191
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:39,690
of having to submit our lives...

192
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:42,560
every single day.

193
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:46,670
I decided that it would be better
for me to become the leader.

194
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:50,970
This is why I thought it would be better
for me to take this role.

195
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:54,410
I think it's hard to find the midpoint...

196
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:55,710
- for the three of us.
- Right.

197
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,550
You are someone who seeks peace.

198
00:07:57,550 --> 00:07:58,780
You are a hardliner.

199
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:01,050
I'm sure the others know this as well.

200
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:02,620
I'm the one who mediates.

201
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:04,420
I believe that...

202
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,690
I'm the most neutral...

203
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:10,090
- out of the three of us.
- I thought that...

204
00:08:10,090 --> 00:08:12,890
you were the one with a driving force...

205
00:08:12,890 --> 00:08:14,260
and sought war.

206
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,730
And she was the one who sought peace.

207
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,500
I thought that
I was the one in the middle.

208
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:20,430
As the one in the middle,

209
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,940
I believed that my role...

210
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:25,140
was to fight for our team.

211
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:28,080
I think that both of you...

212
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:29,740
are total hardliners.

213
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:32,010
None of you are in the middle.

214
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:34,650
The leader's main role
is to conduct negotiations.

215
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,580
During those negotiations,

216
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,890
I was the one who represented our team.

217
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:41,920
Isn't that the leader?

218
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:44,160
Is the one in the back the leader?

219
00:08:44,430 --> 00:08:46,130
I didn't step up because I was incapable.

220
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:47,360
I was capable,

221
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,960
but I trusted our leader to do a good job.

222
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:53,100
Our leader is smart and competent. So...

223
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:56,600
Right. I thought that the one capable...

224
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,770
should be the leader.

225
00:08:57,770 --> 00:09:00,440
There's a benefit to being young.

226
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:04,310
I sensed that the other leaders
understood me better...

227
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,880
since I was young.

228
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:08,480
I'm never trying to force everyone
to make me the leader until the end.

229
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:10,350
- And...
- As we go through each day,

230
00:09:10,350 --> 00:09:12,950
this discussion will continue to pile up.

231
00:09:12,950 --> 00:09:16,320
I believe it's right to make a change now
if we are to make a change.

232
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,290
When considering our relationship
with the others,

233
00:09:18,290 --> 00:09:22,000
I believe it's right for someone
who is less strong to be the leader.

234
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,200
You're definitely not someone
who is less strong.

235
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:27,770
I don't think we'll reach an agreement
based on who is stronger.

236
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:29,470
Well...

237
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:32,140
It doesn't matter if we go through a vote.

238
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,840
Well, it's just the three of us.

239
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,710
That just means
it's based on Salt's decision.

240
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,850
After going through a vote,

241
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:42,750
I'm fine with reaching a decision
for the best of our team.

242
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:46,350
Salt said this to me.

243
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:49,590
She said that she's someone...

244
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:51,590
who struggles to talk about
uncomfortable topics.

245
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:55,500
She said that she felt impressed
and grateful...

246
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:59,600
when I stood up for her
during those situations.

247
00:09:59,670 --> 00:10:01,370
I started a campaign...

248
00:10:01,370 --> 00:10:03,870
to get one person's vote.

249
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:07,540
As of right now,
I have a greater trust in myself...

250
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,580
more than Genie.

251
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:12,850
This is based on the better of our team.

252
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:14,850
Salt and I both have the same opinion...

253
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:19,490
of being against having
a strong person as a leader.

254
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,890
