00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:45,150
- Why? To keep you alive, Donkey.
- Thanks.

514
00:20:45,150 --> 00:20:46,380
- Also...
- Second,

515
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:48,380
I came up with a fake code.

516
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,950
Please let me know if people...

517
00:20:49,950 --> 00:20:51,690
- start doubting or talking.
- Got it.

518
00:20:51,850 --> 00:20:53,490
I'll come up with a new one.

519
00:20:53,490 --> 00:20:54,650
Right, got it.

520
00:20:54,650 --> 00:20:56,090
- Sure.
- You get what I said, right?

521
00:20:56,090 --> 00:20:57,720
(Vector and Donkey share
the fake wall code.)

522
00:20:58,530 --> 00:20:59,860
It's taking him a while.

523
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:01,460
I'm stepping out as well.

524
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:03,060
Sure.

525
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:08,770
They're not even bothering to vote
for my reelection as leader now.

526
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,670
They couldn't even care.

527
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:15,510
(Team Red's Maillard, reelected as leader)

528
00:21:16,110 --> 00:21:17,810
Letting the others solve it themselves...

529
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,380
I think that'd be better.

530
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:25,690
- This could be bad...
- Right.

531
00:21:25,690 --> 00:21:27,690
or good. So...

532
00:21:28,090 --> 00:21:29,360
Congratulations, Vector.

533
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:30,920
- It was no joke.
- Izaha...

534
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:32,230
Did you need something?

535
00:21:32,230 --> 00:21:34,160
No, I just got curious.
You were taking a while.

536
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:36,260
- Team White was here earlier.
- I see.

537
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:37,700
Here's something I only wanted...

538
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,200
- to tell Team Red.
- Sure.

539
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:41,070
I want an alliance,

540
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:42,400
and with Team Red if possible.

541
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,470
- Really?
- Yes.

542
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:45,840
Why? Because you think
we have what it takes?

543
00:21:45,840 --> 00:21:47,440
To be honest, yes.

544
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,810
- We've been doing our best.
- Honestly,

545
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:51,510
you guys were the most help
with cracking the code.

546
00:21:51,910 --> 00:21:52,950
- Right.
- Nice.

547
00:21:52,950 --> 00:21:54,080
- That's why,
- Yes?

548
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,550
when the Platform comes online,

549
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:58,320
I might be able to store some resources.

550
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:01,190
If you need it, unlike the other teams,

551
00:22:01,190 --> 00:22:03,260
we can strike a deal at a fair price.

552
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:05,460
- But I want your word in exchange.
- Sure.

553
00:22:05,890 --> 00:22:07,360
Yesterday, Maillard...

554
00:22:08,030 --> 00:22:10,230
worked the crowd
and threw shade at me a little.

555
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:13,930
- I struggled with that.
- It hurt you a lot.

556
00:22:13,930 --> 00:22:15,740
(The previous morning)

557
00:22:16,170 --> 00:22:17,300
He won't give us the code.

558
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:19,040
Why aren't you giving us the code?

559
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:20,640
I can't because I don't have it.

560
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:21,940
- I really don't have it.
- Oh, please.

561
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:24,210
I heard that Team Black has the code.

562
00:22:24,210 --> 00:22:25,510
Yes, I heard that too.

563
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:27,580
No, it said I could know the code or not.

564
00:22:27,780 --> 00:22:30,080
- Your word keeps changing.
- The lies continue.

565
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:31,580
- There's a hint of that.
- I agree.

566
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,520
- But...
- How can I trust him?

567
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,120
I wasn't able to check.
I seriously don't have it.

568
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,460
Can't we challenge Team Black to a war?

569
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,560
Are you kidding me?

570
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:41,230
I'd appreciate your trust and assistance.

571
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:42,760
Up until now,

572
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,300
you were just a small shop owner.

573
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:45,600
But now, you own a huge market.

574
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:47,800
- I've come into a little power.
- Your influence has grown.

575
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:50,800
- It's like you own Coupang now.
- Yes, Coupang should do it.

576
00:22:50,970 --> 00:22:53,370
I worked hard to crack it
to stop Team White...

577
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:55,340
- from obtaining its skill.
- Theirs is too strong.

578
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:57,310
We don't know all the skills, but still.

579
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:59,850
Honestly, it'll be like
being robbed blind...

580
00:22:59,850 --> 00:23:01,350
- in broad daylight.
- That's right.

581
00:23:01,450 --> 00:23:02,780
- What if they issued 100 million of them?
- Exactly.

582
00:23:02,780 --> 00:23:03,780
Our diamonds would be worth...

583
00:23:03,780 --> 00:23:04,820
- less than a cent a piece.
- I know.

584
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:06,350
It'll become the key currency.

585
00:23:06,350 --> 00:23:07,690
They'll become the US.

586
00:23:07,690 --> 00:23:09,360
I had to stop at least that.

587
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:11,120
- It was in the public interest.
- That's true.

588
00:23:11,290 --> 00:23:12,490
I think Team Black's power...

589
00:23:12,490 --> 00:23:15,200
is needed to maintain balance here.

590
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:16,300
Right.

591
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:18,500
I have mixed feelings
regarding Team Black.

592
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:22,000
But I'm one of the people who trusts him.

593
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:24,500
I feel like he treats Team Red well...

594
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:28,210
and has been upfront
about wanting an alliance.

595
00:23:28,210 --> 00:23:29,640
Even though he's a bit suspicious,

596
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:32,550
I think he's someone
we can somewhat trust.

597
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:35,580
Vector and I have been signaling...

598
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:39,190
that we want an alliance
between our teams.

599
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:42,560
He's been reasonable with our team so far,

600
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:44,490
like he's being considerate.

601
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:46,460
I think the Platform...

602
00:23:46,690 --> 00:23:49,060
will pose as a neutral ground for balance,

603
00:23:49,330 --> 00:23:52,200
but it won't actually allow
easy resource exchanges...

604
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:57,170
and will let specific teams gain
an unfair advantage.

605
00:23:57,670 --> 00:24:00,710
It is going to act
as the true invisible hand.

606
00:24:02,310 --> 00:24:03,840
We're at a disadvantage.

607
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:06,080
We talked to Vector.

608
00:24:06,410 --> 00:24:07,580
What's the correct answer?

609
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:08,850
He hasn't told us yet.

610
00:24:08,850 --> 00:24:09,850
- Really?
- That's right.

611
00:24:09,850 --> 00:24:13,020
He did say it might not be good for us.

612
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:14,020
As in the effect.

613
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:17,090
According to him,
Red is at a disadvantage with the skills.

614
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:19,560
Since he wants to keep things balanced,

615
00:24:19,560 --> 00:24:21,560
he wants to show us his good faith.

616
00:24:21,690 --> 00:24:22,900
Why would he want balance?

617
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:25,370
Apparently, his goal is...

618
00:24:25,370 --> 00:24:27,400
to make everyone live well together.

619
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:30,170
Judging by his words and actions,
I think he's telling the truth.

620
00:24:30,170 --> 00:24:32,070
- Does he need as many people alive?
- Right, so...

621
00:24:32,070 --> 00:24:35,710
He was especially hurt by what you said.

622
00:24:35,940 --> 00:24:37,880
- While everyone was around, you...
- What?

623
00:24:37,880 --> 00:24:39,110
He's the one who lied.

624
00:24:39,110 --> 00:24:40,880
So please don't upset him...

625
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:43,120
- Don't seek pity.
- when everyone's around.

626
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:46,120
Team Black gained a lot of power
by cracking every riddle.

627
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:48,090
If we cooperate,

628
00:24:48,090 --> 00:24:51,090
he'll do his best to help us
to our advantage.

629
00:24:51,090 --> 00:24:52,660
That's what Black said.

630
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:55,560
I think we should play nice with him
for a while...

631
00:24:55,930 --> 00:24:57,330
and utilize that.

632
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:59,600
I couldn't stand it.

633
00:24:59,730 --> 00:25:02,570
Everything's going to go
the way Black wants now.

634
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,270
The situation is worse.

635
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:06,670
Hey, there's something there.

636
00:25:06,670 --> 00:25:08,740
Those are the rules on
how the Platform operates.

637
00:25:09,310 --> 00:25:10,940
The Platform operation rules.

638
00:25:10,940 --> 00:25:13,250
"When all the skills are developed..."

639
00:25:13,250 --> 00:25:16,050
"Team Black's skill will be activated,
which is the transition to the Platform."

640
00:25:16,650 --> 00:25:18,950
When all the skills are developed,

641
00:25:19,650 --> 00:25:22,690
Team Black's skill will be activated,
which is the transition to the Platform.

642
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:24,790
Once the Platform is activated,

643
00:25:24,790 --> 00:25:26,990
the existing Trading Station
will be closed.

644
00:25:27,290 --> 00:25:30,230
From now on, all transactions
will be handled through the Platform.

645
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:33,330
They're closing the Trading Station?

646
00:25:33,330 --> 00:25:35,100
We can't trade by ourselves anymore.

647
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,570
The teams can't trade now, right?

648
00:25:37,570 --> 00:25:39,770
The trade we used to do...

649
00:25:39,770 --> 00:25:43,110
with other teams
must now only be conducted...

650
00:25:43,110 --> 00:25:45,210
under Black's watch.

651
00:25:45,210 --> 00:25:46,710
- Before,
- We'll be at a disadvantage...

652
00:25:46,710 --> 00:25:48,380
he was only told the trading results.

653
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,680
Now he can interfere...

654
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:51,420
- with the trades directly?
- Yes, he can interfere.

655
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:53,220
"At the Platform, direct bartering..."

656
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:55,890
"like trading lives and credits
isn't possible anymore."

657
00:25:55,890 --> 00:25:57,160
(Bartering is prohibited.)

658
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,960
"Only diamonds are accepted as currency."

659
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:03,360
(Only diamonds are accepted as currency.)

660
00:26:03,460 --> 00:26:06,030
"Credits aren't accepted as currency
on the Platform."

661
00:26:06,730 --> 00:26:08,770
- In other words, we have a currency now.
- Right.

662
00:26:08,770 --> 00:26:10,470
Before, it was the primitive ages.

663
00:26:10,470 --> 00:26:12,070
Now, we've entered the age of currency.

664
00:26:12,170 --> 00:26:13,940
- Exactly. You're right.
- Right.

665
00:26:13,940 --> 00:26:17,810
From here on out,
you can't buy or sell without diamonds.

666
00:26:17,810 --> 00:26:18,980
That's right, which is good for us.

667
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:20,280
- We're at an advantage.
- Right.

668
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:21,350
On top of that,

669
00:26:21,350 --> 00:26:22,980
- credits are no longer needed to trade.
- That's right.

670
00:26:23,220 --> 00:26:25,750
If credits can't be used to trade,
then the credits...

671
00:26:26,490 --> 00:26:28,690
- Is it worth nothing now?
- We can't buy lives with it.

672
00:26:28,690 --> 00:26:30,320
We'll have to buy them with diamonds
at the Platform.

673
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:33,230
We can no longer buy lives with credits.

674
00:26:33,230 --> 00:26:34,390
We're worthless now.

675
00:26:35,030 --> 00:26:36,230
Absolutely worthless.

676
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:38,870
"You may operate the Platform..."

677
00:26:38,870 --> 00:26:40,800
"even without receiving lives
from other teams."

678
00:26:41,030 --> 00:26:42,240
Are lives no longer used at all?

679
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:44,270
It's a transition,
rather than an addition.

680
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:45,940
That's what I got so far.

681
00:26:46,070 --> 00:26:47,170
Are you kidding me?

682
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:49,710
- Let's go.
- What do we do with our credits now?

683
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,010
But why...

684
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:54,410
What do you gain
by monopolizing the Platform?

685
00:26:54,650 --> 00:26:57,020
Whoever operates it
might receive a commission.

686
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:58,950
We could pay 50 diamonds,

687
00:26:58,950 --> 00:27:00,590
only to get 45 of something back...

688
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:01,920
because of a commission.

689
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:04,920
Black's revenue stream shifted
from only direct sales...

690
00:27:05,260 --> 00:27:07,760
to earning business commissions too.

691
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:09,960
- Black's gaining power.
- There will be a commission.

692
00:27:10,130 --> 00:27:11,860
Now that the Platform is open,

693
00:27:11,860 --> 00:27:14,270
Black could make an earning
through commissions.

694
00:27:14,670 --> 00:27:16,740
- He's in "show me the money" mode.
- He has power.

695
00:27:16,740 --> 00:27:17,770
He has all the power.

696
00:27:17,770 --> 00:27:20,110
- Tell me about it.
- He'll have a different attitude today.

697
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:23,080
He's been acting like that
since yesterday.

698
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:25,110
The Platform that has all three skills...

699
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:26,810
is operational?

700
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:28,650
He's going to rake in money.

701
00:27:38,290 --> 00:27:41,890
Shortly, today's productive activity
will begin.

702
00:27:42,560 --> 00:27:44,100
The keyword
for today's productive activity...

703
00:27:44,100 --> 00:27:46,230
is Fermi estimation.

704
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:47,770
What's Fermi estimation again?

705
00:27:47,770 --> 00:27:49,470
- We learned it in season 1.
- It came up in season 1.

706
00:27:49,470 --> 00:27:50,570
Why don't I remember it?

707
00:27:50,570 --> 00:27:52,270
I didn't take part in that round.

708
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,810
Darn, this is a tough one.

709
00:27:55,410 --> 00:27:57,010
- This isn't my expertise.
- I'm clueless.

710
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:58,410
I don't know anything about it.

711
00:27:58,650 --> 00:27:59,780
Shall we get going?

712
00:28:00,750 --> 00:28:03,080
Team Blue won't be able to produce
a lot of lives today.

713
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:04,280
This is bad.

714
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:07,290
They could be better at this
than we think. I believe in them.

715
00:28:07,290 --> 00:28:09,120
If a war breaks out today,

716
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:10,290
- Exactly.
- we'll be in trouble too.

717
00:28:10,290 --> 00:28:12,630
We need to go back
to living harmoniously together.

718
00:28:12,630 --> 00:28:13,860
We need to shift our stance.

719
00:28:14,790 --> 00:28:16,360
- Here we go.
- Bring the fire.

720
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:17,730
(All three teams arrive
at the production site.)

721
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:20,770
Team Blue will be made aware...

722
00:28:21,170 --> 00:28:24,100
of the life reserves
before the productive activity begins.

723
00:28:24,940 --> 00:28:28,170
There are 24 lives currently...

724
00:28:28,170 --> 00:28:30,180
- What?
- in reserve.

725
00:28:30,180 --> 00:28:32,780
- Wait. Hold on.
- What did we just hear?

726
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:34,250
That doesn't make any sense.

727
00:28:34,250 --> 00:28:35,350
There were 43,

728
00:28:35,350 --> 00:28:37,280
and we dug up five yesterday.

729
00:28:37,420 --> 00:28:39,320
We estimated that each
of the other teams got two.

730
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:40,990
Yes, but even so...

731
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,860
- I mean...
- Wait, only 24?

732
00:28:42,860 --> 00:28:45,290
It should be 34. There's 10 missing.

733
00:28:45,860 --> 00:28:47,830
- Ten of them?
- Black must've taken them.

734
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,200
They must've gone to Black.

735
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,630
It was a huge slap in the face.

736
00:28:52,130 --> 00:28:54,470
Ten of the lives suddenly went missing.

737
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:58,370
We were short on lives as it was,

738
00:28:59,010 --> 00:29:00,940
and I was suddenly lost for words.

739
00:29:01,110 --> 00:29:02,540
It's just crazy.

740
00:29:02,540 --> 00:29:03,710
(Salt, Writer)

741
00:29:03,710 --> 00:29:05,310
Where did they go?

742
00:29:05,780 --> 00:29:07,480
It had to be Black.

743
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:10,450
This morning, it was announced
that he cracked...

744
00:29:10,450 --> 00:29:11,720
the riddles for the skills.

745
00:29:11,720 --> 00:29:13,490
The Platform suddenly became operational,

746
00:29:13,490 --> 00:29:16,890
and now ten lives are missing
from the reserves.

747
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:21,390
What was the skill that was developed?

748
00:29:21,690 --> 00:29:25,670
What was it that triggered all of this?

749
00:29:26,170 --> 00:29:28,870
- He cracked Team Blue's riddle too.
- Exactly.

750
00:29:28,970 --> 00:29:30,970
Is that what caused the drop in lives?

751
00:29:31,700 --> 00:29:33,670
- Is this what took effect?
- Lives weren't added.

752
00:29:33,670 --> 00:29:34,670
They decreased.

753
00:29:34,670 --> 00:29:36,240
No way.

754
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:38,410
We might have to buy lives from Black now.

755
00:29:38,410 --> 00:29:40,050
- Rather than...
- You're right.

756
00:29:40,050 --> 00:29:42,050
That makes the most sense.

757
00:29:42,580 --> 00:29:45,050
Whoever it is,
someone gaining more power...

758
00:29:45,050 --> 00:29:47,820
means the collapse
of the market system in some way.

759
00:29:47,820 --> 00:29:50,520
I felt like he came in
to some massive power.

760
00:29:50,990 --> 00:29:53,230
The situation keeps changing.

761
00:29:53,730 --> 00:29:55,330
So rather than sticking
to a specific strategy,

762
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:58,330
we don't know
how quickly things might change,

763
00:29:58,330 --> 00:30:00,200
so for now, we should focus
on collecting lives.

764
00:30:00,670 --> 00:30:02,170
We'll go with the lives.

765
00:30:02,170 --> 00:30:03,740
We'll produce lives.

766
00:30:04,770 --> 00:30:06,070
Lives.

767
00:30:07,440 --> 00:30:08,910
We'll go with credits.

768
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:13,410
Today's production keyword
is "Fermi estimation."

769
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,480
Fermi estimation.

770
