1512
00:56:59,450 --> 00:57:01,050
That's not a bad thing for us right now.

1513
00:57:01,050 --> 00:57:02,820
I'm going to request it right now!

1514
00:57:04,590 --> 00:57:07,160
- He looks excited.
- I think it's zero dollars.

1515
00:57:07,460 --> 00:57:09,460
- That's what it said on the screen.
- Right.

1516
00:57:10,860 --> 00:57:12,560
So it was made for us to start a war.

1517
00:57:12,560 --> 00:57:13,900
We developed the skills...

1518
00:57:13,900 --> 00:57:16,870
Does a war start
once skills are developed?

1519
00:57:19,070 --> 00:57:22,340
My real goal
is the weapon dealer's profits.

1520
00:57:22,510 --> 00:57:25,440
Getting fees through the Platform...

1521
00:57:25,710 --> 00:57:27,480
is completely meaningless to me.

1522
00:57:27,910 --> 00:57:29,580
So I gave it a lot of thought.

1523
00:57:30,250 --> 00:57:32,380
Team Blue is worried...

1524
00:57:32,380 --> 00:57:34,450
because they're everyone's target.

1525
00:57:34,550 --> 00:57:37,860
If Team White starts the war first,

1526
00:57:37,990 --> 00:57:41,530
they'll issue currency
before they start a war.

1527
00:57:41,530 --> 00:57:43,860
If so, the war cost I carefully set...

1528
00:57:43,860 --> 00:57:46,030
will be lowered.

1529
00:57:46,130 --> 00:57:48,030
That's why I designed things...

1530
00:57:48,030 --> 00:57:51,270
so Team Blue would start the war first,
if there was going to be a war regardless.

1531
00:57:51,400 --> 00:57:53,070
"Many effects were activated,"

1532
00:57:53,070 --> 00:57:55,870
"and one of those effects
is that war costs become 0 dollars."

1533
00:57:55,870 --> 00:57:58,740
"I worked very hard to solve a question
to make that happen."

1534
00:57:58,740 --> 00:58:01,480
I made it sound as if it was good
for everyone.

1535
00:58:01,880 --> 00:58:04,050
It was to instigate a war.

1536
00:58:04,750 --> 00:58:08,120
We might have to start the war first
before people find out about this.

1537
00:58:08,120 --> 00:58:09,590
If the currency value goes up,

1538
00:58:09,590 --> 00:58:12,260
we'll be at a disadvantage when fighting.

1539
00:58:12,260 --> 00:58:14,860
We need to attack first
before they find out the cost is zero.

1540
00:58:14,860 --> 00:58:17,060
If not, they'll definitely figure it out.

1541
00:58:17,060 --> 00:58:18,260
Should I not tell them, then?

1542
00:58:18,560 --> 00:58:21,400
It would be nice if you didn't for now.

1543
00:58:21,400 --> 00:58:23,000
I do want to be fair.

1544
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:26,400
If so, please make it seem
like I just didn't get the chance to.

1545
00:58:26,400 --> 00:58:28,140
- Of course.
- And that is actually the case.

1546
00:58:28,140 --> 00:58:29,610
- Right.
- Because I...

1547
00:58:29,610 --> 00:58:30,740
- We'll say so.
- Because I also...

1548
00:58:30,740 --> 00:58:32,580
need to maintain
my relationship with Team White.

1549
00:58:32,580 --> 00:58:34,380
Because the money...

1550
00:58:34,380 --> 00:58:37,050
I take home is up to Team White.

1551
00:58:37,180 --> 00:58:38,580
Let's hurry and go up.

1552
00:58:38,580 --> 00:58:39,850
It's better than staying here...

1553
00:58:39,850 --> 00:58:41,120
- and running into Team White.
- With Team White...

1554
00:58:46,290 --> 00:58:47,490
Were you talking?

1555
00:58:48,360 --> 00:58:49,990
From today, war is free.

1556
00:58:50,160 --> 00:58:51,230
Really?

1557
00:58:52,000 --> 00:58:53,100
It's here.

1558
00:58:53,230 --> 00:58:55,270
- How?
- Black said so.

1559
00:58:55,270 --> 00:58:57,440
Wasn't there a war cost?

1560
00:58:57,840 --> 00:58:59,940
- It's free now.
- It's just free now?

1561
00:58:59,940 --> 00:59:01,540
- Is it today?
- Is it today?

1562
00:59:02,340 --> 00:59:04,140
It's a free war event today.

1563
00:59:04,710 --> 00:59:07,480
What I thought after seeing
that the war cost was zero was,

1564
00:59:07,650 --> 00:59:10,150
"Did Vector set this cost?"

1565
00:59:10,450 --> 00:59:11,750
"If so, he did such a smart thing."

1566
00:59:11,980 --> 00:59:13,950
"There will definitely be a war today."

1567
00:59:14,420 --> 00:59:16,090
I was cheering inside.

1568
00:59:16,590 --> 00:59:18,020
So we have to do it today.

1569
00:59:18,020 --> 00:59:20,290
- We have to do it today.
- Yes. It's today.

1570
00:59:20,960 --> 00:59:23,490
Those two won't band together
and attack us, right?

1571
00:59:23,660 --> 00:59:24,700
To gain what?

1572
00:59:25,230 --> 00:59:26,300
There's no real gain.

1573
00:59:26,600 --> 00:59:28,970
Hold on. What should happen
with this war, then?

1574
00:59:28,970 --> 00:59:30,370
Who has to start it with who?

1575
00:59:31,270 --> 00:59:34,470
Team White will have no choice
but to attack Team Blue.

1576
00:59:34,710 --> 00:59:36,370
- If they don't want to die.
- If they don't want to die.

1577
00:59:37,040 --> 00:59:40,480
But I don't think Team Blue
can fight against Team White and win.

1578
00:59:40,480 --> 00:59:42,310
- There's no way Team Blue can win.
- No way.

1579
00:59:42,510 --> 00:59:43,650
They'll come to us, right?

1580
00:59:43,780 --> 00:59:45,480
So in this situation...

1581
00:59:45,480 --> 00:59:47,920
if White attacks and Blue asks for help,

1582
00:59:47,920 --> 00:59:49,690
do we help them or not?

1583
00:59:49,690 --> 00:59:51,420
That's the key thing to think about.

1584
00:59:51,520 --> 00:59:52,790
We help them and say,

1585
00:59:52,860 --> 00:59:54,060
"Give us lives."

1586
00:59:55,330 --> 00:59:58,030
- Are we trading after lunch?
- Yes.

1587
00:59:58,130 --> 00:59:59,660
Then starting at lunch,

1588
00:59:59,660 --> 01:00:01,530
- they'll start talking trades.
- Right.

1589
01:00:01,530 --> 01:00:02,970
They'll probably bring up war too.

1590
01:00:03,030 --> 01:00:04,200
What I'm saying is...

1591
01:00:04,200 --> 01:00:06,140
I think war is inevitable.

1592
01:00:06,200 --> 01:00:08,540
As for our lives...

1593
01:00:08,540 --> 01:00:10,910
- Three?
- If the trade is for three lives,

1594
01:00:11,310 --> 01:00:12,480
- we won't need a sacrifice.
- Right.

1595
01:00:12,810 --> 01:00:14,610
If the trade is for two lives,

1596
01:00:14,610 --> 01:00:17,050
we'd have to sacrifice one person.

1597
01:00:17,650 --> 01:00:20,750
So our condition for Team Blue is,

1598
01:00:20,850 --> 01:00:22,120
we tell them,

1599
01:00:22,120 --> 01:00:23,890
- "We won't go to war with you."
- "We won't go to war with you."

1600
01:00:23,990 --> 01:00:27,020
- "We'll go to war with Red tomorrow."
- Right.

1601
01:00:27,090 --> 01:00:28,690
But by tomorrow,

1602
01:00:28,690 --> 01:00:30,730
- we'd only have 5 people.
- We'd be down to 5.

1603
01:00:30,730 --> 01:00:32,830
- If 2 from Blue join them, that's 6.
- Right.

1604
01:00:32,900 --> 01:00:34,400
All I have to say is this.

1605
01:00:34,400 --> 01:00:36,070
We'll take two lives and tell them,

1606
01:00:36,170 --> 01:00:37,770
"We won't attack you today."

1607
01:00:37,770 --> 01:00:39,540
"Help us attack Red. Let's team up."

1608
01:00:39,540 --> 01:00:40,570
- Today?
- Yes.

1609
01:00:40,840 --> 01:00:43,070
So if we get one and a half lives,

1610
01:00:43,070 --> 01:00:44,540
- we'd have six and a half lives.
- That's right.

1611
01:00:44,540 --> 01:00:45,940
We're attacking Team Red today, right?

1612
01:00:45,940 --> 01:00:48,250
- The plan is to attack Team Red today.
- Team Red... Right.

1613
01:00:48,250 --> 01:00:50,550
If Team Blue offers us just one life,

1614
01:00:50,550 --> 01:00:52,350
- "Then we're attacking you today."
- Right.

1615
01:00:52,880 --> 01:00:54,450
Don't say it like that.

1616
01:00:54,450 --> 01:00:56,720
Say they have no choice. They'll get it.

1617
01:00:57,320 --> 01:00:58,490
"Get ready."

1618
01:00:59,390 --> 01:01:01,160
We can't let our numbers drop to five,

1619
01:01:01,160 --> 01:01:03,130
unless we take one of them out first.

1620
01:01:03,130 --> 01:01:04,160
We can never let that happen.

1621
01:01:04,160 --> 01:01:05,760
- Right. We'd be at a disadvantage.
- A huge disadvantage.

1622
01:01:05,760 --> 01:01:07,930
- If we want to survive, we...
- Have to strike first.

1623
01:01:07,930 --> 01:01:09,600
We have to strike first.

1624
01:01:09,730 --> 01:01:12,540
We either attack you or them today.

1625
01:01:12,540 --> 01:01:13,870
- Right.
- Exactly. That's it.

1626
01:01:13,870 --> 01:01:16,070
- Those are our only options.
- That's what it comes down to.

1627
01:01:16,070 --> 01:01:17,340
We're between a rock and a hard place.

1628
01:01:17,340 --> 01:01:18,910
There's no way back.

1629
01:01:18,910 --> 01:01:20,680
- But here's what I'm unsure about.
- If we keep attacking,

1630
01:01:20,680 --> 01:01:22,810
what happens after that?

1631
01:01:22,810 --> 01:01:24,280
Do we have an exit strategy?

1632
01:01:24,280 --> 01:01:25,820
As for an exit strategy...

1633
01:01:25,820 --> 01:01:26,950
- We don't have one.
- We don't.

1634
01:01:26,950 --> 01:01:28,490
- But once...
- Once a war breaks out,

1635
01:01:28,490 --> 01:01:30,120
- it'll be war every day.
- Right.

1636
01:01:30,120 --> 01:01:32,020
But after that war,

1637
01:01:32,160 --> 01:01:35,090
- if Team White wants to win,
- Right.

1638
01:01:35,090 --> 01:01:36,960
- we have to strike first.
- Improving our chances...

1639
01:01:36,960 --> 01:01:39,930
- is the whole point.
- People on both sides will die anyway.

1640
01:01:39,930 --> 01:01:42,030
But if wars keep breaking out,

1641
01:01:42,030 --> 01:01:44,070
- I want to keep our numbers up.
- Right.

1642
01:01:44,070 --> 01:01:46,740
Let's completely reset for a second.

1643
01:01:46,740 --> 01:01:49,040
Could all the contestants collude,

1644
01:01:49,140 --> 01:01:51,480
so no one has to die?

1645
01:01:51,710 --> 01:01:52,910
Right now,

1646
01:01:53,340 --> 01:01:55,010
what we have,

1647
01:01:55,010 --> 01:01:56,880
what Team Red and Team Blue have,

1648
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:58,380
- pool it all.
- Pool everything?

1649
01:01:58,380 --> 01:02:00,720
Pool it and split it among everyone.

1650
01:02:00,720 --> 01:02:02,020
That would keep us alive for just today.

1651
01:02:02,020 --> 01:02:03,620
- Today.
- Then just for today.

1652
01:02:03,620 --> 01:02:05,290
- We can all survive today.
- Is that 13 lives in total?

1653
01:02:05,290 --> 01:02:06,990
- We have 17 lives right now.
- We have 17.

1654
01:02:06,990 --> 01:02:08,530
If we divide them evenly,

1655
01:02:08,530 --> 01:02:10,530
- everyone should survive today.
- Right.

1656
01:02:10,530 --> 01:02:12,530
Then out of those 17 lives,

1657
01:02:12,530 --> 01:02:14,370
how many does Team Blue have right now?

1658
01:02:15,300 --> 01:02:18,140
Can we assume Team Blue has about nine?

1659
01:02:18,140 --> 01:02:19,800
- If we work backward?
- That many?

1660
01:02:20,140 --> 01:02:23,210
- Yes. I first thought they had nine.
- They might.

1661
01:02:23,510 --> 01:02:27,410
(Team Blue actually holds 14 lives.)

1662
01:02:27,880 --> 01:02:30,450
How many they have doesn't matter.

1663
01:02:30,450 --> 01:02:32,320
- Either way, they have plenty.
- Actually... Anyway...

1664
01:02:32,320 --> 01:02:34,720
- The total is at least 13 right now.
- Right.

1665
01:02:34,720 --> 01:02:37,050
- Right? So we can all survive today.
- Yes, that's right.

1666
01:02:37,050 --> 01:02:38,420
So if we reset everything...

1667
01:02:38,420 --> 01:02:41,760
and somehow divide the resources
among ourselves,

1668
01:02:41,760 --> 01:02:43,130
we can actually all survive.

1669
01:02:43,130 --> 01:02:45,500
- Then we don't have to start a war.
- Right.

1670
01:02:45,500 --> 01:02:47,130
- That's right.
- Right. Basically.

1671
01:02:47,600 --> 01:02:50,670
- Right.
- It's best to agree to keep this going.

1672
01:02:51,400 --> 01:02:52,540
We'll just have to go hungry.

1673
01:02:52,540 --> 01:02:54,510
(If all lives are shared,
everyone can survive.)

1674
01:02:55,040 --> 01:02:57,240
Let's go. I think we should meet Team Red.

1675
01:02:58,340 --> 01:02:59,510
Should I just knock?

1676
01:02:59,510 --> 01:03:00,540
- Yes.
- Yes.

1677
01:03:02,410 --> 01:03:03,980
(Team Blue requests a meeting
with Team Red.)

1678
01:03:04,950 --> 01:03:06,080
Yes?

1679
01:03:06,950 --> 01:03:08,020
Who is it?

1680
01:03:08,720 --> 01:03:10,120
- Coming.
- Is that Team Blue?

1681
01:03:11,060 --> 01:03:12,090
An alliance offer?

1682
01:03:12,290 --> 01:03:13,690
It's all about...

1683
01:03:14,090 --> 01:03:15,560
school, hometown, and family ties.

1684
01:03:16,360 --> 01:03:18,330
(Their proximity makes it easier
for the two teams to meet.)

1685
01:03:18,330 --> 01:03:19,760
- We...
- We'd like to talk.

1686
01:03:19,760 --> 01:03:20,800
- Should we talk?
- Should we go in?

1687
01:03:20,800 --> 01:03:22,230
- Team Blue?
- Yes!

1688
01:03:22,370 --> 01:03:24,030
Let's keep this quick and brief.

1689
01:03:24,030 --> 01:03:26,400
- White doesn't know the war cost is zero.
- They don't.

1690
01:03:26,400 --> 01:03:28,540
- But they'll know when trading starts.
- They'll know.

1691
01:03:28,540 --> 01:03:31,110
We need to reach
the Community Center first.

1692
01:03:31,210 --> 01:03:33,510
Otherwise, if Team White attacks,

1693
01:03:33,510 --> 01:03:35,550
- they'll issue a bunch, and it's over.
- Right.

1694
01:03:35,550 --> 01:03:38,120
- More issuance drives up the weapon cost.
- They'll drive it up.

1695
01:03:38,150 --> 01:03:40,450
If we're going to attack,
we should do it as soon as possible.

1696
01:03:40,550 --> 01:03:42,920
- First, we need to decide who attacks.
- So war is happening.

1697
01:03:42,920 --> 01:03:44,590
We also need to decide who attacks first.

1698
01:03:44,590 --> 01:03:46,190
We may be allies, but still.

1699
01:03:46,220 --> 01:03:48,360
What do you want to do?
Either way is fine with us.

1700
01:03:48,790 --> 01:03:50,930
But you hold plenty of lives.

1701
01:03:50,930 --> 01:03:52,700
- If you lose, you'll lose a lot.
- We have a lot to lose.

1702
01:03:52,760 --> 01:03:53,830
You'd lose a lot.

1703
01:03:53,900 --> 01:03:55,000
Should we attack?

1704
01:03:55,230 --> 01:03:56,570
Then we'll be allies.

1705
01:03:56,630 --> 01:03:59,070
If we lose today,

1706
01:03:59,240 --> 01:04:00,810
one person from our team has to leave.

1707
01:04:00,910 --> 01:04:02,440
- A life...
- A life for that person...

1708
01:04:02,440 --> 01:04:04,440
- We'll guarantee it, of course.
- We'll cover it.

1709
01:04:05,140 --> 01:04:06,380
- Got it.
- First...

1710
01:04:06,380 --> 01:04:09,110
- Let's make sure we meet at lunch.
- We'll meet and talk then.

1711
01:04:09,110 --> 01:04:10,950
- And bring some diamonds with you.
- Okay.

1712
01:04:10,950 --> 01:04:12,550
Let's go over there and talk first.

1713
01:04:12,620 --> 01:04:14,450
- Because we need to buy a weapon?
- Right. We need to buy one.

1714
01:04:14,450 --> 01:04:15,590
But...

1715
01:04:16,950 --> 01:04:18,420
But what do we gain...

1716
01:04:18,490 --> 01:04:20,790
by attacking Team White?

1717
01:04:21,460 --> 01:04:22,790
I'm not sure.

1718
01:04:22,990 --> 01:04:27,260
Right. Who knows? Maybe 50 or 60 diamonds?

1719
01:04:28,430 --> 01:04:30,940
But say Team Blue starts a war and loses.

1720
01:04:30,940 --> 01:04:32,570
Then we wouldn't get anything, right?

1721
01:04:32,570 --> 01:04:34,770
- All the lives go to Team White.
- Of course.

1722
01:04:34,870 --> 01:04:38,110
That would be the worst of the worst.

1723
01:04:38,110 --> 01:04:41,010
Why would Team Blue
form an alliance with us first...

1724
01:04:41,010 --> 01:04:43,180
or try to strike first themselves?

1725
01:04:43,350 --> 01:04:45,550
If Team White learns the war cost is zero,

1726
01:04:45,550 --> 01:04:47,790
do they think Team White will go to war?

1727
01:04:47,950 --> 01:04:50,960
Where did you hear about the war cost?

1728
01:04:51,660 --> 01:04:52,890
Black came over and told us,

1729
01:04:52,890 --> 01:04:54,120
but it could be a lie.

1730
01:04:54,120 --> 01:04:55,390
We can't trust anything.

1731
01:04:55,390 --> 01:04:57,160
We're the underdogs right now.

1732
01:04:57,160 --> 01:04:59,330
(Vector)

1733
01:05:00,100 --> 01:05:01,470
The war cost is...

1734
01:05:01,470 --> 01:05:02,900
zero diamonds.

1735
01:05:03,770 --> 01:05:06,270
The war cost has been set.

1736
01:05:06,640 --> 01:05:09,170
Please set the weapon cost.

1737
01:05:10,340 --> 01:05:11,610
The weapon cost is...

1738
01:05:12,680 --> 01:05:14,710
(Lunchtime)

1739
01:05:17,650 --> 01:05:20,480
Since the Platform was introduced today,

1740
01:05:20,480 --> 01:05:23,120
please purchase food through the Platform.

1741
01:05:23,150 --> 01:05:25,490
- Please enjoy your meals at your leisure.
- It's in the same place.

1742
01:05:25,490 --> 01:05:26,990
- Purchases go through the Platform too.
- So we buy through the Platform too.

1743
01:05:26,990 --> 01:05:29,330
- The store is on the Platform too.
- Right. So it's all the same.

1744
01:05:29,530 --> 01:05:31,560
- What should we do with these diamonds?
- Trading for Day Four will now begin.

1745
01:05:32,230 --> 01:05:34,400
- These won't fit in your bag, right?
- This concludes the announcement.

1746
01:05:34,530 --> 01:05:36,970
- Do we have a pouch?
- Just put them loose in a pouch.

1747
01:05:36,970 --> 01:05:38,840
Put them loose in a pouch.

1748
01:05:38,900 --> 01:05:40,500
Should we go get something to eat?

1749
01:05:40,500 --> 01:05:41,670
Let's go buy lunch first.

1750
01:05:43,040 --> 01:05:45,310
- This isn't a very appealing situation.
- Right.

1751
01:05:46,210 --> 01:05:48,850
There's no huge incentive for us.

1752
01:05:49,180 --> 01:05:53,320
- I never meant to start a war like this.
- Right.

1753
01:05:53,320 --> 01:05:55,720
- I'd only fight for a clear payoff.
- Exactly.

1754
01:05:55,820 --> 01:05:57,890
- Either wage a war of conquest.
- Right.

1755
01:05:57,890 --> 01:06:00,890
- Or fight for a greater cause.
- Right.

1756
01:06:00,890 --> 01:06:02,530
I'd be fine with that kind of war.

1757
01:06:02,530 --> 01:06:05,630
- This would only leave us with a burden.
- Right.

1758
01:06:05,930 --> 01:06:07,430
Why should we do this?

1759
01:06:08,070 --> 01:06:10,600
Team Blue can't produce enough anyway,

1760
01:06:10,800 --> 01:06:12,970
so all those dependents are a huge burden.

1761
01:06:12,970 --> 01:06:14,870
Whether there are 3 of them or just 1,

1762
01:06:14,870 --> 01:06:16,110
they can't get the answers right.

1763
01:06:16,110 --> 01:06:17,340
Just kill them.

1764
01:06:18,310 --> 01:06:19,680
Hello.

1765
01:06:19,680 --> 01:06:21,050
Hello.

1766
01:06:21,110 --> 01:06:23,280
Congratulations on the opening.

1767
01:06:26,050 --> 01:06:27,220
- Well...
- No, the store...

1768
01:06:27,250 --> 01:06:28,750
- We'll...
- Yes.

1769
01:06:28,750 --> 01:06:29,920
We'll do it.

1770
01:06:29,920 --> 01:06:31,260
- Do what?
- We'll attack.

1771
01:06:31,320 --> 01:06:32,790
- I see.
- In return,

1772
01:06:32,790 --> 01:06:35,090
if our prize money gets cut in half,

1773
01:06:35,090 --> 01:06:36,630
could you split the money equally with us?

1774
01:06:36,630 --> 01:06:39,030
War is still all you can think about.

1775
01:06:39,300 --> 01:06:40,560
Right. If that's what you mean...

1776
01:06:40,560 --> 01:06:41,600
Look.

1777
01:06:42,430 --> 01:06:44,100
If we start a war,

1778
01:06:44,970 --> 01:06:46,570
everyone will blame us.

1779
01:06:47,070 --> 01:06:48,170
Yes.

1780
01:06:48,170 --> 01:06:50,140
To be honest,

1781
01:06:50,570 --> 01:06:52,940
if anyone becomes a target of war,

1782
01:06:53,240 --> 01:06:55,450
there's no benefit unless it's Team Blue.

1783
01:06:56,080 --> 01:06:57,250
That's the cold truth.

1784
01:06:57,550 --> 01:06:59,850
- I see.
- Everyone else has far too few lives.

1785
01:07:00,250 --> 01:07:01,750
It's absurdly low.

1786
01:07:01,750 --> 01:07:03,750
- The war would get us nothing.
- Right.

1787
01:07:05,660 --> 01:07:07,560
I don't know. Let's eat first.

1788
01:07:07,560 --> 01:07:08,860
Let's talk while we eat.

1789
01:07:14,830 --> 01:07:16,030
But...

1790
01:07:16,700 --> 01:07:18,500
Did she put them in something?

1791
01:07:18,840 --> 01:07:21,470
I think she took the whole container.

1792
01:07:24,710 --> 01:07:26,280
It's Team White.

1793
01:07:26,440 --> 01:07:27,850
We gain nothing from running into them.

1794
01:07:27,850 --> 01:07:29,310
We really shouldn't run into them.

1795
01:07:30,610 --> 01:07:33,120
(Luna finally comes out of the dormitory.)

1796
01:07:33,620 --> 01:07:35,950
- Wait here for just a second...
- Where are you going?

1797
01:07:35,990 --> 01:07:37,120
So you can see?

1798
01:07:38,190 --> 01:07:39,360
You probably won't see them.

1799
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:48,470
Hi.

1800
01:07:48,530 --> 01:07:49,630
Who is it?

1801
01:07:49,630 --> 01:07:50,900
- Luna.
- I see.

1802
01:07:52,000 --> 01:07:53,200
How is it going?

1803
01:07:53,670 --> 01:07:55,440
We're in serious trouble.

1804
01:07:56,010 --> 01:07:57,470
You got zero answers?

1805
01:07:58,210 --> 01:08:00,010
You got zero lives?

1806
01:08:00,010 --> 01:08:02,010
It's a complete disaster right now.

1807
01:08:02,080 --> 01:08:03,850
I keep wondering,

1808
01:08:03,850 --> 01:08:05,150
what are we supposed to do now?

1809
01:08:05,150 --> 01:08:06,550
War is our only option.

1810
01:08:11,420 --> 01:08:13,890
Sure enough, Team Blue...

1811
01:08:13,890 --> 01:08:15,060
couldn't mine any lives.

1812
01:08:15,060 --> 01:08:16,660
They mined zero.

1813
01:08:16,690 --> 01:08:19,160
Granted, these were verbal promises.

1814
01:08:19,160 --> 01:08:21,400
Team Blue hasn't kept its word to us.

1815
01:08:21,400 --> 01:08:24,030
It's happened far too many times.

1816
01:08:24,030 --> 01:08:27,000
Yesterday, we even gave them credits.

1817
01:08:27,070 --> 01:08:28,440
We even provided aid.

1818
01:08:28,440 --> 01:08:32,010
The day before, we had priority,

1819
01:08:32,010 --> 01:08:34,240
but we didn't get a single life.

1820
01:08:34,240 --> 01:08:35,410
After all that,

1821
01:08:35,410 --> 01:08:37,010
they still won't give us any lives.

1822
01:08:37,010 --> 01:08:40,950
Even if it wasn't a firm promise,

1823
01:08:41,090 --> 01:08:42,850
since we only have one life,

1824
01:08:42,850 --> 01:08:45,260
we truly can't give it to Team White.

1825
01:08:45,260 --> 01:08:46,660
Then,

1826
01:08:46,660 --> 01:08:48,530
the moment we say,
"We can't give it to you. Too bad,"

1827
01:08:48,530 --> 01:08:52,030
it would practically be
a declaration of war.

1828
01:08:52,030 --> 01:08:54,400
I kept getting that uneasy feeling.

1829
01:08:54,430 --> 01:08:58,800
- Hello.
- Hello.

1830
01:08:58,900 --> 01:09:00,970
I've thought it through,

1831
01:09:01,070 --> 01:09:03,540
- and I want to introduce tiered pricing.
- Exactly. That's how it should be.

1832
01:09:03,540 --> 01:09:05,280
- Tiered pricing.
- Tiered pricing.

1833
01:09:05,280 --> 01:09:06,710
Wouldn't that be more reasonable?

1834
01:09:06,710 --> 01:09:07,710
We're using tiered pricing.

1835
01:09:07,710 --> 01:09:09,110
Could you give us the room for a moment?

1836
01:09:09,110 --> 01:09:11,380
- Sure.
- Sorry, but Team Blue...

1837
01:09:11,380 --> 01:09:12,450
We got here first.

1838
01:09:12,450 --> 01:09:14,420
- Then Team Blue can go first.
- Let Team Blue go first.

1839
01:09:14,420 --> 01:09:16,320
- Team Blue is going first.
- Please step away for a moment.

1840
01:09:16,320 --> 01:09:18,460
- Over there. Go on.
- Sure.

1841
01:09:19,090 --> 01:09:20,990
- We need the prices to decide...
- I should close the door.

1842
01:09:20,990 --> 01:09:22,130
what we're going to eat.

1843
01:09:22,490 --> 01:09:24,630
This one costs 1,
and the rest cost 2 each.

1844
01:09:25,260 --> 01:09:26,730
They cost three diamonds, right?

1845
01:09:27,830 --> 01:09:30,230
I wanted to ask you both something.

1846
01:09:32,100 --> 01:09:34,300
He says this costs three diamonds.

1847
01:09:34,400 --> 01:09:35,940
Do you want to put it on our tab
until after the war?

1848
01:09:37,440 --> 01:09:38,810
Why would I run a tab...

1849
01:09:39,110 --> 01:09:40,480
No. It's in case we need weapons later.

1850
01:09:41,110 --> 01:09:43,550
But we're paying together with Team Red.

1851
01:09:43,550 --> 01:09:46,050
Something feels off right now.

1852
01:09:47,580 --> 01:09:49,420
Seriously, I think we might get attacked.

1853
01:09:50,720 --> 01:09:52,020
I don't think Team Red wants a war.

1854
01:09:52,020 --> 01:09:53,060
Team Red?

1855
01:09:53,490 --> 01:09:55,790
I feel like if they don't attack us,

1856
01:09:55,790 --> 01:09:57,790
they may not want a war. I'm not sure.

1857
01:09:57,930 --> 01:09:59,030
Earlier, they said...

1858
01:09:59,130 --> 01:10:01,800
"A war not targeting Team Blue
"is pointless."

1859
01:10:02,200 --> 01:10:03,270
That's what they said.

1860
01:10:03,270 --> 01:10:04,570
- Team Red said that?
- Yes.

1861
01:10:04,570 --> 01:10:06,970
I don't know how it came to this.

1862
01:10:07,800 --> 01:10:10,940
"Why attack Team White
instead of Team Blue?"

1863
01:10:10,940 --> 01:10:12,480
That's what they said.

1864
01:10:12,480 --> 01:10:13,680
"There's nothing in it for us."

1865
01:10:13,680 --> 01:10:15,350
That's basically what they were saying.

1866
01:10:15,350 --> 01:10:17,080
So little by little,

1867
01:10:17,080 --> 01:10:18,850
it's starting to make me nervous.

1868
01:10:19,320 --> 01:10:21,490
Should we just pay now? It's only three.

1869
01:10:22,950 --> 01:10:24,150
- Then let's pay now.
- Three diamonds, please.

1870
01:10:25,520 --> 01:10:28,060
Honestly, I'm giving you a great deal.

1871
01:10:28,060 --> 01:10:30,560
- Then buy some now.
- That's not what I mean.

1872
01:10:30,560 --> 01:10:32,160
You said we might need to buy weapons.

1873
01:10:32,960 --> 01:10:35,600
Shouldn't we buy them after the war?

1874
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:37,630
We don't know what the weapons will cost.

1875
01:10:37,770 --> 01:10:40,500
If we end up being attacked,

1876
01:10:40,500 --> 01:10:42,840
are we going to buy bagels here
instead of weapons?

1877
01:10:45,840 --> 01:10:48,280
That's why weapons seem crucial now.

1878
01:10:48,380 --> 01:10:50,550
Then put it on our tab,

1879
01:10:50,550 --> 01:10:52,550
and you have to sell me one life today.

1880
01:10:57,320 --> 01:10:58,560
- Okay.
- Okay.

1881
01:10:58,560 --> 01:11:00,090
Okay. Then I'll put it on your tab.

1882
01:11:00,190 --> 01:11:01,490
- Got it.
- Yes.

1883
01:11:02,390 --> 01:11:04,700
- I'll do that.
- We should probably eat here.

1884
01:11:04,760 --> 01:11:06,900
But what's going on with them right now?

1885
01:11:06,900 --> 01:11:08,170
Even just to keep an eye on them,

1886
01:11:08,170 --> 01:11:10,370
- you're better off staying here.
- We should stay here.

1887
01:11:10,870 --> 01:11:12,370
Can everyone on your team survive?

1888
01:11:12,370 --> 01:11:13,470
- Us?
- Yes.

1889
01:11:14,200 --> 01:11:15,870
We're only covered through today.

1890
01:11:16,870 --> 01:11:18,410
- Just through today.
- Got it.

1891
01:11:19,510 --> 01:11:21,110
Today's going to be chaos for us.

1892
01:11:21,510 --> 01:11:24,510
For example, if Team Blue gives Black...

1893
01:11:24,510 --> 01:11:26,080
no lives at all,

1894
01:11:26,080 --> 01:11:27,880
there won't be any lives left to buy.

1895
01:11:27,880 --> 01:11:28,890
Then war breaks out.

1896
01:11:28,890 --> 01:11:30,990
Team Red! They're asking for Team Red.

1897
01:11:30,990 --> 01:11:33,390
And here's something even more shocking.

1898
01:11:34,220 --> 01:11:35,930
The total life supply has plummeted.

1899
01:11:36,730 --> 01:11:38,460
- The total life supply dropped?
- Yes.

1900
01:11:38,900 --> 01:11:39,930
Then the effect...

1901
01:11:39,930 --> 01:11:42,130
Black solved the question,
so the passive effect kicked in.

1902
01:11:42,300 --> 01:11:44,530
- I think that cut the total life supply.
- Yes.

1903
01:11:45,100 --> 01:11:47,200
So almost no lives are left to buy.

1904
01:11:49,140 --> 01:11:50,710
Should we get three mackerel?

1905
01:11:51,110 --> 01:11:53,910
Maybe two dumplings? Three? One more?

1906
01:11:53,910 --> 01:11:55,380
- What's this?
- Right now,

1907
01:11:55,380 --> 01:11:57,410
can we afford to eat this well?

1908
01:11:57,410 --> 01:11:58,920
- With what we have?
- No.

1909
01:11:59,120 --> 01:12:01,390
Won't the store close if war breaks out?

1910
01:12:01,390 --> 01:12:02,390
Right. You won't be able to trade.

1911
01:12:02,390 --> 01:12:04,320
That's why we want to stock up.

1912
01:12:04,320 --> 01:12:06,190
- Really? I want a corn dog.
- We're stocking up.

1913
01:12:06,190 --> 01:12:07,390
Eat. Go ahead.

1914
01:12:07,720 --> 01:12:09,790
- Then we'll each have a lunchbox.
- Right.

1915
01:12:10,060 --> 01:12:12,160
- That'll take care of lunch.
- Right.

1916
01:12:12,160 --> 01:12:15,070
- We'll get ramyeon for emergencies.
- And some instant rice and ramyeon.

1917
01:12:15,900 --> 01:12:17,500
Fifteen diamonds should do.

1918
01:12:18,600 --> 01:12:20,640
You'll take 6 small Yukgaejang cups
and 3 bowls of instant rice,

1919
01:12:20,640 --> 01:12:22,410
plus 1 corn dog and 3 orders of dumplings.

1920
01:12:22,410 --> 01:12:24,910
(Team Red's lunch: 15 diamonds,
worth about 7,500 dollars)

1921
01:12:24,910 --> 01:12:27,110
I heard from Maillard that...

1922
01:12:27,110 --> 01:12:28,450
the total life supply dropped.

1923
01:12:28,450 --> 01:12:30,880
The moment the Platform was activated,

1924
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:32,750
the total life supply dropped?

1925
01:12:34,050 --> 01:12:37,120
Let's discuss Team White's meal now.

1926
01:12:37,390 --> 01:12:38,420
Let's go.

1927
01:12:38,460 --> 01:12:39,920
We need to see how the Platform works.

1928
01:12:39,920 --> 01:12:41,290
Let's ask while we're buying food.

1929
01:12:46,600 --> 01:12:48,200
- The special costs 5 diamonds.
- Snacks cost 1 diamond.

1930
01:12:48,330 --> 01:12:49,800
- The special is five diamonds?
- Yes.

1931
01:12:49,800 --> 01:12:50,970
Four diamonds for a lunchbox.

1932
01:12:51,600 --> 01:12:52,870
- Four diamonds each.
- It's a little pricey.

1933
01:12:52,870 --> 01:12:55,870
Honestly, Team White pays a little more.

1934
01:12:55,870 --> 01:12:57,640
- I get it.
- I already knew that.

1935
01:12:57,640 --> 01:12:58,640
I know everything, you see.

1936
01:12:58,640 --> 01:13:00,610
I hope you don't hold it against me.

1937
01:13:00,610 --> 01:13:01,780
Of course. We understand.

1938
01:13:02,580 --> 01:13:04,180
This is capitalism at its finest.

1939
01:13:04,180 --> 01:13:05,480
- Let's pick our meals first.
- Let's eat. Food first.

1940
01:13:05,480 --> 01:13:07,520
- What should we get?
- I'll pay 18 diamonds for lunchboxes.

1941
01:13:07,520 --> 01:13:08,850
- Got it.
- Yes.

1942
01:13:09,050 --> 01:13:10,520
- I'm hungry.
- Me too.

1943
01:13:10,520 --> 01:13:12,090
- Seriously. I might pass out.
- My head hurts so bad.

1944
01:13:13,290 --> 01:13:15,860
Team White's special meals have arrived.

1945
01:13:16,460 --> 01:13:17,490
Food!

1946
01:13:17,490 --> 01:13:19,500
- We got lunchboxes too.
- We got lunchboxes too.

1947
01:13:19,500 --> 01:13:20,960
- Let's go!
- This is good.

1948
01:13:21,200 --> 01:13:22,530
That looks good.

1949
01:13:22,700 --> 01:13:24,600
- I'll clear this away.
- This is seriously good.

1950
01:13:24,870 --> 01:13:26,570
I'm seriously starving.

1951
01:13:26,570 --> 01:13:28,170
- Dig in.
- My hands are actually shaking.

1952
01:13:29,140 --> 01:13:30,210
I'm so hungry.

1953
01:13:32,340 --> 01:13:33,340
This is good.

1954
01:13:36,650 --> 01:13:38,250
When you eat after fasting,

1955
01:13:38,550 --> 01:13:39,880
- everything tastes really salty.
- Right.

1956
01:13:39,880 --> 01:13:41,350
- It does.
- We only fasted for a day.

1957
01:13:41,350 --> 01:13:43,920
- That's wild.
- Fasting makes every flavor intense.

1958
01:13:44,990 --> 01:13:46,360
- Lunchboxes are great.
- Yes.

1959
01:13:47,290 --> 01:13:48,330
Amazing.

1960
01:13:51,500 --> 01:13:52,930
I'm hungry.

1961
01:13:54,870 --> 01:13:58,400
Even if we get attacked,

1962
01:13:58,670 --> 01:14:00,540
stocking up isn't a bad idea.

1963
01:14:00,540 --> 01:14:01,740
I think it's a good call.

1964
01:14:01,740 --> 01:14:04,570
If we're doing this, let's spend it all.

1965
01:14:04,570 --> 01:14:06,010
Let's at least stock up on food.

1966
01:14:06,010 --> 01:14:07,610
- They have soft-boiled eggs too.
- Soft-boiled eggs.

1967
01:14:07,610 --> 01:14:09,180
- Soft-boiled eggs.
- The soft-boiled eggs are good.

1968
01:14:09,180 --> 01:14:10,910
Then pick one I'm Real drink each.

1969
01:14:10,910 --> 01:14:12,080
I'll get blueberry.

1970
01:14:13,250 --> 01:14:15,350
(Team Blue spends 11 diamonds
on extra food.)

1971
01:14:15,390 --> 01:14:17,520
Eleven diamonds.

1972
01:14:18,390 --> 01:14:20,690
The supermarket was closed the day before,

1973
01:14:20,690 --> 01:14:22,390
and everyone had gone hungry,

1974
01:14:22,390 --> 01:14:24,530
so I knew demand would be huge.

1975
01:14:24,760 --> 01:14:27,200
Sure enough, everyone came running,

1976
01:14:27,200 --> 01:14:29,030
eyes blazing like they were possessed.

1977
01:14:29,730 --> 01:14:31,540
They waved diamonds, begging for food.

1978
01:14:31,800 --> 01:14:34,910
And with war possibly breaking out,

1979
01:14:34,910 --> 01:14:37,910
I'd quietly spread the word...

1980
01:14:37,910 --> 01:14:39,010
that the war cost was zero.

1981
01:14:39,010 --> 01:14:41,280
That sent everyone into crisis mode,

1982
01:14:41,280 --> 01:14:44,550
stocking up on emergency food
and war rations.

1983
01:14:44,750 --> 01:14:46,050
I'll put it in there.

1984
01:14:46,280 --> 01:14:48,120
All of it? What about the eggs...

1985
01:14:48,120 --> 01:14:49,320
Everyone's stocking up.

1986
01:14:49,520 --> 01:14:50,550
No one knows what'll happen.

1987
01:14:50,790 --> 01:14:52,620
- Everyone sensed it.
- They all already did.

1988
01:14:52,620 --> 01:14:54,690
They all think war will break out today.

1989
01:14:54,690 --> 01:14:57,430
But I'm stocking up as much as I can,

1990
01:14:58,230 --> 01:14:59,730
and while I can still get war supplies,

1991
01:14:59,730 --> 01:15:01,260
I need to secure and stockpile them.

1992
01:15:01,260 --> 01:15:03,130
We don't know how long this could drag on.

1993
01:15:07,440 --> 01:15:10,070
I think a war's about to break out,

1994
01:15:10,070 --> 01:15:11,610
so is that why I can't get food down?

1995
01:15:11,810 --> 01:15:14,740
I think that's happening to me too.

1996
01:15:14,740 --> 01:15:16,080
- We have to force ourselves to eat now.
- I can't digest anything.

1997
01:15:16,080 --> 01:15:18,180
Don't complain when you've got food.

1998
01:15:20,080 --> 01:15:21,320
- But I can't get it down.
- Are you okay?

1999
01:15:21,320 --> 01:15:22,450
This is miserable.

2000
01:15:22,450 --> 01:15:24,090
- But you have to eat.
- I'll get sick if I force it down.

2001
01:15:24,220 --> 01:15:25,920
- You need to eat while you can.
- I really think I'll get sick.

2002
01:15:28,090 --> 01:15:29,330
Where did Maillard go?

2003
01:15:29,990 --> 01:15:31,530
- Where did Maillard go?
- Over there.

2004
01:15:32,600 --> 01:15:34,000
What's going on with the talks?

2005
01:15:34,100 --> 01:15:35,200
Did your needs change?

2006
01:15:35,630 --> 01:15:38,300
I don't think we know yet.
We need to run the numbers.

2007
01:15:38,300 --> 01:15:40,100
- We haven't made up our minds yet.
- Because...

2008
01:15:40,100 --> 01:15:42,610
But if they start a war over there,

2009
01:15:42,610 --> 01:15:44,640
they'll go over and change...

2010
01:15:44,640 --> 01:15:45,710
the value of the currency for sure.

2011
01:15:45,710 --> 01:15:47,680
- They'll realize what we're doing.
- Right.

2012
01:15:47,940 --> 01:15:49,880
If we don't strike first,

2013
01:15:49,880 --> 01:15:51,750
- we won't be able to buy weapons.
- Right.

2014
01:15:51,750 --> 01:15:53,180
- You get what I'm saying, right?
- Right.

2015
01:15:53,480 --> 01:15:55,690
So by the time trading begins here,

2016
01:15:55,690 --> 01:15:56,920
we have to decide.

2017
01:15:57,150 --> 01:15:59,460
- I know you're running the numbers.
- Right.

2018
01:15:59,460 --> 01:16:00,960
- But at least before trading begins...
- We need a decision fast either way.

2019
01:16:00,960 --> 01:16:02,660
- You need to tell us before trading.
- Quickly.

2020
01:16:02,660 --> 01:16:03,690
Okay.

2021
01:16:04,290 --> 01:16:06,060
They're pressing for a quick decision.

2022
01:16:06,360 --> 01:16:09,630
Team Blue thinks Team White
will print a fortune,

2023
01:16:09,630 --> 01:16:12,840
use it to gain a huge weapons advantage,

2024
01:16:13,500 --> 01:16:14,500
and then attack.

2025
01:16:14,500 --> 01:16:17,140
Why does Team Blue want a war?

2026
01:16:17,140 --> 01:16:18,140
What's their goal?

2027
01:16:18,140 --> 01:16:19,210
They want fewer mouths to feed.

2028
01:16:19,210 --> 01:16:20,640
Before the others get stronger.

2029
01:16:23,010 --> 01:16:24,450
Team Blue has a lot to lose.

2030
01:16:27,950 --> 01:16:29,490
Say we join in...

2031
01:16:30,850 --> 01:16:32,190
and get two lives.

2032
01:16:32,690 --> 01:16:35,490
Right. That's profit with no risk.

2033
01:16:35,690 --> 01:16:37,830
And the funny thing is, Team White...

2034
01:16:37,830 --> 01:16:39,530
might try to recruit us as allies.

2035
01:16:39,830 --> 01:16:42,500
- If Team Blue declares war on White...
- Right.

2036
01:16:42,900 --> 01:16:44,600
If we consider another option,

2037
01:16:44,600 --> 01:16:46,000
we side with Team White.

2038
01:16:46,000 --> 01:16:48,240
Would we get more out of that?

2039
01:16:50,070 --> 01:16:51,310
- That's funny.
- Yes.

2040
01:16:55,180 --> 01:16:57,480
They're seriously all checking each other,

2041
01:16:57,480 --> 01:16:59,380
each locked into position,

2042
01:17:00,550 --> 01:17:02,220
keeping tabs so no one can meet.

2043
01:17:02,720 --> 01:17:04,220
And everyone's so defensive.

2044
01:17:05,090 --> 01:17:06,120
It's the calm before the storm.

2045
01:17:08,590 --> 01:17:12,060
I saw Team Blue and Team Red
exchanging looks...

2046
01:17:12,630 --> 01:17:15,230
and waiting around.

2047
01:17:15,570 --> 01:17:18,470
I saw that. My first thought was...

2048
01:17:18,470 --> 01:17:22,070
keeping them from forming an alliance
in case a war breaks out.

2049
01:17:25,040 --> 01:17:27,410
We'll take this to our dormitory first.

2050
01:17:27,410 --> 01:17:28,980
But we should also...

2051
01:17:28,980 --> 01:17:31,110
- Finish eating and come upstairs.
- Okay.

2052
01:17:32,280 --> 01:17:33,950
What? They want us upstairs?

2053
01:17:35,020 --> 01:17:36,220
Do they want to talk?

2054
01:17:37,050 --> 01:17:38,320
Who are you siding with?

2055
01:17:38,960 --> 01:17:40,720
- Us?
- Yes. As allies.

2056
01:17:40,720 --> 01:17:42,160
Whoever gives us the better deal?

2057
01:17:43,260 --> 01:17:44,290
That's right. Exactly.

2058
01:17:44,290 --> 01:17:45,630
We'll have to think about it.

2059
01:17:46,630 --> 01:17:49,070
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

2060
01:17:49,630 --> 01:17:52,100
The trading for Day Four will begin.

2061
01:17:52,100 --> 01:17:54,770
- We haven't even finished eating...
- From now on, all trades...

2062
01:17:54,940 --> 01:17:57,770
must go through the Platform.

2063
01:17:58,440 --> 01:18:01,680
If trading does not go smoothly,

2064
01:18:01,680 --> 01:18:03,680
- you may declare war.
- We haven't even finished eating.

2065
01:18:03,680 --> 01:18:04,910
Now I can't even digest my food.

2066
01:18:05,750 --> 01:18:08,250
The leader of any team seeking war...

2067
01:18:08,250 --> 01:18:10,420
must visit the Community Center,

2068
01:18:10,420 --> 01:18:12,420
pay the war cost,

2069
01:18:12,420 --> 01:18:14,690
and declare war.

2070
01:18:14,920 --> 01:18:16,660
- This is insane.
- Once war is declared,

2071
01:18:16,930 --> 01:18:20,830
all trading through the Platform
will stop immediately,

2072
01:18:20,830 --> 01:18:23,930
and Community Town will be
in a state of war.

2073
01:18:23,930 --> 01:18:25,470
Did they just mention the war cost?

2074
01:18:26,140 --> 01:18:28,070
Today's war cost is...

2075
01:18:28,540 --> 01:18:31,310
- zero diamonds.
- Zero diamonds?

2076
01:18:33,010 --> 01:18:34,580
The war cost paid...

2077
01:18:34,580 --> 01:18:36,280
- will be deducted from the final prize.
- They want us to do it.

2078
01:18:36,280 --> 01:18:37,380
What does zero diamonds even mean?

2079
01:18:37,380 --> 01:18:38,380
- They're telling us to fight.
- They want us to fight.

2080
01:18:38,380 --> 01:18:40,050
They seriously want us to go to war?

2081
01:18:40,050 --> 01:18:41,720
You will receive half...

2082
01:18:41,720 --> 01:18:43,820
of the losing team's total resources.

2083
01:18:45,660 --> 01:18:47,090
- Zero?
- Absolutely nothing.

2084
01:18:47,660 --> 01:18:50,830
- They're telling us to go to war.
- They really want a war.

2085
01:18:50,830 --> 01:18:52,060
This concludes the announcement
from Community Center.

2086
01:18:52,060 --> 01:18:53,360
(Now they know too.)

2087
01:18:53,360 --> 01:18:54,500
Are we going to war?

2088
01:18:56,200 --> 01:18:59,340
Some shady force is...

2089
01:18:59,340 --> 01:19:01,570
pushing everyone to start a war.

2090
01:19:03,240 --> 01:19:04,310
What?

2091
01:19:05,180 --> 01:19:07,210
We were absolutely sure...

2092
01:19:07,210 --> 01:19:08,410
the choice to start a war was ours.

2093
01:19:08,410 --> 01:19:10,680
We thought there would be a war cost.

2094
01:19:10,680 --> 01:19:12,350
So before paying the war cost,

2095
01:19:12,350 --> 01:19:14,180
we planned to issue currency.

2096
01:19:14,180 --> 01:19:16,190
That's why we kept carrying it around.

2097
01:19:16,350 --> 01:19:18,690
But now the war cost is zero.

2098
01:19:18,690 --> 01:19:21,220
So our whole plan fell apart.

2099
01:19:21,490 --> 01:19:23,390
With the war cost at zero,

2100
01:19:23,390 --> 01:19:27,700
anyone can start one on a whim.

2101
01:19:27,700 --> 01:19:30,600
If they wage wars indiscriminately
since it doesn't cost money,

2102
01:19:30,600 --> 01:19:32,770
and purchase arms,

2103
01:19:32,770 --> 01:19:34,540
that would lead to an arms race.

2104
01:19:34,540 --> 01:19:37,170
And we all know
what comes after an arms race.

2105
01:19:37,170 --> 01:19:39,410
A war is going to happen anyway.

2106
01:19:39,410 --> 01:19:42,510
Everyone would perceive us as a threat...

2107
01:19:42,510 --> 01:19:45,450
and would try to thin our numbers,
I thought.

2108
01:19:45,450 --> 01:19:48,150
So we need to team up
with either Team Blue...

2109
01:19:48,150 --> 01:19:49,590
or Team Red...

2110
01:19:49,590 --> 01:19:51,050
to prepare ourselves for a war.

2111
01:19:53,090 --> 01:19:54,090
It's scary.

2112
01:19:57,090 --> 01:19:58,830
- Has the trade begun already?
- Yes.

2113
01:19:58,830 --> 01:19:59,900
- Yes, it's time for trade now.
- Have you talked about it?

2114
01:20:00,100 --> 01:20:01,230
Now let's talk about it.

2115
01:20:01,230 --> 01:20:03,370
For now, we're in debt...

2116
01:20:03,370 --> 01:20:05,000
to Team Black.

2117
01:20:05,000 --> 01:20:06,900
- So we...
- Yes.

2118
01:20:07,340 --> 01:20:08,910
We need to talk...

2119
01:20:09,240 --> 01:20:10,240
between ourselves.

2120
01:20:10,910 --> 01:20:12,110
Are you going to trade?

2121
01:20:12,110 --> 01:20:15,550
- Now we can't trade anyway.
- If you ring the bell for trading later,

2122
01:20:15,550 --> 01:20:17,050
you can't trade with us.

2123
01:20:17,050 --> 01:20:18,550
You need to go through them anyway.

2124
01:20:18,550 --> 01:20:20,350
- You should talk to us first.
- You need to do it with us, anyway.

2125
01:20:20,350 --> 01:20:22,520
- How about talking with us now?
- However, the trading...

2126
01:20:22,520 --> 01:20:24,050
only takes place here,

2127
01:20:24,050 --> 01:20:25,760
and we can talk between us.

2128
01:20:25,760 --> 01:20:27,390
But we're supposed to talk to them first.

2129
01:20:27,390 --> 01:20:28,930
Can we come back later after that?

2130
01:20:28,930 --> 01:20:29,930
You mean with Team Red?

2131
01:20:29,930 --> 01:20:32,100
- We'll come back here.
- We'll be back right away.

2132
01:20:32,300 --> 01:20:33,300
Then,

2133
01:20:33,960 --> 01:20:35,770
you shouldn't meet with Team Red first.

2134
01:20:36,730 --> 01:20:38,570
You should come to us first
after the meeting.

2135
01:20:38,570 --> 01:20:39,940
That's a win-win, you know.

2136
01:20:40,400 --> 01:20:41,840
We're not going to trade with Team Red.

2137
01:20:41,840 --> 01:20:43,340
We need to talk between ourselves.

2138
01:20:43,340 --> 01:20:44,740
I know you're going to talk
between yourselves,

2139
01:20:44,740 --> 01:20:46,580
- We'll never trade with them.
- but come to us first later.

2140
01:20:46,580 --> 01:20:49,450
We can't trade with them anyway.

2141
01:20:51,950 --> 01:20:54,480
Aren't we being too naive
letting them go, just like that?

2142
01:20:54,480 --> 01:20:56,320
- They left in such a hurry.
- Right.

2143
01:20:56,320 --> 01:20:57,890
They need to talk between themselves.

2144
01:20:57,890 --> 01:21:00,590
- No, they're going to Team Red.
- They were watching Team Red.

2145
01:21:00,590 --> 01:21:02,060
They left as we made a move.

2146
01:21:02,060 --> 01:21:03,630
They're going to talk to Team Red.

2147
01:21:04,960 --> 01:21:06,960
What was that attitude?

2148
01:21:06,960 --> 01:21:09,100
If we hand over enough lives to them,

2149
01:21:09,100 --> 01:21:10,900
they're not going to wage a war.
That's their attitude.

2150
01:21:10,900 --> 01:21:12,670
That's never going to happen.

2151
01:21:12,670 --> 01:21:14,000
They're going to talk to Team Red.

2152
01:21:14,000 --> 01:21:15,540
- Not between themselves.
- Let's follow them now.

2153
01:21:15,540 --> 01:21:17,810
- Is that so? I'm sorry.
- We need to get in on it too.

2154
01:21:19,680 --> 01:21:20,810
Excuse me...

2155
01:21:20,810 --> 01:21:23,680
- I'll pay for the meal.
- You can buy something, Luna.

2156
01:21:23,680 --> 01:21:25,320
- Can I? I will.
- Yes, go ahead.

2157
01:21:25,320 --> 01:21:26,850
I'll make a purchase
and join you right away.

2158
01:21:27,180 --> 01:21:30,820
The thing is, if Team Red
intends to wage a war against us...

2159
01:21:30,820 --> 01:21:31,820
That is not going to happen.

2160
01:21:32,290 --> 01:21:33,390
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

2161
01:21:33,390 --> 01:21:36,060
They don't intend to wage a war. As I see,

2162
01:21:36,060 --> 01:21:39,430
they have doubts about waging a war.

2163
01:21:39,730 --> 01:21:40,730
What?

2164
01:21:41,000 --> 01:21:42,000
What's that?

2165
01:21:42,200 --> 01:21:45,200
They asked if we're going to wage a war,

2166
01:21:45,200 --> 01:21:47,140
so I answered that we would.

2167
01:21:56,380 --> 01:21:58,180
This situation
doesn't look attractive to me.

2168
01:21:59,850 --> 01:22:01,180
If we can surely get something,

2169
01:22:02,850 --> 01:22:04,390
we can carry out a war of conquest.

2170
01:22:05,520 --> 01:22:07,820
If someone has to be
the target of our war,

2171
01:22:09,560 --> 01:22:11,760
it should be Team Blue.

2172
01:22:12,700 --> 01:22:14,430
He went in there.

2173
01:22:14,430 --> 01:22:16,870
What? Why?

2174
01:22:16,870 --> 01:22:18,170
There he is. He's waiting.

2175
01:22:18,170 --> 01:22:19,170
I know.

2176
01:22:22,870 --> 01:22:24,310
(The Trading Station is currently closed.)

2177
01:22:24,310 --> 01:22:25,710
(If you wish to declare war,)

2178
01:22:25,710 --> 01:22:27,110
(state that you will declare war.)

2179
01:22:27,340 --> 01:22:29,410
If he wished to wage a war,
he made a right choice of standing there.

2180
01:22:29,410 --> 01:22:31,920
I'm curious about with whom
he wants to have a war.

2181
01:22:31,920 --> 01:22:33,650
Us, in the first place.

2182
01:22:33,880 --> 01:22:35,720
If not, he has no reason to stand there.

2183
01:22:35,720 --> 01:22:36,820
That's what I'm saying.

2184
01:22:36,820 --> 01:22:38,490
I mean, if that's what he wants...

2185
01:22:38,490 --> 01:22:39,860
- Where are you going?
- The weapons left...

2186
01:22:39,860 --> 01:22:41,760
are only one for each item.

2187
01:22:41,760 --> 01:22:43,760
The first one who buys it can take it.

2188
01:22:43,760 --> 01:22:45,330
You can purchase an alliance too.

2189
01:22:46,460 --> 01:22:49,570
If one team purchases a weapon,

2190
01:22:49,570 --> 01:22:51,770
are other teams not allowed to buy one?

2191
01:22:51,970 --> 01:22:53,700
Weapons are classified into three classes.

2192
01:22:53,700 --> 01:22:56,210
For each class, we prepared one item.

2193
01:22:56,210 --> 01:22:59,040
And there's no limit on purchases
for each team.

2194
01:23:00,110 --> 01:23:03,980
Can teams participating as an alliance
purchase weapons?

2195
01:23:04,580 --> 01:23:08,020
Teams in an alliance can purchase weapons.

2196
01:23:08,550 --> 01:23:09,550
Thank you.

2197
01:23:09,550 --> 01:23:11,690
(Maillard came to check out
the rules regarding weapons.)

2198
01:23:12,320 --> 01:23:13,860
We should go.

2199
01:23:13,860 --> 01:23:15,460
But don't you need to trade?

2200
01:23:15,460 --> 01:23:16,660
You have no credit, don't you?

2201
01:23:17,260 --> 01:23:18,730
We can't make a trade...

2202
01:23:18,730 --> 01:23:20,460
- with just two, anyway.
- I see.

2203
01:23:20,460 --> 01:23:21,530
We need to collect a commission
through the platform.

2204
01:23:21,530 --> 01:23:22,830
We need to make a purchase
through the platform.

2205
01:23:23,630 --> 01:23:25,640
Then, would you like to leave
some credits with us?

2206
01:23:25,640 --> 01:23:27,440
I know. We should make a pre-trade first.

2207
01:23:27,440 --> 01:23:30,070
- We need to trade for about an hour.
- Then go ahead.

2208
01:23:30,070 --> 01:23:31,270
- Don't you think so?
- For now,

2209
01:23:31,270 --> 01:23:33,740
the other side definitely has caught on.

2210
01:23:33,740 --> 01:23:35,480
That's for sure.

2211
01:23:35,480 --> 01:23:37,250
If you want to purchase weapons first,
you need to go in.

2212
01:23:38,380 --> 01:23:40,280
All right.

2213
01:23:41,080 --> 01:23:43,090
- Share some lives with me.
- Okay.

2214
01:23:45,250 --> 01:23:46,460
Where are you off to in such a rush?

2215
01:23:46,690 --> 01:23:49,130
It was so heartless the way
they just walked away.

2216
01:23:50,090 --> 01:23:51,230
Why are they going in there?

2217
01:23:52,930 --> 01:23:54,630
So does he mean...

2218
01:23:54,630 --> 01:23:56,130
that Team Red bought weapons?

2219
01:23:56,500 --> 01:23:58,130
No, he wants us to buy them.

2220
01:23:58,130 --> 01:24:00,370
He says we can buy an alliance too.
That's why he tells us to do so.

2221
01:24:00,570 --> 01:24:02,470
He just checked out
how much the weapons are.

2222
01:24:03,110 --> 01:24:04,310
And he wants us to buy them?

2223
01:24:04,310 --> 01:24:06,040
- And they'd buy an alliance?
- We told them we'd do so,

2224
01:24:06,040 --> 01:24:07,410
and we handed over our lives.

2225
01:24:07,480 --> 01:24:08,980
For now, we'll have to handle

2226
01:24:08,980 --> 01:24:12,350
- the subsequent trading later.
- But can we trust Team Red?

2227
01:24:12,950 --> 01:24:15,120
Even if we can't,
there's no way to avoid them now.

2228
01:24:15,690 --> 01:24:17,050
If they declare war on us,

2229
01:24:17,050 --> 01:24:18,090
it's 6 to 3.

2230
01:24:18,090 --> 01:24:19,490
Otherwise, it's 6 to 6.

2231
01:24:20,190 --> 01:24:22,290
We have to be six, no matter what.

2232
01:24:22,290 --> 01:24:24,060
And she's following us now.

2233
01:24:24,760 --> 01:24:25,960
One from Team White came.

2234
01:24:25,960 --> 01:24:27,330
She noticed something.

2235
01:24:28,630 --> 01:24:30,370
Did you make a purchase?

2236
01:24:30,600 --> 01:24:32,140
- Purchase what?
- Did you buy food?

2237
01:24:32,400 --> 01:24:34,540
- They're buying.
- You need to hurry before a war begins.

2238
01:24:34,840 --> 01:24:36,470
Do you need
the kimchi flavored cup noodles?

2239
01:24:36,470 --> 01:24:37,810
- Or what do you want?
- I'll have the kimchi flavored ones.

2240
01:24:37,810 --> 01:24:38,910
- Kimchi flavored ones?
- Four kimchi flavored ones.

2241
01:24:39,410 --> 01:24:40,610
- Are these 50 in total?
- It's 50 in total. Right.

2242
01:24:40,610 --> 01:24:42,210
One, two, three, four.

2243
01:24:42,210 --> 01:24:43,210
- Take those.
- Okay.

2244
01:24:43,210 --> 01:24:44,810
One, two, three, four, five. Okay.

2245
01:24:44,810 --> 01:24:45,820
You have the paper, right?

2246
01:24:46,350 --> 01:24:48,020
We'll have to devalue the currency.

2247
01:24:48,720 --> 01:24:49,920
I think we need to devalue the currency.

2248
01:24:51,990 --> 01:24:53,490
So it's a preemptive strike.

2249
01:24:55,830 --> 01:24:57,330
Were they trying to declare war on us?

2250
01:25:00,730 --> 01:25:03,000
If you're anxious about that,
I'll stay here...

2251
01:25:03,430 --> 01:25:04,870
while you go talk to Team Red.

2252
01:25:05,500 --> 01:25:06,600
Anyway, the one who came in first...

2253
01:25:06,600 --> 01:25:09,210
Earlier, you said that Team Red
changed their mind.

2254
01:25:09,210 --> 01:25:10,210
Is that true?

2255
01:25:10,540 --> 01:25:12,810
They did change their mind,
but I talked to them again.

2256
01:25:12,810 --> 01:25:15,040
I told them we needed to declare war first
for the sake of currency value.

2257
01:25:15,480 --> 01:25:16,750
- I told them that.
- Did they agree on that?

2258
01:25:16,750 --> 01:25:18,780
We agreed to talk about that again.

2259
01:25:18,780 --> 01:25:20,050
Seeing that he was standing there,

2260
01:25:20,050 --> 01:25:22,190
I guessed they wanted to declare war...

2261
01:25:22,190 --> 01:25:23,620
and came in here first.

2262
01:25:23,620 --> 01:25:24,890
But if you still feel anxious about that,

2263
01:25:24,890 --> 01:25:26,190
- I'll be standing here.
- When Donkey was coming earlier,

2264
01:25:26,190 --> 01:25:28,960
he said, "All right.
Share some lives with me."

2265
01:25:30,160 --> 01:25:31,890
Yes, we'll join you.

2266
01:25:32,600 --> 01:25:34,560
- We'll join you.
- Okay.

2267
01:25:34,560 --> 01:25:35,870
All right.

2268
01:25:36,770 --> 01:25:38,170
Share some lives with me.

2269
01:25:38,170 --> 01:25:39,170
Okay.

2270
01:25:40,300 --> 01:25:42,840
But in case we lose,

2271
01:25:42,840 --> 01:25:45,780
are they going to share the risk together?
Can you check that out?

2272
01:25:45,780 --> 01:25:47,280
- I'll stay here.
- Okay.

2273
01:25:47,280 --> 01:25:48,280
You know what I mean?

2274
01:25:48,680 --> 01:25:51,380
So we... Wait. Let's recap this
so I can deliver it clearly.

2275
01:25:51,380 --> 01:25:53,250
We're going to declare war. That's a fact.

2276
01:25:53,250 --> 01:25:54,920
However, in case we lose,

2277
01:25:54,920 --> 01:25:57,920
are they willing to cover half
of what we forfeit regarding the diamonds?

2278
01:25:57,920 --> 01:25:58,920
- Exactly.
- Okay. I got it.

2279
01:25:58,920 --> 01:25:59,920
That's what you need to tell them.

2280
01:25:59,920 --> 01:26:01,620
We're going to pay for the weapons.

2281
01:26:01,620 --> 01:26:03,590
No. We need to charge them
for the weapons too,

2282
01:26:03,590 --> 01:26:05,060
- split exactly in half.
- That's right.

2283
01:26:05,060 --> 01:26:06,660
Split exactly in half. I got it.

2284
01:26:06,660 --> 01:26:07,960
For now, guard this spot.

2285
01:26:07,960 --> 01:26:09,770
You have to block Team White
from getting in first.

2286
01:26:09,770 --> 01:26:10,770
Okay.

2287
01:26:17,340 --> 01:26:20,080
If Team White enters first
and issues currency,

2288
01:26:20,080 --> 01:26:23,310
we cannot buy weapons, first of all.

2289
01:26:23,310 --> 01:26:25,650
For today, we need to stop them
from issuing the currency.

2290
01:26:25,650 --> 01:26:28,580
I'm not sure about
how much they went yesterday,

2291
01:26:28,580 --> 01:26:31,090
but I decided to block
the currency issuance today.

2292
01:26:31,090 --> 01:26:33,420
That's why I entered in the first place.

2293
01:26:36,430 --> 01:26:37,830
I wonder if...

2294
01:26:38,230 --> 01:26:39,760
- If...
- No, we didn't declare war.

2295
01:26:39,760 --> 01:26:41,230
- Did you declare war?
- No, we didn't.

2296
01:26:41,230 --> 01:26:42,470
Why did you do that?

2297
01:26:42,470 --> 01:26:43,470
We didn't declare war.

2298
01:26:43,470 --> 01:26:44,700
Then please have a talk with us.

2299
01:26:44,930 --> 01:26:46,270
How about alliances...

2300
01:26:46,600 --> 01:26:47,600
and sanctions?

2301
01:26:48,140 --> 01:26:49,940
- I want you to have a talk with us.
- Can't you talk with us now?

2302
01:26:49,940 --> 01:26:52,110
Exactly. Now it's time for trading.

2303
01:26:52,940 --> 01:26:54,940
- You mean regarding the trading?
- Yes.

2304
01:26:54,940 --> 01:26:58,350
For now, I need to check one thing out.

2305
01:26:58,350 --> 01:26:59,950
Then can one of you stay with us?

2306
01:27:00,320 --> 01:27:01,320
Will you stay here?

2307
01:27:01,320 --> 01:27:02,790
- Yes, I'll be waiting.
- Yes, please do so.

2308
01:27:03,350 --> 01:27:05,520
(Salt is left behind
to reassure Team White.)

2309
01:27:06,220 --> 01:27:08,320
Shouldn't we give some information
to Team Blue?

2310
01:27:09,490 --> 01:27:10,490
Well...

2311
01:27:10,660 --> 01:27:11,760
Regarding conditions for trading...

2312
01:27:11,760 --> 01:27:13,360
- They're out.
- You mean Team Blue?

2313
01:27:13,360 --> 01:27:14,360
They didn't declare war.

2314
01:27:17,630 --> 01:27:19,470
It's not as easy as it looks
when it comes down to it, I guess.

2315
01:27:21,470 --> 01:27:24,670
Wait, Genie is passing by.
I'll try to hold her back.

2316
01:27:27,540 --> 01:27:29,410
- How did it go?
- I need to check one thing out.

2317
01:27:29,780 --> 01:27:32,550
First of all,
we'll be the ones to declare war.

2318
01:27:33,020 --> 01:27:35,620
- Let's go.
- What's going on?

2319
01:27:35,620 --> 01:27:40,020
For now, one of us is taking over
the Community Center.

2320
01:27:40,020 --> 01:27:41,960
And lastly, before we declare war,

2321
01:27:41,960 --> 01:27:45,130
we need to check out
the details of this alliance.

2322
01:27:45,130 --> 01:27:48,900
We'll bear the risk of what we bet.

2323
01:27:48,900 --> 01:27:51,170
However, whether we win or lose,
we have the risks...

2324
01:27:51,170 --> 01:27:52,740
- of the cost of buying the weapons.
- Yes.

2325
01:27:52,740 --> 01:27:55,000
About that, we want you
to split the risks in half.

2326
01:27:55,000 --> 01:27:57,270
Instead, if we win,
we will split the spoils.

2327
01:27:57,270 --> 01:27:59,580
We're here
with that exact 50-50 concept in mind.

2328
01:27:59,580 --> 01:28:01,810
If you bear the risks,
we'll split those in half.

2329
01:28:01,810 --> 01:28:03,750
If there's no risk,
we don't have to split anything.

2330
01:28:03,750 --> 01:28:05,750
- That's right.
- That's how it goes.

2331
01:28:05,750 --> 01:28:08,520
We can split the diamonds with you.

2332
01:28:08,520 --> 01:28:10,590
And we need two lives.

2333
01:28:10,590 --> 01:28:13,520
All right. Anyway,

2334
01:28:13,520 --> 01:28:14,920
I get it. So it's 50-50.

2335
01:28:14,920 --> 01:28:16,090
- Then I'll declare war now.
- Okay.

2336
01:28:16,090 --> 01:28:17,090
- All right.
- Okay.

2337
01:28:17,830 --> 01:28:20,400
She asked us to be their ally.

2338
01:28:20,400 --> 01:28:21,400
And we agreed.

2339
01:28:21,400 --> 01:28:23,770
Because we happened to need lives
at that moment as well.

2340
01:28:23,770 --> 01:28:26,440
In fact, what matters more
than the profit split is,

2341
01:28:26,440 --> 01:28:30,140
in case Team White demolishes
Team Blue by a landslide,

2342
01:28:30,140 --> 01:28:33,010
Team White will stay
as a team of six members.

2343
01:28:33,010 --> 01:28:36,480
Considering the balance of power
at this moment,

2344
01:28:36,480 --> 01:28:39,750
if all members of Team White remain,
it's tough for us.

2345
01:28:39,750 --> 01:28:41,080
We need to cut down their numbers.

2346
01:28:43,120 --> 01:28:44,250
Why isn't she coming?

2347
01:29:01,170 --> 01:29:02,940
Here's the biggest problem we face.

2348
01:29:02,940 --> 01:29:04,340
If two of us are left...

2349
01:29:04,340 --> 01:29:06,610
or even only one of us happens to survive,

2350
01:29:06,610 --> 01:29:09,110
then honestly, from now on...

2351
01:29:09,110 --> 01:29:11,810
- So...
- Because we fully understand that,

2352
01:29:11,810 --> 01:29:13,950
we're talking to you first.

2353
01:29:13,950 --> 01:29:17,120
And we're going to make
a sacrifice anyway.

2354
01:29:17,120 --> 01:29:18,620
But that's not going to happen today.

2355
01:29:19,020 --> 01:29:20,190
If you can help us out a bit,

2356
01:29:20,920 --> 01:29:21,920
why don't you turn your gaze
to the other teams?

2357
01:29:23,090 --> 01:29:26,300
I'll go to Team Black. I'll ask,
"What happens to the credits?"

2358
01:29:26,300 --> 01:29:27,460
- That's what I'm going to try.
- Okay.

2359
01:29:28,130 --> 01:29:29,770
- You know...
- I'll go outside.

2360
01:29:29,800 --> 01:29:31,700
Don't you think you need to bring
diamonds with you?

2361
01:29:32,600 --> 01:29:34,370
- Diamonds?
- To buy the weapons for the war first.

2362
01:29:35,300 --> 01:29:37,440
I'll fill my pockets with diamonds.

2363
01:29:37,440 --> 01:29:38,840
I shouldn't let them see the boxes.

2364
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:40,410
(Genie goes
to the Community Center again...)

2365
01:29:40,410 --> 01:29:41,810
(after negotiating with Team Red.)

2366
01:29:41,810 --> 01:29:44,180
- It's the same for you.
- Then wait a minute.

2367
01:29:45,480 --> 01:29:46,780
Genie, by any chance,

2368
01:29:47,180 --> 01:29:49,950
since we can't do anything at this moment,

2369
01:29:50,120 --> 01:29:51,350
why don't we listen
to what these people say...

2370
01:29:51,350 --> 01:29:53,190
- Will you listen to what we say?
- before we leave?

2371
01:29:53,360 --> 01:29:54,460
- Is that okay with you?
- All right.

2372
01:29:54,460 --> 01:29:55,620
- All right?
- Yes.

2373
01:29:56,130 --> 01:29:58,160
The quiz today was so tough.

2374
01:29:58,160 --> 01:30:01,630
So there are not enough lives
that we can get.

2375
01:30:01,730 --> 01:30:05,030
It's natural to think,
"Team White is going to attack for sure."

2376
01:30:05,370 --> 01:30:07,170
But we're not fools either.

2377
01:30:07,470 --> 01:30:09,940
We don't want to get involved
in a war and lose everything.

2378
01:30:10,140 --> 01:30:12,710
If you help us just enough
not to cross the final line...

2379
01:30:12,710 --> 01:30:15,510
Exactly how many lives do you have now
and how many do you need?

2380
01:30:15,510 --> 01:30:17,080
- How many do we need to give you?
- We need three of them.

2381
01:30:17,380 --> 01:30:19,720
Without those, we'll definitely die today.

2382
01:30:20,050 --> 01:30:21,350
To be honest,

2383
01:30:21,350 --> 01:30:24,550
you kept throwing away diamonds you mined
and keeping the balance running negative.

2384
01:30:24,690 --> 01:30:27,790
And after trading, the next day,

2385
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,360
what if you go,
"We do not have enough diamonds today."

2386
01:30:29,360 --> 01:30:30,990
"We have no alternatives
other than declaring war."

2387
01:30:30,990 --> 01:30:33,360
- That's the situation we worried about.
- That's right.

2388
01:30:33,360 --> 01:30:35,000
However, the truth is,

2389
01:30:35,200 --> 01:30:37,100
let's say, tomorrow,

2390
01:30:37,670 --> 01:30:39,700
Team Red gets ten credits.

2391
01:30:40,240 --> 01:30:42,240
They'll have the initiative to attack.

2392
01:30:42,940 --> 01:30:47,040
(If we use a lot of credits,)

2393
01:30:47,040 --> 01:30:48,180
(we can eliminate...)

2394
01:30:48,180 --> 01:30:49,750
(a lot of lives.)

2395
01:30:49,750 --> 01:30:50,750
(It's a bomb.)

2396
01:30:50,910 --> 01:30:55,850
(Team Red has a skill
to destroy life reserves.)

2397
01:30:56,050 --> 01:30:58,520
Then, definitely Team Blue
will be the target.

2398
01:30:58,990 --> 01:31:00,920
We're going to raid Team Red.

2399
01:31:01,020 --> 01:31:02,220
Are you saying we ally...

2400
01:31:02,220 --> 01:31:03,690
- to attack Team Red?
- Yes.

2401
01:31:03,690 --> 01:31:04,890
- You mean we declare war?
- Yes.

2402
01:31:05,390 --> 01:31:06,560
They're up there.

2403
01:31:07,330 --> 01:31:09,000
Then they won't be able to attack us.

2404
01:31:09,030 --> 01:31:10,100
- And...
- Be quiet.

2405
01:31:10,100 --> 01:31:13,870
Please secure at least
a minimum of two lives for us.

2406
01:31:14,340 --> 01:31:16,340
- A minimum amount.
- You can sell them to us.

2407
01:31:16,340 --> 01:31:17,840
(Suggestions of trading 2 lives
and attacking Team Red)

2408
01:31:17,840 --> 01:31:18,940
- We'd appreciate that.
- Right.

2409
01:31:19,780 --> 01:31:21,580
In conclusion, Team White suggested...

2410
01:31:21,740 --> 01:31:24,780
to form an alliance and attack Team Red.

2411
01:31:25,080 --> 01:31:27,750
"Since Team Red has such a skill,"

2412
01:31:27,880 --> 01:31:29,890
"we might as well use
our numerical advantage..."

2413
01:31:30,020 --> 01:31:32,220
"to definitely wipe out one team."

2414
01:31:32,220 --> 01:31:34,120
"We need to keep their credits in check."

2415
01:31:34,420 --> 01:31:36,360
- For now...
- We're a team anyway,

2416
01:31:36,360 --> 01:31:38,390
- so we'll discuss it together quickly.
- Okay.

2417
01:31:38,390 --> 01:31:39,730
- She must be waiting for us.
- Sure.

2418
01:31:39,730 --> 01:31:41,060
She must be worried.

2419
01:31:41,060 --> 01:31:42,700
Please tell her
that she has nothing to worry about.

2420
01:31:45,130 --> 01:31:48,570
In the end, we're going to have
two lives out.

2421
01:31:48,570 --> 01:31:50,340
- It's the same for both of them.
- This is ridiculous.

2422
01:31:50,910 --> 01:31:52,940
You should've told me first.

2423
01:31:52,940 --> 01:31:54,980
How come you talked to them first?

2424
01:31:55,140 --> 01:31:57,250
I had a talk with Team Red first.

2425
01:31:57,380 --> 01:31:59,620
- Team Red said, as we requested,
- Yes.

2426
01:31:59,620 --> 01:32:01,320
regarding the weapons and the costs,

2427
01:32:01,320 --> 01:32:02,850
they'll split them exactly in half.

2428
01:32:02,850 --> 01:32:04,890
Instead, we'll also split
the spoils in half later.

2429
01:32:04,890 --> 01:32:07,090
All they need is two lives.

2430
01:32:07,090 --> 01:32:09,160
Team White wants to ally with us...

2431
01:32:09,560 --> 01:32:10,860
and attack Team Red.

2432
01:32:10,860 --> 01:32:14,230
It's because they find
Team Red's skill dangerous.

2433
01:32:14,230 --> 01:32:16,530
They think it makes sense
to seize their credits.

2434
01:32:16,530 --> 01:32:19,340
And they insist that in the end,
they only need two lives.

2435
01:32:19,570 --> 01:32:21,940
Now, we need to decide
which one we will attack.

2436
01:32:23,040 --> 01:32:24,540
Which team do you trust more?

2437
01:32:24,540 --> 01:32:27,310
To be honest, until a few minutes ago,
I definitely trusted Team Red.

2438
01:32:27,310 --> 01:32:28,310
Same here.

2439
01:32:28,310 --> 01:32:30,110
Until this morning,

2440
01:32:30,110 --> 01:32:32,010
I trusted Team Red, without a doubt.

2441
01:32:32,110 --> 01:32:34,020
However, they changed
their attitude in the middle a while ago.

2442
01:32:34,020 --> 01:32:35,280
That scared me so much.

2443
01:32:35,550 --> 01:32:37,020
If we look at this logically,

2444
01:32:37,290 --> 01:32:39,490
I think it's the right thing
to team up with Team White.

2445
01:32:39,690 --> 01:32:42,490
We just need to think about
what we ultimately want to walk away with.

2446
01:32:43,130 --> 01:32:44,460
Do you want to walk away with money?

2447
01:32:44,560 --> 01:32:46,730
Then we need to ally with Team White.

2448
01:32:46,860 --> 01:32:48,830
Do you need to be safe until the end?

2449
01:32:49,030 --> 01:32:50,970
If you think about that,
we need to choose Team Red.

2450
01:32:51,600 --> 01:32:53,300
Gosh, I'm so confused.

2451
01:32:53,900 --> 01:32:55,770
I like a winning game, no matter what.

2452
01:32:56,740 --> 01:32:58,340
You mean we team up with Team White?

2453
01:32:58,340 --> 01:33:00,640
However, even if...

2454
01:33:00,640 --> 01:33:02,040
- They won't go home, right?
- Team Red is attacked today,

2455
01:33:02,040 --> 01:33:03,980
- they're not going home.
- They have enough time to get things.

2456
01:33:03,980 --> 01:33:05,680
Tomorrow, they'll declare war on us.

2457
01:33:05,850 --> 01:33:08,180
Then shall we just ally with Team Red?
What do you think?

2458
01:33:08,180 --> 01:33:10,650
Honestly, I think Team Red
has the upper hand in power.

2459
01:33:10,650 --> 01:33:12,190
However, on the other hand,
that team is too powerful,

2460
01:33:12,190 --> 01:33:14,520
- so I'm hoping to weaken them.
- That's what I'm saying.

2461
01:33:14,720 --> 01:33:16,260
Anyway, one of those should go home.

2462
01:33:16,260 --> 01:33:18,260
I believe cutting down the numbers
is the right call.

2463
01:33:18,260 --> 01:33:21,400
The bottom line
is that we generated too few lives.

2464
01:33:21,400 --> 01:33:22,430
That's what I'm saying.

2465
01:33:22,430 --> 01:33:23,830
We need to reduce headcount.

2466
01:33:23,830 --> 01:33:26,100
- They need to go home.
- Let's ally with Team Red.

2467
01:33:26,100 --> 01:33:28,000
(The consensus narrows down
to an alliance with Team Red.)

2468
01:33:28,270 --> 01:33:30,040
You don't want to trade credits, do you?

2469
01:33:30,040 --> 01:33:31,170
- Trade credits?
- Yes.

2470
01:33:31,170 --> 01:33:32,170
The idea is on the table.

2471
01:33:32,170 --> 01:33:33,840
- There's a dissident.
- Shall we do that now?

2472
01:33:33,840 --> 01:33:35,210
Yes, if you want to.

2473
01:33:35,310 --> 01:33:36,880
Shall we go?

2474
01:33:38,550 --> 01:33:40,080
Now that I have opened Platform,

2475
01:33:40,080 --> 01:33:41,820
I want to see how it goes.

2476
01:33:41,820 --> 01:33:43,220
(Luna saw Team Red
trying to trade credits.)

2477
01:33:43,220 --> 01:33:44,620
- Look at that.
- Over there.

2478
01:33:45,620 --> 01:33:46,620
Excuse me.

2479
01:33:46,620 --> 01:33:47,720
I wonder...

2480
01:33:48,520 --> 01:33:50,230
how much progress has been made.

2481
01:33:50,430 --> 01:33:52,900
- We can't just wait forever...
- We've reached almost 90 percent.

2482
01:33:52,900 --> 01:33:55,030
Do you want to listen to her?
Do you want to talk?

2483
01:33:55,030 --> 01:33:56,930
- We talked earlier, but...
- Isn't Team Red in front of this place?

2484
01:33:56,930 --> 01:33:58,270
- They left.
- Team Red left with Team Black.

2485
01:33:58,270 --> 01:34:00,170
- Team Red disappeared.
- I wonder if Team Red...

2486
01:34:00,170 --> 01:34:02,170
- is trying to buy Team Black's skill.
- I know.

2487
01:34:02,170 --> 01:34:03,840
- As they're in a tight spot now...
- That's really dangerous.

2488
01:34:03,840 --> 01:34:05,270
How can they buy Team Black's skill?

2489
01:34:05,440 --> 01:34:07,080
If they buy it from Team Black,

2490
01:34:07,080 --> 01:34:08,780
they can get it for a diamond.

2491
01:34:08,780 --> 01:34:10,380
But he'll never sell it like that.

2492
01:34:10,380 --> 01:34:11,610
I suppose he won't sell it that way,

2493
01:34:11,610 --> 01:34:13,980
but if they buy the skill,
they can use it as a threat...

2494
01:34:13,980 --> 01:34:15,550
without using it.

2495
01:34:15,650 --> 01:34:16,950
They might go, "Do you want to ally
and wage a war?"

2496
01:34:16,950 --> 01:34:19,120
"We have this skill. See?"
That's what I'm worried about.

2497
01:34:19,120 --> 01:34:20,760
That's why I came here, getting anxious.

2498
01:34:20,990 --> 01:34:24,460
According to what Team White
said internally,

2499
01:34:24,590 --> 01:34:26,730
they're willing to send away
1 or 2 members.

2500
01:34:26,730 --> 01:34:28,060
That's what I heard.

2501
01:34:28,430 --> 01:34:30,130
We thought so yesterday.

2502
01:34:30,130 --> 01:34:31,970
We need to run the numbers too.

2503
01:34:31,970 --> 01:34:33,240
But if we lose one member,

2504
01:34:33,240 --> 01:34:36,040
we'll surely become
the target of a war afterward.

2505
01:34:36,170 --> 01:34:37,840
So for us, it's the right thing
to wage a war...

2506
01:34:37,840 --> 01:34:39,710
before we lose one member.

2507
01:34:39,910 --> 01:34:42,210
- Before you lose a member?
- If we lose one person,

2508
01:34:42,210 --> 01:34:43,580
there will be only five of us tomorrow.

2509
01:34:43,580 --> 01:34:45,650
Then if two teams team up,
we become a minority.

2510
01:34:46,620 --> 01:34:49,620
Other teams might think
that we can sacrifice...

2511
01:34:49,620 --> 01:34:51,420
at least one player.

2512
01:34:51,520 --> 01:34:52,890
However, the moment it happens,

2513
01:34:52,890 --> 01:34:54,990
our team starts tomorrow
as a team of five.

2514
01:34:54,990 --> 01:34:56,760
We'll be short of lives again anyway.

2515
01:34:56,860 --> 01:34:58,290
Then it's a war again.

2516
01:34:58,290 --> 01:35:00,160
And it's 6 to 5.

2517
01:35:00,160 --> 01:35:02,970
Rather than being 6 to 5
and keeping the war going,

2518
01:35:02,970 --> 01:35:06,140
we'd start with 6 to 6
and have a chance to win.

2519
01:35:06,140 --> 01:35:08,870
I thought it would be more advantageous
to drag them in first.

2520
01:35:09,100 --> 01:35:11,940
To be honest, what surprised me...

2521
01:35:11,940 --> 01:35:14,510
was that Luna was very hesitant...

2522
01:35:14,840 --> 01:35:18,080
to discuss reducing the headcount.

2523
01:35:18,250 --> 01:35:20,480
But I wondered, "In that case,"

2524
01:35:20,550 --> 01:35:22,120
"if there are casualties,"

2525
01:35:22,120 --> 01:35:24,320
"aren't we the ones losing our headcount?"

2526
01:35:24,650 --> 01:35:28,490
Let's say we ally with Team White
and we need to let one person go.

2527
01:35:28,490 --> 01:35:31,260
When Team White has that many players
and none of them wants to go,

2528
01:35:31,760 --> 01:35:34,600
we could end up getting abandoned.
That was what I thought.

2529
01:35:35,430 --> 01:35:37,970
But in this situation,

2530
01:35:37,970 --> 01:35:39,570
- it's a different story.
- Right.

2531
01:35:40,000 --> 01:35:41,440
Is the story going to be negative?

2532
01:35:41,440 --> 01:35:43,840
It could be either positive or negative,
but it will be different.

2533
01:35:44,340 --> 01:35:45,970
So we're going to get two lives,

2534
01:35:45,970 --> 01:35:48,410
and get one more,

2535
01:35:48,410 --> 01:35:49,910
- we're going to attack them.
- Team Red, I see.

2536
01:35:50,650 --> 01:35:51,650
Maillard,

2537
01:35:52,510 --> 01:35:54,620
isn't Team Blue waiting for us?

2538
01:35:54,880 --> 01:35:56,120
- Why?
- Team Blue,

2539
01:35:56,490 --> 01:35:58,190
being in a certain situation,

2540
01:35:58,190 --> 01:35:59,420
they're not taking any action...

2541
01:35:59,420 --> 01:36:01,660
- since we're not there.
- Shall we go there and see?

2542
01:36:01,660 --> 01:36:02,660
- Yes.
- Let's go.

2543
01:36:02,830 --> 01:36:03,960
The alliance...

2544
01:36:03,960 --> 01:36:05,890
- We'll go and check it out for a minute.
- Okay.

2545
01:36:05,890 --> 01:36:06,930
All right.

2546
01:36:07,900 --> 01:36:09,730
This is one of the things
we're concerned about.

2547
01:36:09,870 --> 01:36:12,600
In fact, in the case of Team Red,
even if they lose today,

2548
01:36:12,870 --> 01:36:15,140
none of them has to go home.

2549
01:36:15,370 --> 01:36:16,570
- Why?
- Why wouldn't they go home?

2550
01:36:16,770 --> 01:36:18,040
Can all of them stay
with only half of their lives?

2551
01:36:18,040 --> 01:36:19,170
They have enough lives.

2552
01:36:19,170 --> 01:36:21,180
Then they have the most lives.

2553
01:36:21,180 --> 01:36:22,680
Yes, they have a lot of those.

2554
01:36:22,680 --> 01:36:25,050
If that's the case,
they should have given us...

2555
01:36:25,050 --> 01:36:26,880
- the lives yesterday even more so.
- They should have.

2556
01:36:26,880 --> 01:36:28,220
We really had no credits.

2557
01:36:28,220 --> 01:36:30,090
- We had no credits.
- We used all, so we have zero credits.

2558
01:36:30,090 --> 01:36:31,250
Then you could have asked us...

2559
01:36:31,250 --> 01:36:32,890
- for aid.
- We could have made a transfer...

2560
01:36:32,890 --> 01:36:34,990
- and given you more.
- That's what I'm saying.

2561
01:36:35,690 --> 01:36:36,790
But you gave us only one.

2562
01:36:36,790 --> 01:36:38,030
It's because you gave us none.

2563
01:36:38,030 --> 01:36:39,330
You didn't give us any.
How could we give you more?

2564
01:36:39,330 --> 01:36:41,130
- We didn't get any.
- I get it.

2565
01:36:41,130 --> 01:36:42,530
- Stop it.
- When we say just one word,

2566
01:36:42,530 --> 01:36:43,800
- five of you swarm us.
- We can't do this.

2567
01:36:43,800 --> 01:36:45,530
When each of you says a word,

2568
01:36:45,530 --> 01:36:46,770
- we get five words back.
- I'm sorry.

2569
01:36:46,770 --> 01:36:50,410
In reality, the bottom line is that
we can't help...

2570
01:36:50,410 --> 01:36:52,510
- but feel intimidated by your headcount.
- Exactly.

2571
01:36:52,510 --> 01:36:54,310
Looking at your attitude as a whole,

2572
01:36:54,310 --> 01:36:56,810
- it's scary for us...
- That's right.

2573
01:36:56,810 --> 01:36:58,910
- to blindly believe in this alliance.
- I understand.

2574
01:36:58,910 --> 01:37:00,380
- I know.
- It's because...

2575
01:37:00,380 --> 01:37:03,090
there has to be some consensus that
we can eliminate a few mouths to feed...

2576
01:37:03,090 --> 01:37:06,590
if things go sideways within the team.

2577
01:37:06,590 --> 01:37:08,420
Otherwise, we'll end up in a situation...

2578
01:37:08,420 --> 01:37:10,760
- where our entire team gets wiped out.
- The reason...

2579
01:37:10,760 --> 01:37:14,430
why we're saying
we can't sacrifice any of us is this.

2580
01:37:14,600 --> 01:37:17,230
If a casualty occurs in our team,
we'll be the very first victims.

2581
01:37:17,500 --> 01:37:18,970
When we both have casualties
at the same time,

2582
01:37:18,970 --> 01:37:20,740
we can let go 1 or 2 of us.

2583
01:37:20,740 --> 01:37:23,270
But if we have to make
the first sacrifice today,

2584
01:37:23,270 --> 01:37:24,840
we'll be at too much of a disadvantage.

2585
01:37:25,140 --> 01:37:26,580
Even if that's true,

2586
01:37:26,580 --> 01:37:29,280
in the first place, the reason
we're even in this war...

2587
01:37:29,610 --> 01:37:32,480
is that the 5-3-3 setup
is just too heavy for us.

2588
01:37:33,080 --> 01:37:35,750
Then you can just do 3-3
to make it 6, can't you?

2589
01:37:36,990 --> 01:37:38,490
Right? As we play along this game,

2590
01:37:38,650 --> 01:37:40,920
Team Red might have the upper hand
if they go to war.

2591
01:37:40,920 --> 01:37:42,260
Then you need to ally with Team Red.

2592
01:37:42,260 --> 01:37:43,990
Team Blue is destined
to ally with someone.

2593
01:37:44,430 --> 01:37:46,260
So, you just need to align yourselves
with the winning side.

2594
01:37:46,260 --> 01:37:47,860
And today, it should be us.

2595
01:37:47,860 --> 01:37:49,000
That's exactly why we're making
a transparent proposal.

2596
01:37:49,000 --> 01:37:50,400
Yes. You can just use one enemy
to defeat another.

2597
01:37:50,600 --> 01:37:52,940
But in this situation,
if we ally with you,

2598
01:37:52,940 --> 01:37:54,200
- we become betrayers.
- Right.

2599
01:37:54,200 --> 01:37:55,770
- Team Red will attack us.
- Yes.

2600
01:37:55,770 --> 01:37:58,240
No, what I'm asking is, does betrayal
even play a part in this?

2601
01:37:58,240 --> 01:37:59,610
On the first day, you asked us
to ally with you. And the next day,

2602
01:37:59,610 --> 01:38:01,480
- you negotiated with Team Red.
- No, I'm saying it...

2603
01:38:01,480 --> 01:38:02,810
from the perspective...

2604
01:38:02,810 --> 01:38:03,980
- of Team Red.
- That's right.

2605
01:38:03,980 --> 01:38:05,280
We're the ones Team Red
would hold a grudge against.

2606
01:38:05,280 --> 01:38:06,280
- I'm not saying we're betrayers.
- No.

2607
01:38:06,280 --> 01:38:07,650
Team Red isn't a team...

2608
01:38:07,650 --> 01:38:08,920
- that gets swayed by emotions.
- Not by emotions.

2609
01:38:08,920 --> 01:38:10,650
- They only look at resources.
- They will attack...

2610
01:38:10,650 --> 01:38:11,820
whoever holds the most assets.

2611
01:38:11,820 --> 01:38:12,820
And that's us.

2612
01:38:12,820 --> 01:38:15,090
Anyway, when it's all said and done,

2613
01:38:15,090 --> 01:38:16,530
Team White is the only one
who can issue the currency,

2614
01:38:16,530 --> 01:38:17,830
- not us.
- Right.

2615
01:38:17,830 --> 01:38:20,230
Are you even in a position to give us...

2616
01:38:20,230 --> 01:38:21,800
a verbal promise
that you won't overissue the currency?

2617
01:38:21,800 --> 01:38:23,670
Actually, we gave you the verbal promise
from the first day.

2618
01:38:23,670 --> 01:38:25,500
Can you give us the exact numbers?

2619
01:38:25,500 --> 01:38:28,200
To be honest, that's something
we have no way of knowing.

2620
01:38:28,200 --> 01:38:29,870
We've been keeping our promise,

2621
01:38:29,870 --> 01:38:31,510
but you haven't.

2622
01:38:34,180 --> 01:38:36,480
However, when we talk...

2623
01:38:36,480 --> 01:38:37,780
- about why it ended up this way,
- We get it. Okay.

2624
01:38:37,780 --> 01:38:41,020
Team White never told us
there are limits either.

2625
01:38:41,020 --> 01:38:42,680
Then tell us our total life supply.

2626
01:38:43,150 --> 01:38:44,890
- We didn't know the limits either.
- It's everyone's last resort.

2627
01:38:44,890 --> 01:38:46,560
- It's because we don't know.
- All right. Then for now,

2628
01:38:46,560 --> 01:38:48,960
- since everyone is forced to lie,
- Everyone here...

2629
01:38:48,960 --> 01:38:50,390
- has told a lie.
- let's set that aside.

2630
01:38:50,560 --> 01:38:52,330
- Everyone here had told a lie.
- We haven't told a lie.

2631
01:38:52,330 --> 01:38:53,500
- Right?
- We haven't.

2632
01:38:53,700 --> 01:38:55,000
I mean, that team...

2633
01:38:55,000 --> 01:38:57,600
came to us asking to form an alliance
on the first day.

2634
01:38:58,000 --> 01:38:59,470
The next day, they completely ignored us.

2635
01:38:59,670 --> 01:39:01,570
They cut us off, but like absolute idiots,

2636
01:39:01,570 --> 01:39:04,570
we still handed over
our credits anyway. And then,

2637
01:39:04,710 --> 01:39:06,340
they ignored us again.

2638
01:39:06,340 --> 01:39:09,380
Isn't that, at the very least,
a violation of basic business ethics?

2639
01:39:09,610 --> 01:39:14,050
I thought they wouldn't listen to us
even if we persuaded them earnestly.

2640
01:39:14,580 --> 01:39:17,950
That wasn't an unacceptable claim.

2641
01:39:18,090 --> 01:39:19,720
It was only a threat.

2642
01:39:19,720 --> 01:39:22,760
From Team Blue's position,
it's the same for today and tomorrow.

2643
01:39:23,090 --> 01:39:24,530
They must have found us ridiculous.

2644
01:39:24,830 --> 01:39:28,200
Since there are only three of us,
we're already outnumbered.

2645
01:39:28,260 --> 01:39:30,730
We were already losing the numbers game,
but they kept pressuring us.

2646
01:39:30,800 --> 01:39:33,270
The moment I uttered a single word,
I got bombarded with five in return,

2647
01:39:33,270 --> 01:39:34,570
and it was honestly terrifying.

2648
01:39:34,670 --> 01:39:37,440
The feeling of being threatened
we felt at that moment...

2649
01:39:37,440 --> 01:39:40,440
was perceived as violence.

2650
01:39:41,610 --> 01:39:43,380
Are they already arguing inside?

2651
01:39:44,680 --> 01:39:46,080
The sign doesn't say it's occupied.

2652
01:39:48,920 --> 01:39:50,290
Why are you all standing at the entrance?

2653
01:39:50,290 --> 01:39:51,820
- It feels very cool here.
- Because it's cool?

2654
01:39:51,820 --> 01:39:53,120
- That's nice.
- What's going on?

2655
01:39:54,120 --> 01:39:56,120
First of all,
regarding our actual needs...

2656
01:39:56,120 --> 01:39:57,660
If you could just give us three minutes,

2657
01:39:57,660 --> 01:40:00,060
we'd like to take a moment
to evaluate our own needs.

2658
01:40:00,430 --> 01:40:02,430
We can totally understand
what you're saying now,

2659
01:40:02,430 --> 01:40:03,930
- and we totally can see your attitude.
- Okay.

2660
01:40:03,930 --> 01:40:05,230
- All right.
- We'll discuss it,

2661
01:40:05,700 --> 01:40:07,500
- and let's meet up in three minutes.
- All right.

2662
01:40:07,870 --> 01:40:08,940
What's going on?

2663
01:40:09,270 --> 01:40:10,570
I think we need to pull out of this.

2664
01:40:14,240 --> 01:40:15,280
Gosh, really.

2665
01:40:18,180 --> 01:40:19,250
Is this right?

2666
01:40:20,150 --> 01:40:21,250
I think...

2667
01:40:21,980 --> 01:40:23,290
To which team are you attracted now?

2668
01:40:23,820 --> 01:40:26,020
Honestly, I was attracted
to Team Red first.

2669
01:40:26,320 --> 01:40:27,960
Listening to them talk,

2670
01:40:28,320 --> 01:40:30,290
it seems they have a lot
of built-up resentment toward us.

2671
01:40:30,830 --> 01:40:32,260
They seem to have
so many grievances against us.

2672
01:40:32,260 --> 01:40:33,360
And to be honest,

2673
01:40:33,360 --> 01:40:36,500
I don't really understand their comment,

2674
01:40:36,500 --> 01:40:38,500
"If a casualty occurs today,
we'll be the first ones to go."

2675
01:40:38,500 --> 01:40:39,770
That's what I don't understand either.

2676
01:40:39,770 --> 01:40:41,170
Of course, that team should be
the first to produce a casualty.

2677
01:40:41,170 --> 01:40:43,110
The bottom line is, our basic premise...

2678
01:40:43,110 --> 01:40:46,710
is that we need to cut down
Team White's headcount.

2679
01:40:46,840 --> 01:40:49,850
Honestly, watching them swarm us...

2680
01:40:50,180 --> 01:40:52,250
with those numbers made me realize...

2681
01:40:52,780 --> 01:40:54,050
this is just too much.

2682
01:40:54,680 --> 01:40:56,450
If we side with Team White here,

2683
01:40:56,850 --> 01:40:58,290
it's an act of violence against Team Red.

2684
01:40:59,820 --> 01:41:02,790
I really can't go through this
now that I've experienced it myself.

2685
01:41:02,790 --> 01:41:03,860
We shouldn't do this.

2686
01:41:03,860 --> 01:41:05,860
This is too unethical.

2687
01:41:14,270 --> 01:41:15,470
- Right?
- Yes.

2688
01:41:15,470 --> 01:41:17,140
- We're on the same page, right?
- Yes.

2689
01:41:41,200 --> 01:41:43,200
We declare war.

2690
01:41:44,900 --> 01:41:48,000
Please state the target team
you wish to declare war on.

2691
01:41:59,180 --> 01:42:00,280
It's Team White.

2692
01:42:01,680 --> 01:42:05,490
Team Blue has declared war on Team White.

2693
01:42:07,060 --> 01:42:11,260
Today's war cost is zero diamonds,

2694
01:42:11,730 --> 01:42:13,430
so the payment has been completed.

2695
01:42:15,500 --> 01:42:17,400
- A war has been declared.
- The siren sounds.

2696
01:42:18,270 --> 01:42:20,370
- Team Blue has declared war...
- What?

2697
01:42:20,370 --> 01:42:22,100
on Team White.

2698
01:42:22,100 --> 01:42:23,140
Let's go.

2699
01:42:23,610 --> 01:42:25,510
They sided with this team here.

2700
01:42:25,710 --> 01:42:26,710
Wait a minute.

2701
01:42:26,940 --> 01:42:28,380
- That's right.
- Team Red and Team Blue.

2702
01:42:28,380 --> 01:42:29,680
- What?
- We're in a state of war.

2703
01:42:30,250 --> 01:42:34,480
As of this moment, Community Town
is transitioning to a state of war.

2704
01:42:34,920 --> 01:42:39,220
(State of war)

2705
01:42:39,520 --> 01:42:40,990
As we're in a state of war,

2706
01:42:41,290 --> 01:42:44,430
all functions of Community Town
are suspended.

2707
01:42:46,060 --> 01:42:47,760
When the siren blared,

2708
01:42:47,760 --> 01:42:50,770
I totally felt like
I was stabbed in the back.

2709
01:42:50,770 --> 01:42:52,200
I was just dumbfounded.

2710
01:42:52,470 --> 01:42:54,740
I thought I now had to kill them all.

2711
01:42:55,240 --> 01:42:56,840
The prize had no meaning anyway.

2712
01:42:57,110 --> 01:42:58,910
I will see who goes down first.

2713
01:42:59,410 --> 01:43:01,440
What kind of crazy stunt is this?

2714
01:43:01,440 --> 01:43:03,450
Are they seriously planning
to go on a reckless rampage?

2715
01:43:04,010 --> 01:43:05,780
If you're going to do this, fine.
Let's do it.

2716
01:43:06,110 --> 01:43:08,420
You're all going to die.
But we'll be the ones left standing.

2717
01:43:10,450 --> 01:43:12,750
Inside, I cheered. It's war.

2718
01:43:13,760 --> 01:43:15,090
I'm so happy now.

2719
01:43:15,320 --> 01:43:17,690
On the surface, I might look
totally strapped and anxious,

2720
01:43:17,690 --> 01:43:20,500
"No, we can't have a war.
What's going to happen now?"

2721
01:43:20,500 --> 01:43:22,630
"I finally opened the Platform today
with great difficulty,"

2722
01:43:22,630 --> 01:43:25,130
"but I couldn't make a single trade
and have no revenue. What do I do?"

2723
01:43:25,570 --> 01:43:26,940
That might be how I look to others.

2724
01:43:27,270 --> 01:43:29,940
However, everything
is happening just as I wish.

2725
01:43:31,970 --> 01:43:34,010
I think the justification
Pitou mentioned earlier is right.

2726
01:43:34,010 --> 01:43:35,310
What? Which one?

2727
01:43:35,310 --> 01:43:37,780
When she realized
the headcount of six people...

2728
01:43:38,110 --> 01:43:41,620
And honestly, I think it's right
to attack the side that's more desperate.

2729
01:43:41,780 --> 01:43:43,050
What makes them more desperate?

2730
01:43:43,050 --> 01:43:45,150
It's because the probability
that they go home increases.

2731
01:43:46,090 --> 01:43:48,490
Team White might come to us,
asking to ally.

2732
01:43:49,160 --> 01:43:50,260
That's possible.

2733
01:43:50,790 --> 01:43:52,430
It would be so funny if they came.

2734
01:43:52,430 --> 01:43:53,500
Right.

2735
01:43:54,700 --> 01:43:56,360
The ones who claim to be for peace...

2736
01:43:56,360 --> 01:43:58,000
are going around stirring up trouble
everywhere right now.

2737
01:43:59,030 --> 01:44:01,200
One minute they say they'll kill us,
and the next they're going to help us.

2738
01:44:02,200 --> 01:44:04,370
If you're going to be like that,
split up right now.

2739
01:44:05,140 --> 01:44:06,240
I can see through your dark intentions.

2740
01:44:07,340 --> 01:44:08,640
Our color has never changed.
We were always red.

2741
01:44:09,840 --> 01:44:11,310
We have to think about winning this.

2742
01:44:11,310 --> 01:44:12,810
- And Team Red...
- We have to persuade Team Red.

2743
01:44:12,810 --> 01:44:14,680
We just need to think about how we
can give Team Red a proper justification.

2744
01:44:14,680 --> 01:44:17,420
Or, at least, we need to tell
Team Red to do nothing about it.

2745
01:44:17,420 --> 01:44:20,060
Yes. We need to tell them
to do nothing or be on our team.

2746
01:44:20,560 --> 01:44:23,730
We can talk anyway
when we go to buy weapons.

2747
01:44:23,990 --> 01:44:25,390
We all need to buy weapons, definitely.

2748
01:44:25,390 --> 01:44:26,860
- No matter what.
- We all have to.

2749
01:44:27,060 --> 01:44:29,030
The prize doesn't matter now.

2750
01:44:29,200 --> 01:44:30,200
No.

2751
01:44:30,530 --> 01:44:32,570
- We all need to buy one.
- One for each.

2752
01:44:32,570 --> 01:44:34,200
We all need to get one.
The more expensive, the stronger it is.

2753
01:44:34,270 --> 01:44:36,040
Gosh, they have no idea
how expensive weapons are.

2754
01:44:37,570 --> 01:44:41,740
(The rule card on the detailed rules
of the war arrives.)

2755
01:44:42,510 --> 01:44:44,010
Please read this.

2756
01:44:44,180 --> 01:44:46,150
- I will read this for you.
- Okay.

2757
01:44:46,780 --> 01:44:48,750
The detailed rules of war.

2758
01:44:49,050 --> 01:44:50,220
Forming an alliance.

2759
01:44:50,390 --> 01:44:53,590
Team Blue and Team White that are
included in the declaration of war...

2760
01:44:54,260 --> 01:44:57,090
can ask Team Red to form an alliance.

2761
01:44:58,090 --> 01:44:59,730
If you want to form an alliance,

2762
01:44:59,930 --> 01:45:02,060
use the call button in your dormitory...

2763
01:45:02,330 --> 01:45:05,430
and request a meeting
at the Community Center.

2764
01:45:06,200 --> 01:45:09,470
When the request is accepted,
all the residents of the two teams...

2765
01:45:09,870 --> 01:45:11,540
visit the Community Center.

2766
01:45:11,710 --> 01:45:15,410
After the two leaders declare an alliance,
the alliance is formed.

2767
01:45:15,740 --> 01:45:18,250
If they win or lose the war,

2768
01:45:18,450 --> 01:45:20,350
the two teams, upon mutual agreement,

2769
01:45:20,350 --> 01:45:23,950
shall either submit or collect the spoils.

2770
01:45:24,150 --> 01:45:27,120
The quantity of the spoils of war
is determined...

2771
01:45:27,560 --> 01:45:29,920
based on the teams
in the initial declaration,

2772
01:45:29,920 --> 01:45:31,790
excluding the alliance team.

2773
01:45:31,930 --> 01:45:35,030
While the quantity is strictly based
on the parties involved,

2774
01:45:35,200 --> 01:45:38,070
the actual payment can still be made
together with the alliance.

2775
01:45:38,270 --> 01:45:40,870
During the state of war,

2776
01:45:40,870 --> 01:45:42,740
you can purchase weapons
at the Community Center.

2777
01:45:43,440 --> 01:45:46,410
There is one weapon per class...

2778
01:45:46,410 --> 01:45:47,780
available for Classes A, B, and C.

2779
01:45:48,010 --> 01:45:50,750
and there's no limit
on the purchase quantity per team.

2780
01:45:51,080 --> 01:45:53,750
Then if someone dashes and gets one
for each class, that's it?

2781
01:45:53,750 --> 01:45:55,250
That means it's first come, first served.

2782
01:45:55,250 --> 01:45:56,450
That's exactly right.

2783
01:45:56,450 --> 01:45:57,820
But our dormitory is located
in such a high spot...

2784
01:45:57,950 --> 01:45:59,390
when we need to run
to the Community Center.

2785
01:45:59,390 --> 01:46:00,520
Shall we wait with our shoes on?

2786
01:46:00,590 --> 01:46:02,090
(Springing to his feet)

2787
01:46:02,260 --> 01:46:04,630
The war cost and the weapon cost...

2788
01:46:04,830 --> 01:46:07,330
will be deducted
from the total prize pool,

2789
01:46:07,660 --> 01:46:09,900
equivalent to the value of the diamonds
at the time of purchase.

2790
01:46:10,930 --> 01:46:12,900
You can request a meeting
and purchase weapons...

2791
01:46:13,100 --> 01:46:15,270
after the announcement.

2792
01:46:16,740 --> 01:46:18,970
It would be great if we could just reach
a good agreement...

2793
01:46:18,970 --> 01:46:21,510
and fight without any weapons.

2794
01:46:21,780 --> 01:46:25,310
But Team White is desperate now,
so that won't happen.

2795
01:46:25,310 --> 01:46:26,950
But is Team White
really desperate enough to survive...

2796
01:46:26,950 --> 01:46:28,380
at the cost of cutting down
the total prize pool?

2797
01:46:28,380 --> 01:46:29,680
- Of course.
- Of course they are.

2798
01:46:31,320 --> 01:46:33,320
Let's say you're about to die today.

2799
01:46:33,320 --> 01:46:35,160
- Why would you care?
- Why would you increase the prize pool...

2800
01:46:35,160 --> 01:46:36,290
- for those left here?
- You don't have to care.

2801
01:46:36,660 --> 01:46:38,760
- Is that so?
- Sure.

2802
01:46:38,760 --> 01:46:40,160
I wouldn't do so,
if I'm going to die anyway.

2803
01:46:40,160 --> 01:46:41,830
- Would you die just like that?
- I wouldn't go that far.

2804
01:46:42,000 --> 01:46:44,670
- No, not before you actually die.
- You should try your best.

2805
01:46:48,300 --> 01:46:49,870
I don't care about the prize money
or anything else anymore.

2806
01:46:51,010 --> 01:46:52,640
This is going to be deducted
from our total prize pool.

2807
01:46:52,640 --> 01:46:53,980
Bring it here.

2808
01:46:54,310 --> 01:46:55,880
So we can't issue the currency now?

2809
01:46:55,880 --> 01:46:56,910
- No.
- We can't.

2810
01:46:57,180 --> 01:46:59,580
It's deducted based
on the current value of the diamonds.

2811
01:46:59,580 --> 01:47:00,820
- Yes.
- At its current value.

2812
01:47:00,820 --> 01:47:02,620
- How much is it per each now?
- It's 500 dollars.

2813
01:47:02,620 --> 01:47:03,650
- Is it 500 dollars?
- Yes.

2814
01:47:03,650 --> 01:47:05,350
Then 1,000 dollars will be deducted
if we get 2 of those.

2815
01:47:05,350 --> 01:47:06,390
Right.

2816
01:47:08,990 --> 01:47:12,360
Everything is going exactly
as I planned. This is amazing.

2817
01:47:12,360 --> 01:47:15,160
We can purchase weapons
during this state of war.

2818
01:47:15,160 --> 01:47:16,500
Then while we're at that,

2819
01:47:16,500 --> 01:47:18,370
someone can request a meeting
with Team Red...

2820
01:47:18,530 --> 01:47:20,500
and talk about it to them.

2821
01:47:20,500 --> 01:47:22,140
- Talk about what?
- Someone buys the weapons...

2822
01:47:22,140 --> 01:47:23,670
I hear something.

2823
01:47:26,170 --> 01:47:27,240
- They're announcing something.
- Get ready to press it.

2824
01:47:27,240 --> 01:47:30,380
From now on, you can request a meeting.

2825
01:47:30,910 --> 01:47:32,510
When the request is accepted,

2826
01:47:32,510 --> 01:47:34,380
you will receive an instruction.

2827
01:47:34,380 --> 01:47:37,120
- We need to call Team Red.
- And if you want to purchase weapons,

2828
01:47:37,250 --> 01:47:39,250
please bring diamonds with you.

2829
01:47:39,250 --> 01:47:41,390
- I think so, but...
- Not only the leaders...

2830
01:47:41,390 --> 01:47:44,860
but the residents can also purchase them
by paying with diamonds.

2831
01:47:45,090 --> 01:47:46,860
- Shall we go?
- You need to take diamonds with you.

2832
01:47:47,100 --> 01:47:48,700
- Come with me.
- Shall we go?

2833
01:47:48,830 --> 01:47:50,060
- Go.
- Hurry!

2834
01:47:50,060 --> 01:47:51,100
(Team White dashes
right after the announcement.)

2835
01:47:51,100 --> 01:47:52,500
Gosh, do we really have to do this?

2836
01:47:54,200 --> 01:47:55,270
Watch out!

2837
01:48:02,680 --> 01:48:05,180
- Does it mean we can buy them now?
- I guess so. We need to run now.

2838
01:48:05,350 --> 01:48:06,450
If Team White runs now...

2839
01:48:06,450 --> 01:48:08,380
and gets all Classes A to C,
it's over. Am I right?

2840
01:48:08,380 --> 01:48:10,790
Right. Why isn't Team Blue running?

2841
01:48:11,820 --> 01:48:13,290
Team White requested a meeting.

2842
01:48:13,820 --> 01:48:14,890
We will decline it.

2843
01:48:15,690 --> 01:48:17,460
The request for a meeting
has been declined.

2844
01:48:17,460 --> 01:48:18,560
They declined our request.

2845
01:48:20,160 --> 01:48:21,160
They declined it.

2846
01:48:21,800 --> 01:48:23,770
- I will be in front of the Center.
- Okay.

2847
01:48:24,270 --> 01:48:26,800
Why isn't Team Blue calling us right away?

2848
01:48:26,800 --> 01:48:28,000
Are they not really in a rush?

2849
01:48:28,370 --> 01:48:30,140
What are you thinking now, Team Blue?
What's wrong with you?

2850
01:48:30,140 --> 01:48:33,040
Get your act together.
We just started it, and we have to win.

2851
01:48:33,140 --> 01:48:34,610
Don't we need to meet
Team Red in the first place?

2852
01:48:34,610 --> 01:48:36,810
We should ask them to lend us
what they have.

2853
01:48:37,610 --> 01:48:39,550
- Gosh, wait a minute.
- Team Blue...

2854
01:48:39,550 --> 01:48:41,950
requests a meeting with Team Red.

2855
01:48:42,080 --> 01:48:43,350
I guess they don't feel
any sense of urgency.

2856
01:48:43,450 --> 01:48:44,620
Then tell them to suit themselves.

2857
01:48:45,420 --> 01:48:46,820
(Team Blue requests a meeting
with Team Red.)

2858
01:48:46,820 --> 01:48:48,460
- Accept it.
- We'll accept it.

2859
01:48:48,460 --> 01:48:49,560
Let's go to the Center.

2860
01:48:50,090 --> 01:48:51,430
Let's go to the Center!

2861
01:48:52,330 --> 01:48:53,360
How can we get it?

2862
01:48:55,900 --> 01:48:57,430
I hope they're not waiting there.

2863
01:49:01,470 --> 01:49:03,370
Gosh, this is tough.

2864
01:49:05,140 --> 01:49:08,610
(Team White arrives at the Center first.)

2865
01:49:09,640 --> 01:49:10,710
He's coming, right?

2866
01:49:11,380 --> 01:49:12,380
You're so fast.

2867
01:49:13,750 --> 01:49:15,680
(Occupied: Please wait.)

2868
01:49:15,680 --> 01:49:17,450
We'll purchase weapons.

2869
01:49:18,020 --> 01:49:20,460
The weapon costs are as follows.

2870
01:49:20,460 --> 01:49:22,490
(Weapon costs)

2871
01:49:22,490 --> 01:49:23,830
It's one each.

2872
01:49:24,160 --> 01:49:27,160
The weapon costs are 90, 70, and 40...

2873
01:49:27,300 --> 01:49:30,800
for Classes A, B, and C, respectively.

2874
01:49:31,170 --> 01:49:34,040
The total of the weapons
I designed today...

2875
01:49:34,040 --> 01:49:35,770
is 200 diamonds.

2876
01:49:35,770 --> 01:49:37,640
Since the total issuance is 400,

2877
01:49:37,640 --> 01:49:41,210
it's 100,000 dollars, which is half
of the total prize, 200,000 dollars.

2878
01:49:41,680 --> 01:49:43,850
A is 90, B is 70, and C is 40.

2879
01:49:43,850 --> 01:49:45,510
- We can only buy one each?
- Yes.

2880
01:49:45,510 --> 01:49:46,650
Let's buy everything.

2881
01:49:46,650 --> 01:49:48,380
- If we buy everything, we're all in.
- It costs 200.

2882
01:49:48,380 --> 01:49:49,620
It's 200. I know.

2883
01:49:49,620 --> 01:49:50,650
- Shall we buy them all?
- Yes.

2884
01:49:51,650 --> 01:49:53,490
(Class A Weapon, 90 diamonds:
45,000 dollars)

2885
01:49:53,490 --> 01:49:55,590
(Class B Weapon, 70 diamonds:
35,000 dollars)

2886
01:49:55,590 --> 01:49:57,660
(Class C Weapon, 40 diamonds:
20,000 dollars)

2887
01:49:57,760 --> 01:50:00,500
State the class of the weapon
you wish to purchase...

2888
01:50:00,500 --> 01:50:01,630
Shall we only buy Class A and C weapons?

2889
01:50:01,630 --> 01:50:03,930
and put the diamonds in the central box.

2890
01:50:03,930 --> 01:50:07,000
- We should buy them all.
- I agree. In the end...

2891
01:50:11,010 --> 01:50:12,870
This is so exciting.

2892
01:50:13,940 --> 01:50:15,510
We have to buy Class A weapon for sure.

2893
01:50:15,510 --> 01:50:17,480
- That's a must.
- Let's buy Class A first.

2894
01:50:17,480 --> 01:50:18,910
We'll buy Class A weapon.

2895
01:50:19,580 --> 01:50:21,780
You've purchased Class A weapon.

2896
01:50:21,780 --> 01:50:23,420
We'll buy Class B weapon.

2897
01:50:23,620 --> 01:50:25,720
No, my diamonds!

2898
01:50:25,920 --> 01:50:28,020
You've purchased Class B weapon.

2899
01:50:28,020 --> 01:50:29,290
We'll buy Class C weapon.

2900
01:50:29,390 --> 01:50:31,660
You've purchased Class C weapon.

2901
01:50:33,030 --> 01:50:36,230
Actually, we felt betrayed by Team Blue...

2902
01:50:36,330 --> 01:50:37,800
from the moment the war broke out.

2903
01:50:37,900 --> 01:50:41,570
The war they started was their way
of saying they'd cut off our lives...

2904
01:50:41,570 --> 01:50:43,770
even at the cost of the prize money,

2905
01:50:43,770 --> 01:50:46,440
so we were going to buy weapons
to teach them a lesson.

2906
01:50:46,440 --> 01:50:49,080
I definitely thought
we had to buy them all.

2907
01:50:49,080 --> 01:50:51,580
It meant we're spending 100,000 dollars.

2908
01:50:51,680 --> 01:50:53,250
But we had to buy them.

2909
01:50:53,780 --> 01:50:55,120
It'll be helpful.

2910
01:50:55,120 --> 01:50:56,850
If it doesn't,

2911
01:50:56,850 --> 01:51:00,490
we're spending 100,000 dollars
to show how scary the war is.

2912
01:51:00,590 --> 01:51:01,990
I didn't regret spending.

2913
01:51:01,990 --> 01:51:03,730
Since they started the war,

2914
01:51:03,730 --> 01:51:06,160
I thought we had to bear
that level of risk.

2915
01:51:06,160 --> 01:51:08,430
We don't care
if there's no prize money left.

2916
01:51:08,430 --> 01:51:09,830
That's what I thought.

2917
01:51:09,930 --> 01:51:11,270
So we bought them all.

2918
01:51:11,730 --> 01:51:14,070
I turned on the screen,

2919
01:51:14,070 --> 01:51:16,100
and it displayed
the accumulated weapon dealer prize...

2920
01:51:16,100 --> 01:51:17,940
as 100,000 dollars.

2921
01:51:17,940 --> 01:51:20,410
This is why
I went through all that trouble for.

2922
01:51:20,580 --> 01:51:24,150
That 100,000 dollars prize
explained everything.

2923
01:51:24,180 --> 01:51:25,680
(Vector's current accumulated prize:
0 dollars)

2924
01:51:25,680 --> 01:51:29,980
(Vector's current accumulated prize:
100,000 dollars)

2925
01:51:30,790 --> 01:51:33,090
Why are you declining my request?

2926
01:51:33,990 --> 01:51:35,690
I heard you tried to eliminate us.

2927
01:51:35,790 --> 01:51:36,890
My team?

2928
01:51:36,890 --> 01:51:37,930
Yes.

2929
01:51:37,990 --> 01:51:39,660
Your team is the scariest.

2930
01:51:39,660 --> 01:51:41,730
You always say you won't go to war,

2931
01:51:41,800 --> 01:51:44,470
so why are you trying to
eliminate us, who have nothing?

2932
01:51:44,500 --> 01:51:47,100
We were not trying to eliminate Team Red.

2933
01:51:47,100 --> 01:51:49,170
We wanted to secure three lives.

2934
01:51:49,170 --> 01:51:50,670
That's the same thing.

2935
01:51:50,670 --> 01:51:53,310
We don't need to go for a war
if Team Blue gave us...

2936
01:51:53,310 --> 01:51:54,540
three lives.

2937
01:51:54,540 --> 01:51:57,380
- You said you're planning to take...
- And we...

2938
01:51:57,380 --> 01:51:58,510
- three lives from us.
- It was a threat.

2939
01:51:58,510 --> 01:52:00,110
We never started a war.

2940
01:52:00,110 --> 01:52:01,380
You still...

2941
01:52:01,380 --> 01:52:02,650
- tried to...
- Why would we steal lives from you?

2942
01:52:02,650 --> 01:52:04,190
We're trying to get from them.

2943
01:52:04,190 --> 01:52:06,590
What are you talking about?
You were trying to start a war with us.

2944
01:52:06,590 --> 01:52:07,660
- Why would we...
- What's that?

2945
01:52:07,660 --> 01:52:08,660
We weren't trying to start a war.

2946
01:52:08,660 --> 01:52:09,690
- Team Blue did.
- Team Blue is claiming...

2947
01:52:09,690 --> 01:52:11,030
Team Blue and Team White are allies...

2948
01:52:11,030 --> 01:52:12,790
and they will start a war on us.

2949
01:52:12,830 --> 01:52:15,230
- Put yourself in our shoes.
- Okay.

2950
01:52:15,230 --> 01:52:16,960
Who's the better target
to start a war with?

2951
01:52:16,960 --> 01:52:19,100
So we think it doesn't make any sense.

2952
01:52:19,100 --> 01:52:20,870
It doesn't. If we start a war,
we'll be targeting...

2953
01:52:20,870 --> 01:52:22,670
- Team Blue.
- Why fight a pointless war?

2954
01:52:22,670 --> 01:52:24,210
- Let me tell you something.
- That war is...

2955
01:52:24,210 --> 01:52:26,510
- nonsense.
- So don't participate.

2956
01:52:26,510 --> 01:52:28,640
- Team Red doesn't need to.
- Don't participate.

2957
01:52:32,050 --> 01:52:33,210
- What's going on?
- Why fight a pointless war?

2958
01:52:37,550 --> 01:52:39,490
- What now?
- Let's not do this.

2959
01:52:39,490 --> 01:52:41,860
Are they disagreeing on
forming an alliance?

2960
01:52:41,990 --> 01:52:44,590
- We trust Team Red...
- We declined their request.

2961
01:52:44,590 --> 01:52:46,030
- Is that so? They caught him?
- I came first.

2962
01:52:46,030 --> 01:52:47,130
Yes, they caught him.

2963
01:52:47,130 --> 01:52:48,730
Anyway, there's nothing to lose...

2964
01:52:48,730 --> 01:52:50,530
by just watching today.

2965
01:52:51,100 --> 01:52:52,830
- That's for sure.
- And you have your credits...

2966
01:52:52,830 --> 01:52:55,040
- that you made today.
- One will end up at a loss.

2967
01:52:55,040 --> 01:52:56,500
- You can just wait for that.
- And...

2968
01:52:56,500 --> 01:52:57,940
you might need to give out your resources,

2969
01:52:57,940 --> 01:53:00,040
but it's better to just watch
and secure them.

2970
01:53:00,440 --> 01:53:02,710
They're not earning any lives.

2971
01:53:03,240 --> 01:53:06,680
- But we'll take from them.
- We'll take it away from them.

2972
01:53:06,680 --> 01:53:09,050
- If we eliminate in the future...
- If you take it away, Team Blue...

2973
01:53:09,050 --> 01:53:11,690
will be eliminated
and when they become smaller,

2974
01:53:11,720 --> 01:53:13,420
they won't be able to supply lives
even more.

2975
01:53:13,420 --> 01:53:14,620
- Will they?
- Yes.

2976
01:53:14,620 --> 01:53:15,890
- I don't think there'll be a difference.
- It'll be similar.

2977
01:53:15,890 --> 01:53:16,990
There won't be a huge difference.

2978
01:53:16,990 --> 01:53:19,930
- Our production...
- It'll be similar.

2979
01:53:19,930 --> 01:53:21,760
- We have better efficiency.
- Team Blue will be similar.

2980
01:53:21,760 --> 01:53:23,700
We're far better.

2981
01:53:24,230 --> 01:53:26,600
We can produce far better
if you keep us six alive.

2982
01:53:26,700 --> 01:53:28,470
Are we okay to meet up like this?

2983
01:53:28,670 --> 01:53:30,200
- It's not allowed, right?
- Let's go to the Community Center.

2984
01:53:31,910 --> 01:53:33,410
- Let's talk further.
- But...

2985
01:53:33,440 --> 01:53:35,940
- No, wait.
- Wait. There's no decision made.

2986
01:53:35,940 --> 01:53:37,810
- I'll hear you out.
- Okay.

2987
01:53:37,810 --> 01:53:39,350
- Hear me out.
- Why?

2988
01:53:39,350 --> 01:53:40,780
- First of all...
- Okay.

2989
01:53:41,580 --> 01:53:43,650
- I get why they're so desperate.
- Seriously. Yes.

2990
01:53:44,020 --> 01:53:46,590
Earlier, they were saying
we should attack Team Red.

2991
01:53:46,590 --> 01:53:47,790
My goodness.

2992
01:53:47,890 --> 01:53:50,930
- Team White gets tainted everywhere.
- Exactly.

2993
01:53:52,090 --> 01:53:53,830
You're the whitest person here.

2994
01:53:53,830 --> 01:53:55,630
- What happened?
- Yes, you are.

2995
01:53:55,630 --> 01:53:56,700
What's going on?

2996
01:53:56,700 --> 01:53:58,770
- We're going to meet Team Red.
- Together with Team Red...

2997
01:53:58,770 --> 01:54:01,500
Trying to persuade
Team Red not to fight...

2998
01:54:01,500 --> 01:54:04,440
- and just go with 6 to 3.
- Team White is trying.

2999
01:54:05,310 --> 01:54:08,810
(Maillard arrives at the Center first.)

3000
01:54:14,750 --> 01:54:15,980
Team White is sneaky.

3001
01:54:15,980 --> 01:54:17,050
(Occupied: Please wait.)

3002
01:54:17,120 --> 01:54:18,420
Team Red is here.

3003
01:54:18,720 --> 01:54:20,690
Team Red is here.
They're definitely allied.

3004
01:54:20,690 --> 01:54:21,790
I'm sure.

3005
01:54:21,790 --> 01:54:23,760
Our first goal was...

3006
01:54:23,790 --> 01:54:25,960
- getting three lives without a war.
- We didn't want a war.

3007
01:54:26,090 --> 01:54:29,600
To persuade on getting three lives,

3008
01:54:29,600 --> 01:54:31,970
we were giving examples
on what different things we could do,

3009
01:54:31,970 --> 01:54:34,640
and attacking Team Red was
one of the examples.

3010
01:54:34,640 --> 01:54:36,870
They're trying to convince you
by twisting what we said.

3011
01:54:37,310 --> 01:54:40,010
- So it was hypothetical.
- Yes!

3012
01:54:40,170 --> 01:54:41,480
If we were to start a war,

3013
01:54:41,480 --> 01:54:43,310
we would've had pressed the button.

3014
01:54:43,680 --> 01:54:45,350
Team Black is the worst.

3015
01:54:45,450 --> 01:54:47,820
He is the one who made the war cost zero.

3016
01:54:48,050 --> 01:54:51,220
He released the skills,
so the war cost became zero.

3017
01:54:51,290 --> 01:54:54,460
He's trying to make
the war go on indefinitely.

3018
01:54:55,790 --> 01:54:57,630
- Team White is already inside.
- What?

3019
01:54:58,030 --> 01:54:59,530
- They're inside.
- They are?

3020
01:54:59,530 --> 01:55:01,030
We should've run immediately.

3021
01:55:01,030 --> 01:55:02,060
- To buy the weapons.
- Yes.

3022
01:55:02,060 --> 01:55:03,660
Team White ran for it.

3023
01:55:03,660 --> 01:55:05,300
Of course. We're in a state of war.

3024
01:55:05,300 --> 01:55:06,870
And all they've got is diamonds.

3025
01:55:06,870 --> 01:55:08,000
They definitely ran for it.

3026
01:55:09,170 --> 01:55:11,510
(Team White bought all the weapons
with 200 diamonds.)

3027
01:55:11,940 --> 01:55:13,140
We used up...

3028
01:55:13,140 --> 01:55:14,680
- all the prize.
- Yes.

3029
01:55:14,680 --> 01:55:16,380
- But I'm fine with it.
- Are we the villains?

3030
01:55:16,380 --> 01:55:18,310
- It doesn't matter. They started a war.
- I am...

3031
01:55:18,310 --> 01:55:19,780
originally a person who lives modestly.

3032
01:55:20,150 --> 01:55:22,250
Maillard, what's going on?

3033
01:55:22,250 --> 01:55:23,720
We need to go to a meeting.

3034
01:55:24,150 --> 01:55:27,150
- Everyone must go.
- Everyone must attend.

3035
01:55:27,150 --> 01:55:28,490
Why is he stuck there?

3036
01:55:28,820 --> 01:55:30,890
If they don't secure allies here
and buy weapons,

3037
01:55:30,890 --> 01:55:32,390
they have no way to survive.

3038
01:55:32,830 --> 01:55:34,860
- They're out.
- They came out.

3039
01:55:34,860 --> 01:55:36,700
It's time for Izaha to come.

3040
01:55:36,860 --> 01:55:38,400
You should come here now!

3041
01:55:39,570 --> 01:55:40,740
Izaha!

3042
01:55:41,000 --> 01:55:43,470
- We have money to buy weapons.
- Okay.

3043
01:55:43,470 --> 01:55:45,040
More than the two teams combined...

3044
01:55:45,040 --> 01:55:46,240
(Izaha goes to the Center belatedly.)

3045
01:55:48,340 --> 01:55:49,980
- Where's Izaha?
- He's being held back.

3046
01:55:50,610 --> 01:55:52,250
I tried calling him many times,

3047
01:55:52,250 --> 01:55:54,420
but I guess he's going to finalize
the matter.

3048
01:55:56,720 --> 01:55:58,020
Do we all need to gather?

3049
01:55:58,020 --> 01:55:59,850
- Yes, so we waited.
- Sorry to keep you waiting.

3050
01:55:59,850 --> 01:56:01,020
Come on, Izaha.

3051
01:56:01,860 --> 01:56:02,990
We want...

3052
01:56:03,160 --> 01:56:05,590
to be an ally with Team Red.

3053
01:56:06,530 --> 01:56:10,030
Team Blue and Team Red formed an alliance.

3054
01:56:12,570 --> 01:56:15,300
Two teams will be in a war together.

3055
01:56:16,440 --> 01:56:18,340
If you wish to purchase a weapon,

3056
01:56:18,710 --> 01:56:21,240
please request.

3057
01:56:21,440 --> 01:56:23,510
- We wish to purchase weapons.
- We wish to purchase weapons.

3058
01:56:24,750 --> 01:56:27,350
The remaining weapons are as follows.

3059
01:56:28,150 --> 01:56:32,050
(Weapon cost)

3060
01:56:32,790 --> 01:56:34,490
- They bought them.
- They purchased them.

3061
01:56:34,890 --> 01:56:35,990
They already bought them.

3062
01:56:36,620 --> 01:56:37,760
They're all sold out.

3063
01:56:38,160 --> 01:56:40,260
How could they buy them all?

3064
01:56:40,260 --> 01:56:42,460
Wait, they spent that much?

3065
01:56:42,460 --> 01:56:43,800
- Were they that rich?
- But...

3066
01:56:43,800 --> 01:56:45,200
it's a bit underhanded.

3067
01:56:45,330 --> 01:56:47,070
- I know.
- Right?

3068
01:56:47,870 --> 01:56:50,770
What are they, track athletes?

3069
01:56:51,170 --> 01:56:52,940
How did they get there so fast...

3070
01:56:52,940 --> 01:56:54,910
and buy up all the weapons?

3071
01:56:54,940 --> 01:56:57,380
I thought there'd be at least one left,

3072
01:56:57,380 --> 01:56:59,410
but they took them all.

3073
01:56:59,410 --> 01:57:02,650
But I can't really get a sense
of how powerful the weapons are.

3074
01:57:02,720 --> 01:57:04,320
They were all sold out.

3075
01:57:04,350 --> 01:57:05,820
They're so ruthless.

3076
01:57:05,890 --> 01:57:07,220
They say they want peace,

3077
01:57:07,820 --> 01:57:09,490
but how much did they spend on weapons?

3078
01:57:10,260 --> 01:57:12,330
I had no intention of purchasing weapons.

3079
01:57:12,430 --> 01:57:15,030
I was skeptical.

3080
01:57:15,130 --> 01:57:17,160
The prize money gets deducted, right?

3081
01:57:17,160 --> 01:57:19,170
We're all here...

3082
01:57:19,170 --> 01:57:21,070
to win the prize money.

3083
01:57:21,070 --> 01:57:23,470
Rather than all of us
having our prize cut,

3084
01:57:23,570 --> 01:57:24,940
let's just agree not to buy weapons...

3085
01:57:24,940 --> 01:57:26,440
before the war even starts.

3086
01:57:26,440 --> 01:57:28,810
We should have at least said,

3087
01:57:28,810 --> 01:57:30,850
"Let's not cut the total cost."

3088
01:57:30,980 --> 01:57:32,380
I regret...

3089
01:57:32,510 --> 01:57:33,850
not being able to stop it until the end.

3090
01:57:33,850 --> 01:57:35,050
(Pitou, Actress)

3091
01:57:37,690 --> 01:57:41,520
(Battlefield)

3092
01:57:45,390 --> 01:57:46,560
Eliminate them all. Are you confident?

3093
01:57:46,560 --> 01:57:47,660
- Let's go.
- Yes.

3094
01:57:47,660 --> 01:57:48,730
Eliminate them all.

3095
01:57:49,030 --> 01:57:50,870
- I'm scared.
- It's scarier at night.

3096
01:57:50,870 --> 01:57:52,470
- My gosh.
- What's all this?

3097
01:57:52,470 --> 01:57:53,770
There's a strange building.

3098
01:57:54,140 --> 01:57:55,270
It's grand.

3099
01:57:55,270 --> 01:57:56,370
(The battlefield looks very different
from the Community Town.)

3100
01:57:56,370 --> 01:57:59,640
It's so eerie it actually feels...

3101
01:57:59,640 --> 01:58:01,480
like we're at war.

3102
01:58:01,480 --> 01:58:03,180
The abandoned building...

3103
01:58:03,480 --> 01:58:05,480
made it feel a bit overwhelming.

3104
01:58:05,950 --> 01:58:08,680
I don't know why, but I was fired up too.

3105
01:58:08,680 --> 01:58:10,180
- My gosh.
- What's going on?

3106
01:58:11,720 --> 01:58:12,850
- What's this place?
- No!

3107
01:58:12,850 --> 01:58:13,920
- What is it?
- Why?

3108
01:58:13,920 --> 01:58:14,990
(Entering the battlefield)

3109
01:58:15,360 --> 01:58:16,490
- What's this?
- It's amazing.

3110
01:58:16,860 --> 01:58:17,890
It's cool.

3111
01:58:21,830 --> 01:58:22,930
The atmosphere there...

3112
01:58:22,930 --> 01:58:24,670
was immersive.

3113
01:58:24,670 --> 01:58:26,000
It looked like an old cathedral...

3114
01:58:26,000 --> 01:58:28,070
or a church with stained glass.

3115
01:58:28,070 --> 01:58:31,770
Something is about to happen here.

3116
01:58:32,040 --> 01:58:33,640
Things have already turned out this way,

3117
01:58:33,640 --> 01:58:34,810
so if we want to thin the numbers...

3118
01:58:34,810 --> 01:58:38,680
and coexist with whoever's left,

3119
01:58:38,750 --> 01:58:41,580
we have to win this game, no matter what.

3120
01:58:42,680 --> 01:58:44,350
Are you okay with scary stuff?

3121
01:58:44,420 --> 01:58:47,390
There's nothing scarier than losing lives.

3122
01:58:47,390 --> 01:58:48,990
Why are these people all so cool?

3123
01:58:48,990 --> 01:58:50,160
Let's go.

3124
01:58:50,420 --> 01:58:52,230
Honestly, I didn't think of losing.

3125
01:58:52,290 --> 01:58:54,360
Today, I'll teach them a lesson.

3126
01:58:54,400 --> 01:58:55,700
I'll crush them.

3127
01:58:56,430 --> 01:58:58,370
We just win. No matter what.

3128
01:58:58,370 --> 01:59:00,030
We're stuck
between a rock and a hard place.

3129
01:59:00,570 --> 01:59:02,400
If we lose here, we're done.

3130
01:59:02,400 --> 01:59:04,140
We got all the weapons ready.

3131
01:59:04,440 --> 01:59:05,870
Now it's the final showdown.

3132
01:59:05,910 --> 01:59:08,080
Let's give it everything we've got
and survive.

3133
01:59:11,180 --> 01:59:14,350
Residents, welcome to the battlefield.

3134
01:59:14,980 --> 01:59:16,280
Today's battle is...

3135
01:59:18,720 --> 01:59:20,320
the Proposition Race.

3136
01:59:21,090 --> 01:59:22,620
- Proposition Race?
- Proposition Race?

3137
01:59:22,760 --> 01:59:25,260
The Proposition Race is a game
where players find cards...

3138
01:59:25,260 --> 01:59:27,560
with various words
within the time limit...

3139
01:59:27,930 --> 01:59:30,300
and use them to create true propositions.

3140
01:59:30,930 --> 01:59:33,730
The Proposition Race consists of...

3141
01:59:33,730 --> 01:59:37,170
a 45-minute 1st half
followed by a 45-minute 2nd half.

3142
01:59:37,670 --> 01:59:41,110
During each round, residents must search
the underground area...

3143
01:59:41,280 --> 01:59:44,410
and secure the cards they need
to make propositions.

3144
01:59:44,880 --> 01:59:47,620
However,
no items other than proposition cards...

3145
01:59:47,620 --> 01:59:50,480
may be taken out of the underground area.

3146
01:59:50,750 --> 01:59:53,220
Proposition cards consist of
country-name cards,

3147
01:59:53,220 --> 01:59:55,120
comparison-value keyword cards,

3148
01:59:55,520 --> 01:59:58,360
adjective cards with predicates,

3149
01:59:58,760 --> 02:00:03,730
and particle cards containing
"is," "are", "than,"

3150
02:00:03,730 --> 02:00:05,930
and other grammatical particles.

3151
02:00:06,100 --> 02:00:08,670
The location of each card is fixed.

3152
02:00:08,670 --> 02:00:10,640
It's not possible to resubmit...

3153
02:00:10,640 --> 02:00:13,240
the same proposition
by changing the positions of the cards.

3154
02:00:13,970 --> 02:00:17,140
However, propositions using
different predicates will be recognized...

3155
02:00:17,180 --> 02:00:19,150
as separate correct answers,

3156
02:00:19,150 --> 02:00:21,320
even if they deal with the same fact.

3157
02:00:21,780 --> 02:00:24,150
- Find the diamonds.
- We need lots of particle cards.

3158
02:00:24,150 --> 02:00:25,290
Let's get as many particle
and comparison-value keyword cards...

3159
02:00:25,290 --> 02:00:26,320
as possible.

3160
02:00:26,320 --> 02:00:28,020
Don't we just have to sweep them all?

3161
02:00:29,160 --> 02:00:30,660
Once a proposition is complete,

3162
02:00:30,660 --> 02:00:33,760
each team can enter
its proposition submission booth...

3163
02:00:33,760 --> 02:00:35,730
and submit it.

3164
02:00:36,000 --> 02:00:39,230
A correct proposition earns one point,

3165
02:00:39,500 --> 02:00:42,540
while an incorrect proposition
loses two points.

3166
02:00:42,670 --> 02:00:44,670
Duplicate propositions...

3167
02:00:44,670 --> 02:00:46,740
do not earn any points.

3168
02:00:46,740 --> 02:00:50,540
All points are tallied
and revealed only once...

3169
02:00:50,540 --> 02:00:52,310
at the end of each half.

3170
02:00:52,550 --> 02:00:54,720
Whether a submitted proposition
is correct...

3171
02:00:54,720 --> 02:00:57,050
is not revealed at the time of submission.

3172
02:00:57,320 --> 02:00:58,420
Making the right guesses is crucial.

3173
02:00:58,420 --> 02:01:00,150
You lose points for incorrect answers.

3174
02:01:00,490 --> 02:01:04,060
All submitted proposition cards are
discarded regardless of whether...

3175
02:01:04,060 --> 02:01:05,560
they are correct,

3176
02:01:05,990 --> 02:01:09,360
while proposition cards that have
not yet been submitted during...

3177
02:01:09,700 --> 02:01:11,730
the 1st half can be used in the 2nd half.

3178
02:01:11,930 --> 02:01:13,800
In addition,

3179
02:01:13,800 --> 02:01:17,070
a maximum of two members from each team
may enter the underground area at a time.

3180
02:01:17,070 --> 02:01:20,340
Members may be freely replaced.

3181
02:01:20,570 --> 02:01:23,340
However, cards being physically carried
by a member...

3182
02:01:23,340 --> 02:01:25,050
cannot be taken from them.

3183
02:01:25,410 --> 02:01:27,920
Each weapon can be used only once...

3184
02:01:27,920 --> 02:01:29,720
throughout both halves.

3185
02:01:29,720 --> 02:01:33,690
To use a weapon, ring the bell
inside the proposition submission booth.

3186
02:01:33,690 --> 02:01:35,120
(Weapon used)

3187
02:01:35,120 --> 02:01:36,520
We need time to combine the cards.

3188
02:01:36,520 --> 02:01:38,930
Once you gather enough cards,
come up with them.

3189
02:01:38,930 --> 02:01:40,830
- Let's spread them out and work on them.
- Then...

3190
02:01:40,830 --> 02:01:42,360
One from each team should...

3191
02:01:42,360 --> 02:01:44,770
- come up, switch, come up, and switch.
- Okay.

3192
02:01:44,770 --> 02:01:46,670
- Okay.
- I'll go downstairs.

3193
02:01:46,770 --> 02:01:47,800
I'll go.

3194
02:01:47,800 --> 02:01:49,700
- It'll come down to stamina.
- Right.

3195
02:01:49,700 --> 02:01:51,770
- Okay.
- I took a look,

3196
02:01:51,770 --> 02:01:54,910
and I needed to go from my team.

3197
02:01:54,910 --> 02:01:57,510
The other guys are quite old,

3198
02:01:57,510 --> 02:02:00,250
and the ladies are delicate.

3199
02:02:00,250 --> 02:02:01,620
I have to do the search.

3200
02:02:01,620 --> 02:02:03,650
I was fine with running.

3201
02:02:03,650 --> 02:02:06,250
All I needed to do was
bring the cards upstairs.

3202
02:02:06,250 --> 02:02:10,090
Genie and Pitou looked tired...

3203
02:02:10,090 --> 02:02:12,560
whenever we took the stairs.

3204
02:02:12,560 --> 02:02:15,630
So I decided to do the running.

3205
02:02:15,630 --> 02:02:19,000
In the first half, we must secure
as many cards as possible.

3206
02:02:19,000 --> 02:02:20,200
- Look.
- Sweep them all.

3207
02:02:20,200 --> 02:02:21,270
- We'll bring them all.
- Okay.

3208
02:02:21,270 --> 02:02:23,600
But here's the problem.
You must go through the cards quickly...

3209
02:02:23,600 --> 02:02:24,940
and tell us what we're short of.

3210
02:02:24,940 --> 02:02:26,810
- Okay.
- Then we'll look for those.

3211
02:02:26,810 --> 02:02:28,280
Say that things turn out for the worst,

3212
02:02:28,280 --> 02:02:29,280
and I get exhausted.

3213
02:02:29,280 --> 02:02:31,110
- You must get ready to run.
- Of course.

3214
02:02:31,110 --> 02:02:32,810
I'll be all set to run again
after a break,

3215
02:02:32,810 --> 02:02:33,980
- so I'll switch right away.
- Okay.

3216
02:02:33,980 --> 02:02:36,420
But in return,
those who replace us shouldn't think,

3217
02:02:36,420 --> 02:02:38,820
"I'd better work hard and find
as many as possible."

3218
02:02:38,820 --> 02:02:40,750
Move out once we seem better than before.

3219
02:02:40,750 --> 02:02:42,520
- Okay. We'll sub you just for the break.
- Okay.

3220
02:02:42,520 --> 02:02:43,990
Get greedy, and it'll get messy.

3221
02:02:43,990 --> 02:02:45,130
- We'll fail at communicating.
- Correct.

3222
02:02:45,130 --> 02:02:46,990
- How far...
- We only need about 30 seconds...

3223
02:02:46,990 --> 02:02:48,300
- to one minute of rest.
- Got it.

3224
02:02:48,300 --> 02:02:49,930
We must crush them with our stamina.

3225
02:02:50,260 --> 02:02:52,300
You two are very important.

3226
02:02:52,300 --> 02:02:53,400
(Team White's search team is
Boss and Paul.)

3227
02:02:53,570 --> 02:02:56,470
- How complicated.
- That team will switch a lot.

3228
02:02:56,470 --> 02:02:59,140
- Right, the stamina.
- But that's not good.

3229
02:02:59,310 --> 02:03:00,540
It's not good at all.

3230
02:03:00,540 --> 02:03:03,310
We should each be in charge of
that particular role.

3231
02:03:03,510 --> 02:03:06,180
Those who are smart, use your brains.

3232
02:03:06,180 --> 02:03:08,350
Those who are athletic, run.

3233
02:03:08,780 --> 02:03:09,850
Let's do this!

3234
02:03:09,850 --> 02:03:11,220
