02:12:26,570 --> 02:12:29,040
I just need a postposition.

3484
02:12:29,040 --> 02:12:30,980
We definitely need a lot more particles.

3485
02:12:30,980 --> 02:12:33,050
Yes. We have to look for those.

3486
02:12:33,050 --> 02:12:34,180
Smaller cards.

3487
02:12:35,420 --> 02:12:36,420
Hey.

3488
02:12:37,250 --> 02:12:38,520
Could you look for particles?

3489
02:12:38,520 --> 02:12:39,520
- I'm sure I can find some.
- Particles.

3490
02:12:39,520 --> 02:12:40,720
- We got it.
- There's some.

3491
02:12:40,720 --> 02:12:42,390
- Bring back more.
- Should we try that?

3492
02:12:42,390 --> 02:12:44,890
(Salt runs out again
after giving them more particles.)

3493
02:12:48,190 --> 02:12:50,330
Darn it. I'm tired.

3494
02:12:50,900 --> 02:12:52,400
- We can do this.
- We got this.

3495
02:12:58,970 --> 02:12:59,970
I'm so tired.

3496
02:13:01,710 --> 02:13:04,310
Come on. I can't find anything now.

3497
02:13:04,440 --> 02:13:06,480
- We can't. We found everything.
- Now...

3498
02:13:06,980 --> 02:13:08,380
There are no more cards left now.

3499
02:13:09,420 --> 02:13:10,550
I keep looking, but there's none left.

3500
02:13:12,720 --> 02:13:13,920
None means none.

3501
02:13:14,690 --> 02:13:15,690
(1 proposition card)

3502
02:13:16,060 --> 02:13:17,690
Darn it. I don't know how to crack this.

3503
02:13:18,120 --> 02:13:20,360
(Boss is feeling small
when it comes to a quiz box.)

3504
02:13:20,790 --> 02:13:21,800
Paul.

3505
02:13:23,430 --> 02:13:25,000
- Paul.
- Yes?

3506
02:13:25,630 --> 02:13:27,100
Could you crack this for me?

3507
02:13:28,940 --> 02:13:30,070
Crack it for me. I don't know.

3508
02:13:33,440 --> 02:13:35,940
(In what year
did the Berlin Wall come down?)

3509
02:13:36,210 --> 02:13:37,210
I can't crack it either.

3510
02:13:37,410 --> 02:13:38,410
Good luck.

3511
02:13:38,410 --> 02:13:41,380
Actually, I thought
Boss and I had a better strategy...

3512
02:13:41,380 --> 02:13:43,650
and were better equipped physically...

3513
02:13:43,650 --> 02:13:46,150
to find the cards than Teams Blue and Red.

3514
02:13:46,150 --> 02:13:49,260
But when we found
a lot of boxes with locks,

3515
02:13:49,260 --> 02:13:51,290
it was difficult for us
to crack the codes.

3516
02:13:51,290 --> 02:13:55,300
We decided to hide all the boxes
until we got someone on our team...

3517
02:13:55,300 --> 02:13:57,300
who could solve these questions.

3518
02:13:57,730 --> 02:13:58,770
Okay.

3519
02:13:58,770 --> 02:14:00,630
(Paul and Boss hid them
all in the same spot.)

3520
02:14:00,630 --> 02:14:02,500
Paul. I'll go and check in.
Give them to me.

3521
02:14:02,500 --> 02:14:03,970
- Okay. Run.
- Yes.

3522
02:14:03,970 --> 02:14:04,970
Okay.

3523
02:14:05,540 --> 02:14:07,540
I thought we had great teamwork.

3524
02:14:07,540 --> 02:14:10,710
We kept calling each other's name
and checked on each other.

3525
02:14:10,710 --> 02:14:13,080
When people get tired,
they easily lose their focus.

3526
02:14:13,080 --> 02:14:15,550
But since she was in the special forces,

3527
02:14:15,550 --> 02:14:18,690
she was clearly great at running.
She was also fast.

3528
02:14:19,850 --> 02:14:20,850
Leia.

3529
02:14:21,450 --> 02:14:22,960
- When you go in,
- Yes.

3530
02:14:22,960 --> 02:14:24,590
- there's a room on the left.
- Yes.

3531
02:14:24,590 --> 02:14:26,560
We can't open those boxes.

3532
02:14:26,560 --> 02:14:27,560
So you have to go.

3533
02:14:27,560 --> 02:14:29,460
- We have to crack the codes?
- Yes.

3534
02:14:29,960 --> 02:14:30,960
Go and turn left.

3535
02:14:30,960 --> 02:14:32,170
(Dispatching Leia to solve the quiz boxes)

3536
02:14:32,170 --> 02:14:33,370
Go and turn left?

3537
02:14:35,700 --> 02:14:37,070
- Paul.
- Yes.

3538
02:14:37,640 --> 02:14:38,970
- Come here.
- Okay.

3539
02:14:39,870 --> 02:14:41,310
Look. This is what we have.

3540
02:14:41,510 --> 02:14:42,610
Next...

3541
02:14:42,610 --> 02:14:43,610
(Uncovering a pile of boxes)

3542
02:14:43,610 --> 02:14:44,910
- The question mark...
- Okay.

3543
02:14:44,910 --> 02:14:46,550
- I must solve them to take the cards?
- Yes. Stay here.

3544
02:14:46,550 --> 02:14:48,380
- I'll bring everything here.
- Okay.

3545
02:14:49,150 --> 02:14:51,850
We're running out of words and predicates.

3546
02:14:51,850 --> 02:14:53,190
It'd be nice to find more predicates.

3547
02:14:53,190 --> 02:14:55,160
- They might be in the box.
- Okay.

3548
02:14:55,160 --> 02:14:57,020
- I got most of them here.
- Okay.

3549
02:14:57,220 --> 02:15:01,630
Paul had stacked up 3 to 4 boxes.
No, there were 4 to 5 boxes stacked up.

3550
02:15:01,630 --> 02:15:02,760
He wanted me to solve the quizzes.

3551
02:15:02,760 --> 02:15:07,830
Our life was on the line by then.

3552
02:15:07,830 --> 02:15:09,670
I felt a great sense of responsibility.

3553
02:15:11,240 --> 02:15:12,370
(In what year
did the Berlin Wall come down?)

3554
02:15:12,370 --> 02:15:15,240
(The box is open.)

3555
02:15:15,380 --> 02:15:17,680
(In what year did World War I break out?)

3556
02:15:17,680 --> 02:15:20,050
(The box is open.)

3557
02:15:21,050 --> 02:15:23,450
No more. Wait. No. That's not it.

3558
02:15:25,050 --> 02:15:26,050
Over there.

3559
02:15:28,050 --> 02:15:29,060
I got it.

3560
02:15:31,390 --> 02:15:33,360
Where? There's one here too.

3561
02:15:35,930 --> 02:15:39,400
(She finds a proposition card
in the moss-filled water.)

3562
02:15:50,940 --> 02:15:52,980
- Great.
- I'll get back out there.

3563
02:15:52,980 --> 02:15:54,080
- I'm fine.
- Get some rest.

3564
02:15:54,080 --> 02:15:56,420
- It's okay.
- We need to find smaller cards.

3565
02:15:56,720 --> 02:15:57,780
- I...
- Are you all right?

3566
02:15:57,780 --> 02:15:59,620
- I searched everywhere.
- Yes.

3567
02:15:59,620 --> 02:16:00,620
My gosh.

3568
02:16:00,620 --> 02:16:03,220
(Salt has been running around
without switching with anyone.)

3569
02:16:04,720 --> 02:16:08,760
They didn't touch the cards in the water.

3570
02:16:08,760 --> 02:16:10,430
So I dipped my hand in
and found some cards.

3571
02:16:10,830 --> 02:16:11,830
I got those places.

3572
02:16:13,100 --> 02:16:16,600
(Maillard switched with Donkey earlier.)

3573
02:16:24,080 --> 02:16:25,650
Why are there so many keys here?

3574
02:16:26,410 --> 02:16:28,550
I'm going to get to them.
I'm just keeping them here.

3575
02:16:28,550 --> 02:16:30,720
- You can't do that.
- No. I'm getting to them.

3576
02:16:30,720 --> 02:16:33,120
You have to solve them one at a time.
You can't hog all the boxes.

3577
02:16:33,120 --> 02:16:34,820
- That makes no sense.
- Fine. Go ahead.

3578
02:16:36,820 --> 02:16:38,160
- Donkey.
- Yes?

3579
02:16:38,830 --> 02:16:40,290
Did you see the phone number
for Camellia Snack Bar?

3580
02:16:40,290 --> 02:16:41,290
Yes, I did.

3581
02:16:41,760 --> 02:16:42,760
This way.

3582
02:16:44,800 --> 02:16:45,970
Is it here?

3583
02:16:45,970 --> 02:16:47,130
There it is.

3584
02:16:47,570 --> 02:16:48,570
It's 1311.

3585
02:16:49,140 --> 02:16:50,140
It's 1311.

3586
02:16:50,140 --> 02:16:53,440
(They find a clue for the lock
from a thrown-out flyer.)

3587
02:16:53,440 --> 02:16:54,970
- Nice.
- My gosh.

3588
02:16:55,540 --> 02:16:57,940
There's only one card inside the box.
Darn it.

3589
02:17:00,280 --> 02:17:01,810
I should take them.

3590
02:17:01,810 --> 02:17:04,350
(Leia opened all the boxes she could.)

3591
02:17:05,650 --> 02:17:07,290
- That's...
- Paul, do you have more cards for me?

3592
02:17:07,290 --> 02:17:08,490
No. Give them to me.

3593
02:17:08,490 --> 02:17:10,490
- Give them to me.
- I solved all the quizzes over there.

3594
02:17:10,490 --> 02:17:12,130
Okay. Give them to me.

3595
02:17:12,130 --> 02:17:13,490
Okay. I'll take them with me.

3596
02:17:13,490 --> 02:17:15,500
I have to put together sentences.
Then I'll switch out.

3597
02:17:19,600 --> 02:17:20,670
Gosh, what could this be?

3598
02:17:21,500 --> 02:17:23,500
(There are locked boxes
she wasn't able to solve.)

3599
02:17:23,500 --> 02:17:24,500
Wait.

3600
02:17:26,040 --> 02:17:27,040
I know the answer.

3601
02:17:27,310 --> 02:17:29,610
"Wait. The phone number
of a Chinese restaurant?"

3602
02:17:29,610 --> 02:17:30,880
"How do I know that number?"

3603
02:17:31,010 --> 02:17:34,650
I thought about it
and remembered the sticker on the wall.

3604
02:17:34,650 --> 02:17:35,850
I ran out and checked.

3605
02:17:35,850 --> 02:17:37,380
It did say Golden Chinese Restaurant.

3606
02:17:38,220 --> 02:17:40,150
I went back in
and cracked it open right away.

3607
02:17:40,790 --> 02:17:43,390
My gosh. You're a genius.

3608
02:17:43,860 --> 02:17:45,360
- I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

3609
02:17:46,390 --> 02:17:47,760
"What number goes in the question mark?"

3610
02:17:47,960 --> 02:17:51,030
(What number goes in the question mark?)

3611
02:17:51,030 --> 02:17:53,030
Okay.

3612
02:17:53,030 --> 02:17:54,370
Five, nine...

3613
02:17:54,370 --> 02:17:55,470
Try 9839.

3614
02:17:55,470 --> 02:17:56,970
Try 9839.

3615
02:17:56,970 --> 02:17:59,670
There was an addition
of four-digit numbers.

3616
02:17:59,670 --> 02:18:02,180
When you overlap the numbers,
you get the answer.

3617
02:18:02,180 --> 02:18:04,710
I like going to escape rooms.

3618
02:18:04,710 --> 02:18:05,780
So I've done many quizzes like that.

3619
02:18:05,780 --> 02:18:08,480
We should have brought in Hamlet.

3620
02:18:08,480 --> 02:18:11,580
But we didn't have enough time
to stop and think about strategies.

3621
02:18:11,850 --> 02:18:14,690
(Hamlet is in charge of
arranging the cards efficiently.)

3622
02:18:15,190 --> 02:18:17,390
We have time.
Can you check if this makes sense?

3623
02:18:17,390 --> 02:18:18,490
This one.

3624
02:18:18,490 --> 02:18:20,160
Yes, Korea beat Japan.

3625
02:18:20,160 --> 02:18:21,230
- Right?
- Yes.

3626
02:18:23,100 --> 02:18:25,770
Our GDP went up.

3627
02:18:26,430 --> 02:18:27,670
Here's our submission.

3628
02:18:28,400 --> 02:18:31,540
"Greece has a lower GDP than Korea."

3629
02:18:32,070 --> 02:18:33,940
- Without the cards...
- Right.

3630
02:18:33,940 --> 02:18:35,110
- He's back.
- Gosh.

3631
02:18:35,110 --> 02:18:36,540
- I couldn't find any particles.
- None?

3632
02:18:36,540 --> 02:18:38,810
- There aren't any left.
- Oh, no. What do we do?

3633
02:18:38,810 --> 02:18:39,950
- But...
- Should I go and check?

3634
02:18:39,950 --> 02:18:42,250
- No. I'll go back.
- Okay. Are you okay?

3635
02:18:42,250 --> 02:18:44,350
- This is bad. I'm nervous.
- Oh, no.

3636
02:18:44,350 --> 02:18:45,650
They have a lot of black cards.

3637
02:18:45,890 --> 02:18:47,690
- They have so many black cards.
- The black cards are...

3638
02:18:47,690 --> 02:18:49,760
- the key.
- We can say the usage rate is lower.

3639
02:18:49,760 --> 02:18:51,420
- Right? We did one with Korea.
- Should we try that?

3640
02:18:51,560 --> 02:18:53,360
Right. Australia recently banned minors...

3641
02:18:53,360 --> 02:18:54,860
- from using social media.
- Right.

3642
02:18:54,860 --> 02:18:55,960
- That's true.
- Let's make one.

3643
02:18:55,960 --> 02:18:56,960
Japan...

3644
02:18:57,260 --> 02:18:58,800
- It's lower, right?
- Yes.

3645
02:18:58,800 --> 02:18:59,930
The Internet usage rate...

3646
02:19:00,130 --> 02:19:02,400
"Australia has
a lower Internet usage rate than Japan."

3647
02:19:02,400 --> 02:19:03,440
Here's our submission.

3648
02:19:03,440 --> 02:19:04,970
(2 points deducted, Australia:
Ranked 4th, Japan: Ranked 14th)

3649
02:19:05,070 --> 02:19:06,970
The second half will get super intense.

3650
02:19:07,440 --> 02:19:08,740
Do you think Korea has...

3651
02:19:08,740 --> 02:19:10,210
a lower World Happiness Index
than the Netherlands?

3652
02:19:10,210 --> 02:19:11,280
- It has to be lower.
- It would be, wouldn't it?

3653
02:19:11,280 --> 02:19:12,810
Are people in the Netherlands depressed?

3654
02:19:12,950 --> 02:19:15,450
- People are free-spirited there.
- We shouldn't submit...

3655
02:19:15,450 --> 02:19:16,780
uncertain ones in the first half.

3656
02:19:16,780 --> 02:19:19,290
Cannabis is legalized in the Netherlands.
Wouldn't they be happy?

3657
02:19:19,290 --> 02:19:20,320
They must be. Right.

3658
02:19:21,520 --> 02:19:23,790
- I think the index will be higher there.
- I think so.

3659
02:19:23,790 --> 02:19:26,090
Let's complete it, but we won't submit it.

3660
02:19:27,330 --> 02:19:33,300
(First Half)

3661
02:19:34,000 --> 02:19:35,300
- It's over.
- The first half...

3662
02:19:35,300 --> 02:19:37,300
of the Proposition Race is over.

3663
02:19:37,970 --> 02:19:40,670
You can't touch the proposition cards now.

3664
02:19:41,410 --> 02:19:43,710
- You can't submit propositions either.
- We can't touch them.

3665
02:19:44,510 --> 02:19:46,650
- Residents in the basement,
- Ten, twelve, thirteen...

3666
02:19:46,650 --> 02:19:48,380
- please come back upstairs.
- We should have about 16 points.

3667
02:19:48,380 --> 02:19:49,380
- So...
- That's...

3668
02:19:49,380 --> 02:19:51,320
It's over? Okay.

3669
02:19:52,450 --> 02:19:53,490
I got it.

3670
02:19:54,990 --> 02:19:57,490
- Gosh, I'm exhausted.
- Get some rest.

3671
02:19:57,490 --> 02:19:59,860
If we got everything right,
we should have 12 points.

3672
02:19:59,860 --> 02:20:02,130
They used the weapon earlier
and earned three points.

3673
02:20:02,830 --> 02:20:04,660
Their score is probably higher.

3674
02:20:05,530 --> 02:20:08,600
Here are your current scores so far.

3675
02:20:09,200 --> 02:20:10,840
Let's go. Please.

3676
02:20:12,040 --> 02:20:13,140
Team White.

3677
02:20:13,140 --> 02:20:16,010
(Mid-Game Scores: Blue, White)

3678
02:20:16,010 --> 02:20:17,680
- Fourteen points.
- What?

3679
02:20:17,680 --> 02:20:19,050
- One of them was wrong.
- We got one wrong.

3680
02:20:19,050 --> 02:20:21,210
The one we didn't submit must be correct,
and we got one wrong.

3681
02:20:21,950 --> 02:20:22,980
Team Blue.

3682
02:20:22,980 --> 02:20:24,180
(White: 14)

3683
02:20:24,180 --> 02:20:25,690
- Nine points.
- What?

3684
02:20:26,250 --> 02:20:27,350
- It's okay.
- So...

3685
02:20:27,350 --> 02:20:28,620
- did we get a few wrong?
- It's okay.

3686
02:20:28,620 --> 02:20:30,220
We both got one wrong.

3687
02:20:30,220 --> 02:20:31,660
(Japan has a lower
World Press Freedom Index than the US.)

3688
02:20:32,390 --> 02:20:34,260
I need to tell Izaha to get a grip.

3689
02:20:34,260 --> 02:20:36,160
Not submitting false propositions
is the most important.

3690
02:20:36,160 --> 02:20:38,330
One false proposition
would put us three points under.

3691
02:20:38,560 --> 02:20:40,500
We lose two points
for each false proposition.

3692
02:20:40,700 --> 02:20:42,970
When they score 1 point
and we lose 2 points, the difference is 3.

3693
02:20:42,970 --> 02:20:44,400
He needs to know that.

3694
02:20:44,570 --> 02:20:47,040
I think everyone is rushing
to submit the propositions.

3695
02:20:47,040 --> 02:20:49,110
I believe
reviewing the propositions thoroughly...

3696
02:20:49,310 --> 02:20:51,310
and not submitting any false propositions
is the most important.

3697
02:20:51,380 --> 02:20:54,880
They're five points ahead
with Class A Weapon.

3698
02:20:54,880 --> 02:20:57,880
We can't submit
any false propositions now.

3699
02:20:57,880 --> 02:21:00,090
We need to submit
a lot more propositions...

3700
02:21:00,090 --> 02:21:02,060
to make up for this difference.

3701
02:21:02,060 --> 02:21:04,020
Buying the weapon was the right call.

3702
02:21:04,490 --> 02:21:06,090
We can stay ahead with the weapon.

3703
02:21:06,090 --> 02:21:08,260
They will be under more pressure
in the second half.

3704
02:21:10,360 --> 02:21:12,530
The second half will begin shortly,

3705
02:21:12,530 --> 02:21:14,170
and your tables will be switched.

3706
02:21:14,530 --> 02:21:15,740
Isn't it better to search tight spaces...

3707
02:21:15,740 --> 02:21:17,100
- than large spaces?
- That's better.

3708
02:21:17,100 --> 02:21:18,970
Then I'll start from the front
on the left side.

3709
02:21:18,970 --> 02:21:20,910
You can move forward
from the back on the right side.

3710
02:21:20,910 --> 02:21:22,140
- Okay.
- Let's do that.

3711
02:21:22,140 --> 02:21:24,010
- Let's start from opposite ends.
- Yes. Okay.

3712
02:21:24,010 --> 02:21:25,280
What do you need the most?

3713
02:21:25,280 --> 02:21:26,410
All of the black cards are important.

3714
02:21:26,410 --> 02:21:28,980
- Pick up all the black ones you can find.
- Black ones...

3715
02:21:29,250 --> 02:21:31,020
Let's not come upstairs unless we have to.

3716
02:21:31,220 --> 02:21:32,720
It's better not to stay there
as long as we can.

3717
02:21:32,720 --> 02:21:34,520
They took their time before coming up.

3718
02:21:34,520 --> 02:21:36,260
So they found a lot more cards.

3719
02:21:37,920 --> 02:21:39,730
Let's find ways to keep
as many cards as we can on us.

3720
02:21:39,730 --> 02:21:41,230
We should come up
only we can't hold anymore.

3721
02:21:43,630 --> 02:21:45,570
The second half...

3722
02:21:46,300 --> 02:21:48,500
of the Proposition Race begins now.

3723
02:21:51,400 --> 02:21:52,410
Let's go.

3724
02:21:53,140 --> 02:21:55,780
- You got this!
- Let's go!

3725
02:21:56,240 --> 02:21:57,440
My gosh. They're so fast.

3726
02:21:59,450 --> 02:22:02,950
(The speed difference between
the two teams is starting to show.)

3727
02:22:05,590 --> 02:22:06,620
Darn it.

3728
02:22:06,950 --> 02:22:08,120
Let's kill them all.

3729
02:22:11,790 --> 02:22:14,930
