3972
02:34:06,340 --> 02:34:08,140
Great work.

3973
02:34:08,440 --> 02:34:09,540
Well done.

3974
02:34:09,610 --> 02:34:12,310
- Yes!
- Great job.

3975
02:34:18,520 --> 02:34:21,190
(First Half)

3976
02:34:21,190 --> 02:34:23,160
(Blue: 9, White: 14, Class A Weapon)

3977
02:34:23,320 --> 02:34:25,160
(Second Half)

3978
02:34:25,160 --> 02:34:27,390
(Blue: 11, White: 18,
Class B and C Weapon)

3979
02:34:27,560 --> 02:34:28,660
(1st Half, Blue: 9, White: 14)

3980
02:34:28,660 --> 02:34:29,730
(2nd Half, Blue: 11, White: 18)

3981
02:34:29,730 --> 02:34:31,730
(Total Scores, Blue: 20, White: 32)

3982
02:34:32,030 --> 02:34:34,970
Yes. I knew it.
Our team won by a landslide.

3983
02:34:34,970 --> 02:34:36,400
Gosh, give us your lives.

3984
02:34:36,400 --> 02:34:38,970
This is insane.
See? Look at this, you jerks.

3985
02:34:39,170 --> 02:34:42,410
We would've crushed you
even without the hints.

3986
02:34:42,540 --> 02:34:44,710
You wouldn't have lost your lives
had you done nothing.

3987
02:34:44,880 --> 02:34:47,850
I felt the highest degree of joy.

3988
02:34:48,250 --> 02:34:51,350
I thought the only thing we had left
was to enjoy our victory.

3989
02:34:51,750 --> 02:34:53,620
The winning team of the war will take...

3990
02:34:53,620 --> 02:34:55,750
half of
the losing team's entire resources...

3991
02:34:55,920 --> 02:34:58,560
- as spoils of war.
- Thank you.

3992
02:34:58,990 --> 02:35:00,690
If the resources are an odd number,

3993
02:35:00,690 --> 02:35:03,530
decimal values will be rounded up.

3994
02:35:03,530 --> 02:35:04,630
- Great.
- That's great.

3995
02:35:04,630 --> 02:35:06,570
- They'll round it up?
- That's nice.

3996
02:35:06,570 --> 02:35:07,770
They'll round it up, not round it down.

3997
02:35:07,770 --> 02:35:09,300
- Nice.
- Nice.

3998
02:35:09,300 --> 02:35:10,370
Great.

3999
02:35:13,940 --> 02:35:15,570
- We're safe.
- I thought I'd be going home.

4000
02:35:15,870 --> 02:35:17,410
- Oh, my.
- We got to prolong our lives here.

4001
02:35:18,040 --> 02:35:20,080
We might be able to get more lives.

4002
02:35:20,180 --> 02:35:21,180
Right.

4003
02:35:21,180 --> 02:35:23,350
We'll get half.
So it will be either 3 or 4.

4004
02:35:23,350 --> 02:35:26,620
Or did they hide more lives?
Could it be five?

4005
02:35:26,620 --> 02:35:29,090
I was expecting three at least.
I wondered how many lives there were.

4006
02:35:29,090 --> 02:35:31,960
I wanted to see how hard
they were bluffing all this time.

4007
02:35:32,060 --> 02:35:33,260
Five? Or four?

4008
02:35:33,660 --> 02:35:35,630
I thought, "We're safe."

4009
02:35:35,960 --> 02:35:38,960
Here are the total resources...

4010
02:35:38,960 --> 02:35:40,730
Team Blue must hand over...

4011
02:35:40,730 --> 02:35:42,600
- This is important.
- to Team White as spoils of war.

4012
02:35:44,100 --> 02:35:46,040
Thirty-three diamonds.

4013
02:35:47,570 --> 02:35:48,940
- Half of that.
- That's an odd number.

4014
02:35:50,710 --> 02:35:52,380
Zero lives.

4015
02:35:53,650 --> 02:35:55,110
- What?
- What?

4016
02:35:58,480 --> 02:36:00,020
Zero credits.

4017
02:36:00,750 --> 02:36:03,890
(Spoils Settlement)

4018
02:36:04,460 --> 02:36:05,990
- They sold everything.
- They sold everything.

4019
02:36:05,990 --> 02:36:07,660
- They sold everything.
- They sold through the Platform.

4020
02:36:09,090 --> 02:36:10,830
- They've got nothing.
- Yes, they sold everything.

4021
02:36:10,960 --> 02:36:12,660
- They must've sold everything to Black.
- Yes, they did.

4022
02:36:12,660 --> 02:36:13,700
Exactly.

4023
02:36:15,070 --> 02:36:16,130
We're going home.

4024
02:36:29,820 --> 02:36:31,280
(During today's lunch)

4025
02:36:31,550 --> 02:36:33,620
We just have to get there first
to start the war.

4026
02:36:33,920 --> 02:36:35,290
Then...

4027
02:36:36,660 --> 02:36:38,090
let me hold onto your lives.

4028
02:36:40,660 --> 02:36:41,860
- I'll give you diamonds.
- On the Platform?

4029
02:36:42,530 --> 02:36:43,730
- You might lose to them.
- That's...

4030
02:36:43,730 --> 02:36:45,430
- That's not a bad idea.
- That's a good idea.

4031
02:36:45,600 --> 02:36:47,530
I'll hold onto them.
They'll be your collateral.

4032
02:36:47,530 --> 02:36:48,600
- Sounds good.
- Yes.

4033
02:36:48,700 --> 02:36:50,340
If you lose, I can return them to you.

4034
02:36:50,340 --> 02:36:51,570
That's great.

4035
02:36:51,570 --> 02:36:54,010
- But here's what I want in return.
- What do you want?

4036
02:36:54,140 --> 02:36:56,840
As for the spoils of war,

4037
02:36:57,140 --> 02:36:59,310
I want you to sell them to me.
I'm not asking you to give them for free.

4038
02:36:59,780 --> 02:37:01,510
- But only when you guys win.
- Okay.

4039
02:37:01,650 --> 02:37:02,850
I'll run over...

4040
02:37:02,850 --> 02:37:04,520
- and do this deal through the Platform.
- Yes.

4041
02:37:04,520 --> 02:37:05,850
Go and do that first.

4042
02:37:05,950 --> 02:37:09,820
(She heads over to the Platform
during lunch before trading.)

4043
02:37:12,520 --> 02:37:14,090
I brought our lives.

4044
02:37:14,730 --> 02:37:16,700
- How many did you bring?
- I brought everything.

4045
02:37:16,700 --> 02:37:17,860
- Everything?
- Yes.

4046
02:37:18,530 --> 02:37:21,170
(Pitou told him she would hand over
all the lives Team Blue had.)

4047
02:37:21,730 --> 02:37:23,540
(Team Blue has 14 lives
according to the system.)

4048
02:37:24,040 --> 02:37:27,840
(That includes the life they tried
to sell through an illegal trade.)

4049
02:37:30,840 --> 02:37:34,710
Resources can only be traded
during the trading session.

4050
02:37:34,850 --> 02:37:35,910
What?

4051
02:37:35,910 --> 02:37:37,280
(She can only trade for food
during lunch.)

4052
02:37:37,280 --> 02:37:38,420
We can't do this now?

4053
02:37:38,420 --> 02:37:40,020
We have to do this
right before the war then.

4054
02:37:40,020 --> 02:37:41,250
I'll stay here then.

4055
02:37:41,690 --> 02:37:42,850
- The whole time?
- Yes.

4056
02:37:42,990 --> 02:37:44,090
You hold onto them then.

4057
02:37:44,860 --> 02:37:45,890
It looks fancy.

4058
02:37:47,260 --> 02:37:48,360
Why are they so early?

4059
02:37:48,730 --> 02:37:49,730
Hello.

4060
02:37:49,930 --> 02:37:51,260
- Hello.
- Gosh.

4061
02:37:52,360 --> 02:37:54,700
(Team Red has arrived earlier
than they expected.)

4062
02:37:54,700 --> 02:37:56,070
The Reds are here.

4063
02:37:56,470 --> 02:37:57,700
I'll hide them here.

4064
02:37:57,700 --> 02:37:59,970
(She hides the box in a corner
until the trading session begins.)

4065
02:38:02,340 --> 02:38:04,280
Congratulations on the opening.

4066
02:38:06,110 --> 02:38:08,480
(Lunchtime)

4067
02:38:08,480 --> 02:38:11,650
The trading for Day Four will begin.

4068
02:38:11,920 --> 02:38:12,950
Let's go.

4069
02:38:13,420 --> 02:38:17,090
(She makes her move
as soon as the trading session begins.)

4070
02:38:17,960 --> 02:38:19,120
- Let's do it.
- Okay.

4071
02:38:22,360 --> 02:38:24,600
Could you not open it?
There are so many people here.

4072
02:38:27,070 --> 02:38:30,740
(Team Blue sells all of their lives
to the Platform.)

4073
02:38:32,100 --> 02:38:34,610
(That includes 1 life
Black was holding onto.)

4074
02:38:35,110 --> 02:38:38,710
(Black buys all of Team Blue's lives.)

4075
02:38:39,710 --> 02:38:41,080
Thirty-two points.

4076
02:38:42,050 --> 02:38:43,650
- Great work.
- Well done.

4077
02:38:43,650 --> 02:38:44,680
- We did well.
- Great job.

4078
02:38:44,680 --> 02:38:46,220
- We're safe.
- I thought I'd be going home.

4079
02:38:46,220 --> 02:38:47,920
- Oh, no. They think they're safe.
- Oh, my.

4080
02:38:48,090 --> 02:38:50,260
- They think they're safe. My gosh.
- That was great.

4081
02:38:50,790 --> 02:38:53,120
Well, we're not going to lose anything.

4082
02:38:53,690 --> 02:38:55,630
The worst that could happen to us is
losing money.

4083
02:38:55,730 --> 02:38:58,160
- I feel so bad.
- I feel bad.

4084
02:38:58,660 --> 02:39:00,630
What are we going to do?

4085
02:39:01,500 --> 02:39:03,640
They looked happy...

4086
02:39:03,640 --> 02:39:06,140
thinking they weren't going home.

4087
02:39:06,270 --> 02:39:08,470
It felt like forever...

4088
02:39:08,640 --> 02:39:10,540
to watch that.

4089
02:39:10,540 --> 02:39:12,280
Team White had hope...

4090
02:39:12,340 --> 02:39:16,350
of stealing our lives.

4091
02:39:16,450 --> 02:39:20,190
I know how desperate they were...

4092
02:39:21,650 --> 02:39:23,490
among themselves.

4093
02:39:23,960 --> 02:39:25,360
I felt bad.

4094
02:39:26,190 --> 02:39:28,290
- I feel so bad.
- Thirty-three diamonds.

4095
02:39:28,490 --> 02:39:30,630
What do we do?

4096
02:39:31,660 --> 02:39:34,030
- Zero lives.
- What?

4097
02:39:34,330 --> 02:39:36,130
Zero credits.

4098
02:39:41,740 --> 02:39:43,310
- They sold everything.
- They sold everything.

4099
02:39:43,310 --> 02:39:44,910
- They sold everything.
- They sold through the Platform.

4100
02:39:46,550 --> 02:39:47,880
- They noticed it right away.
- Yes.

4101
02:39:49,280 --> 02:39:52,380
They didn't get angry...

4102
02:39:52,550 --> 02:39:54,750
or yell, "How can this happen?"

4103
02:39:54,920 --> 02:39:57,520
They looked like they gave up.

4104
02:39:58,020 --> 02:40:00,260
I felt bad.

4105
02:40:01,360 --> 02:40:02,730
Where did all the lives go?

4106
02:40:02,730 --> 02:40:03,860
Why is it zero?

4107
02:40:04,360 --> 02:40:06,400
I've never seen them making a trade
through the Platform.

4108
02:40:06,500 --> 02:40:08,530
I didn't understand at first.

4109
02:40:08,600 --> 02:40:10,570
Then they told me later...

4110
02:40:10,670 --> 02:40:12,640
that they left everything...

4111
02:40:12,640 --> 02:40:14,410
to Black.

4112
02:40:15,010 --> 02:40:18,040
Since they didn't lose any lives,

4113
02:40:18,110 --> 02:40:20,480
I thought it was a pretty smart idea.

4114
02:40:20,750 --> 02:40:23,680
When the losing team's resources
were revealed,

4115
02:40:23,680 --> 02:40:25,020
I thought, "These punks."

4116
02:40:25,650 --> 02:40:28,390
"They were being smart."

4117
02:40:28,490 --> 02:40:31,060
But this means that our strategy...

4118
02:40:31,060 --> 02:40:34,590
and tactics weren't good enough.

4119
02:40:34,590 --> 02:40:36,030
In a war,

4120
02:40:36,030 --> 02:40:39,060
all you have to do is
do whatever it takes to win...

4121
02:40:39,130 --> 02:40:41,300
and keep damage as minimal as possible.

4122
02:40:41,500 --> 02:40:44,570
And I think that was their way
to keep damage minimal.

4123
02:40:44,570 --> 02:40:45,670
Although it was annoying.

4124
02:40:46,400 --> 02:40:49,340
None of us saw that coming.

4125
02:40:49,440 --> 02:40:50,940
That was like a deposit.

4126
02:40:50,940 --> 02:40:53,080
Selling it through the Platform...

4127
02:40:53,080 --> 02:40:54,880
was one way to do it.

4128
02:40:54,880 --> 02:40:56,380
I never thought of it.

4129
02:40:56,380 --> 02:40:57,920
We missed it.

4130
02:40:57,920 --> 02:40:59,250
It's our defeat.

4131
02:40:59,780 --> 02:41:01,650
That was a shame.

4132
02:41:01,790 --> 02:41:04,290
We didn't see that coming.

4133
02:41:04,560 --> 02:41:07,430
They crossed the line.

4134
02:41:08,390 --> 02:41:09,430
It's funny.

4135
02:41:12,760 --> 02:41:15,700
They knew they were going to lose
when they declared war.

4136
02:41:15,700 --> 02:41:16,800
Right.

4137
02:41:17,140 --> 02:41:20,440
But if you look at it,

4138
02:41:20,670 --> 02:41:21,970
the other three teams united...

4139
02:41:21,970 --> 02:41:24,080
without us.

4140
02:41:24,440 --> 02:41:25,880
- So...
- That's right.

4141
02:41:25,880 --> 02:41:28,280
Team Black lied to us.

4142
02:41:28,750 --> 02:41:30,450
- Because...
- This is so annoying.

4143
02:41:31,320 --> 02:41:32,450
- It's okay.
- Did you expect to survive?

4144
02:41:32,450 --> 02:41:33,620
- It's okay.
- It's okay.

4145
02:41:33,620 --> 02:41:35,020
- It's okay. You did a good job.
- It's okay.

4146
02:41:35,020 --> 02:41:37,820
- Isn't it nice?
- But this is all in vain.

4147
02:41:37,890 --> 02:41:38,990
They crossed the line.

4148
02:41:38,990 --> 02:41:40,690
- It's okay.
- Why did they make us run around?

4149
02:41:40,690 --> 02:41:42,130
That's what a war is about.

4150
02:41:42,130 --> 02:41:43,360
- It's okay.
- It's okay.

4151
02:41:43,360 --> 02:41:45,000
We did everything we could.

4152
02:41:45,160 --> 02:41:47,030
It was a good idea to buy weapons.

4153
02:41:47,300 --> 02:41:49,100
We got to reduce all our resources.

4154
02:41:49,170 --> 02:41:50,300
That's not the point.

4155
02:41:50,300 --> 02:41:51,340
We're going to die today.

4156
02:41:52,140 --> 02:41:55,010
We wasted our time...

4157
02:41:55,010 --> 02:41:56,980
(Leia, Journalist)

4158
02:41:56,980 --> 02:41:58,640
on stage they set up.

4159
02:41:59,340 --> 02:42:03,310
It felt like a wet blanket.

4160
02:42:06,320 --> 02:42:09,150
I didn't want to be in that space
any longer.

4161
02:42:09,950 --> 02:42:12,820
It feels awful...

4162
02:42:12,820 --> 02:42:14,860
to be made a fool.

4163
02:42:14,960 --> 02:42:16,560
I felt terrible.

4164
02:42:17,000 --> 02:42:19,930
I'm not saying we should be optimistic,

4165
02:42:20,000 --> 02:42:22,270
but ignoring all those possibilities,

4166
02:42:22,270 --> 02:42:23,400
they were being all conservative.

4167
02:42:23,400 --> 02:42:24,500
"We must..."

4168
02:42:24,500 --> 02:42:27,210
"kill them now."

4169
02:42:27,210 --> 02:42:30,340
It led to an extreme result.

4170
02:42:30,980 --> 02:42:32,410
That was quite a shame.

4171
02:42:33,040 --> 02:42:34,680
It was shocking.

4172
02:42:35,280 --> 02:42:36,720
I felt betrayed.

4173
02:42:37,080 --> 02:42:40,250
On the other hand, I was furious.

4174
02:42:40,350 --> 02:42:42,890
I was enraged.

4175
02:42:43,150 --> 02:42:45,090
They basically deceived us.

4176
02:42:45,090 --> 02:42:46,290
(Paul, Dancer)

4177
02:42:46,290 --> 02:42:47,890
There was no point of winning.

4178
02:42:47,960 --> 02:42:50,130
When I looked to the left in anger,

4179
02:42:50,700 --> 02:42:53,800
Genie and Pitou were laughing.

4180
02:42:54,330 --> 02:42:55,600
I really wanted to...

4181
02:42:55,600 --> 02:42:57,840
smash their heads.

4182
02:42:58,040 --> 02:43:01,340
In the end, Teams Black, Red, and Blue...

4183
02:43:01,340 --> 02:43:03,170
went after us.

4184
02:43:03,370 --> 02:43:06,980
How far does it go back?

4185
02:43:07,010 --> 02:43:08,480
When did it start?

4186
02:43:08,480 --> 02:43:10,920
Was it Team Black? Team Red? Team Blue?

4187
02:43:10,920 --> 02:43:13,050
Did they unite?
Are we the only ones who didn't know?

4188
02:43:13,620 --> 02:43:15,690
Did they come after us
because we were the strongest?

4189
02:43:15,690 --> 02:43:17,290
I was having a mental breakdown.

4190
02:43:17,760 --> 02:43:21,060
There was something they knew
between themselves...

4191
02:43:21,060 --> 02:43:23,160
and we didn't know.

4192
02:43:23,530 --> 02:43:25,530
Leaving that aside,

4193
02:43:25,530 --> 02:43:26,900
we have to let three people go.

4194
02:43:27,800 --> 02:43:31,300
We will now transfer spoils.

4195
02:43:31,740 --> 02:43:35,140
Fill out the spoil submission form
on the platform...

4196
02:43:35,770 --> 02:43:38,410
and submit it to the central box.

4197
02:43:39,180 --> 02:43:40,880
(17 diamonds from Team Blue
and 16 diamonds from Team Red...)

4198
02:43:40,880 --> 02:43:42,750
(are submitted as spoils.)

4199
02:43:43,980 --> 02:43:45,580
Checking the number of spoils.

4200
02:43:45,650 --> 02:43:47,750
Please wait.

4201
02:43:47,750 --> 02:43:52,990
(The total number of spoils to submit)

4202
02:43:54,360 --> 02:43:56,060
(Team Blue and Team Red
submit 33 diamonds in total.)

4203
02:43:56,060 --> 02:43:58,160
Team White, collect the spoils...

4204
02:43:58,160 --> 02:44:00,270
from the slot.

4205
02:44:05,600 --> 02:44:06,770
Checked.

4206
02:44:16,280 --> 02:44:18,580
Although I started the war,

4207
02:44:18,580 --> 02:44:19,850
I was hungry.

4208
02:44:19,950 --> 02:44:21,750
I own the Platform.

4209
02:44:21,750 --> 02:44:23,760
It's up to me...

4210
02:44:23,820 --> 02:44:25,090
to consume the inventory.

4211
02:44:25,120 --> 02:44:28,060
I am sad and sorry about what happened.

4212
02:44:28,560 --> 02:44:30,630
But it was really good.

4213
02:44:30,660 --> 02:44:32,260
Especially the wrap.

4214
02:44:33,230 --> 02:44:34,770
To be honest,

4215
02:44:34,770 --> 02:44:36,500
all this happened because of me.

4216
02:44:36,500 --> 02:44:38,200
I will be your pawnshop...

4217
02:44:38,200 --> 02:44:40,810
to keep the lives you're worried about.

4218
02:44:40,870 --> 02:44:43,980
Even if you lose or win after the war,

4219
02:44:43,980 --> 02:44:45,610
I'll give you back all the lives.

4220
02:44:45,610 --> 02:44:48,210
I got rid of one of the risks
for Team Blue.

4221
02:44:48,210 --> 02:44:51,120
I helped them participate in the war
without any fear.

4222
02:44:51,120 --> 02:44:53,050
Team White will be the first one
to purchase the weapons.

4223
02:44:53,050 --> 02:44:55,320
After they win by a landslide,

4224
02:44:55,620 --> 02:44:58,120
they receive the spoils,
but there are no lives.

4225
02:44:58,390 --> 02:45:00,290
I designed the helplessness
Team White will feel...

4226
02:45:00,290 --> 02:45:01,560
in that moment.

4227
02:45:01,560 --> 02:45:03,060
(Vector, Businessman)

4228
02:45:03,060 --> 02:45:05,460
The war will be so fun to watch.

4229
02:45:05,460 --> 02:45:08,670
I'm dying to watch everything
that happens.

4230
02:45:08,670 --> 02:45:09,900
It's such a shame...

4231
02:45:10,000 --> 02:45:11,370
that I can't.

4232
02:45:19,980 --> 02:45:23,380
The state of war has come to an end
as of now.

4233
02:45:23,510 --> 02:45:25,850
Soon, the leader negotiation...

4234
02:45:25,850 --> 02:45:28,520
and life submission will be held.

4235
02:45:28,790 --> 02:45:32,790
All residents must wait
in their dormitories.

4236
02:45:32,790 --> 02:45:35,760
I never thought they'd deposit it
in the Platform.

4237
02:45:35,760 --> 02:45:38,930
I think this was planned
even before we went to buy lunch.

4238
02:45:38,930 --> 02:45:41,700
Right. I don't think Team Blue
came up with it.

4239
02:45:41,830 --> 02:45:44,340
I've been suspecting Team Black.

4240
02:45:44,340 --> 02:45:47,540
Because I think Team Black gets to keep
what we pay for the war.

4241
02:45:47,710 --> 02:45:48,940
- Still?
- Yes.

4242
02:45:52,010 --> 02:45:54,280
Leaving everything aside,

4243
02:45:54,350 --> 02:45:56,950
I think we need to be more cunning...

4244
02:45:56,950 --> 02:45:58,080
- tomorrow.
- True.

4245
02:45:58,080 --> 02:46:00,450
- We need to tighten our grip on Black.
- Right.

4246
02:46:00,450 --> 02:46:02,550
With the attitude,
"If you don't sell lives,"

4247
02:46:02,550 --> 02:46:04,220
- "I'm going to kill you."
- Like I said before,

4248
02:46:04,220 --> 02:46:06,290
people have a certain inertia.

4249
02:46:06,720 --> 02:46:08,430
- It's not that easy.
- It's not easy.

4250
02:46:08,430 --> 02:46:10,900
- I hope we stay mad at all times.
- You do?

4251
02:46:10,900 --> 02:46:12,830
I hope this awakens everyone.

4252
02:46:12,830 --> 02:46:15,400
Honestly,
you don't have to be kind anymore.

4253
02:46:15,400 --> 02:46:16,800
- Guys.
- Let's fight.

4254
02:46:16,800 --> 02:46:18,100
Just be as cunning as you can.

4255
02:46:18,100 --> 02:46:20,040
We cost a lot, yet we look powerful.

4256
02:46:20,040 --> 02:46:21,470
That's why they came after us.

4257
02:46:21,470 --> 02:46:24,610
Keep that in mind and be aware of it.

4258
02:46:24,940 --> 02:46:26,810
- We've all gone through the pattern.
- Right.

4259
02:46:26,910 --> 02:46:28,280
It's a cruel world.

4260
02:46:28,310 --> 02:46:30,050
I think...

4261
02:46:30,050 --> 02:46:31,720
that there will be...

4262
02:46:31,720 --> 02:46:33,820
only one person left tomorrow.

4263
02:46:33,820 --> 02:46:35,020
- That's possible.
- Tomorrow?

4264
02:46:35,020 --> 02:46:36,920
So if there's only one person left,

4265
02:46:36,960 --> 02:46:39,490
one final member of Team White won't die.

4266
02:46:39,490 --> 02:46:40,760
- Right.
- Then...

4267
02:46:40,760 --> 02:46:43,430
let's issue 200 every day.

4268
02:46:43,590 --> 02:46:45,160
Credits? Who cares?

4269
02:46:45,160 --> 02:46:46,400
We'll get at least one question right.

4270
02:46:46,400 --> 02:46:48,070
- We actually don't need to...
- No.

4271
02:46:48,070 --> 02:46:49,100
do any productive activities.

4272
02:46:49,100 --> 02:46:50,870
- Because that person won't die.
- Right. No lives are needed.

4273
02:46:50,870 --> 02:46:53,370
No. That person can survive with that.

4274
02:46:53,370 --> 02:46:54,410
Just endure it...

4275
02:46:54,410 --> 02:46:56,110
and keep earning credits.

4276
02:46:56,110 --> 02:46:57,710
It was a good idea to buy a lot.

4277
02:46:57,710 --> 02:46:58,940
Yes, and declare war.

4278
02:46:58,940 --> 02:47:00,750
We could keep declaring war...

4279
02:47:00,750 --> 02:47:02,480
- and buy more weapons.
- Yes.

4280
02:47:02,480 --> 02:47:03,580
We can buy more weapons.

4281
02:47:03,580 --> 02:47:05,850
That's a huge leverage for us.

4282
02:47:05,850 --> 02:47:08,250
The victory doesn't matter anymore.

4283
02:47:08,250 --> 02:47:10,820
- Let's just drop the currency value...
- Just reduce the prize money.

4284
02:47:10,820 --> 02:47:12,390
Just kill time in the dorm for two weeks.
Is that what you want to do?

4285
02:47:12,390 --> 02:47:14,360
- Ruin the prize money.
- We'll all go down together.

4286
02:47:14,360 --> 02:47:16,230
- Let's empty everyone's pockets.
- You got it.

4287
02:47:16,590 --> 02:47:18,830
- We shouldn't declare war.
- Why not?

4288
02:47:18,930 --> 02:47:21,330
He gets to keep the weapon price.

4289
02:47:21,330 --> 02:47:23,400
Because Team Black gets to keep it?
You don't want him to keep that?

4290
02:47:23,400 --> 02:47:24,440
I'm sorry,

4291
02:47:24,440 --> 02:47:26,470
- but I disagree with that.
- That's wrong.

4292
02:47:26,470 --> 02:47:27,870
I disagree with that too.

4293
02:47:27,870 --> 02:47:29,610
- Just do it?
- Just buy weapons.

4294
02:47:29,610 --> 02:47:31,440
- That will just reduce the prize money.
- That'd be a scam.

4295
02:47:31,440 --> 02:47:32,680
Yes.

4296
02:47:32,680 --> 02:47:34,680
After we're reduced to three,

4297
02:47:34,680 --> 02:47:36,150
just start a new game.

4298
02:47:36,150 --> 02:47:39,250
The three of you can just leave.

4299
02:47:39,250 --> 02:47:41,050
The remaining three can refresh...

4300
02:47:41,050 --> 02:47:42,720
- and start all new.
- Sounds good.

4301
02:47:43,790 --> 02:47:45,160
What should we do about the lives now?

4302
02:47:51,000 --> 02:47:53,830
Do we get no more chances today?

4303
02:47:53,830 --> 02:47:55,000
- Can we transfer them?
- We can't.

4304
02:47:55,000 --> 02:47:56,200
- We can't do that.
- We can't transfer them.

4305
02:47:56,200 --> 02:47:57,470
Because we already transferred lives.

4306
02:47:57,470 --> 02:47:59,500
- Because that's their deal?
- Yes.

4307
02:47:59,500 --> 02:48:01,310
You can only transfer once to one team.

4308
02:48:01,310 --> 02:48:03,040
That's already been determined.

4309
02:48:03,610 --> 02:48:06,680
So it's going to be three people
on each team tomorrow.

4310
02:48:10,210 --> 02:48:12,350
So we have to decide who's going to die.

4311
02:48:13,380 --> 02:48:17,360
If Team Red can't get anything tomorrow,

4312
02:48:17,360 --> 02:48:18,420
one person has to leave.

4313
02:48:18,420 --> 02:48:19,890
Honestly, I feel close to them now.

4314
02:48:19,890 --> 02:48:21,090
- A little bit.
- Yes.

4315
02:48:21,090 --> 02:48:23,560
I feel pretty close to them.

4316
02:48:23,560 --> 02:48:24,760
But then...

4317
02:48:24,760 --> 02:48:28,230
- it's not like we owe Team Red anything.
- True.

4318
02:48:28,230 --> 02:48:30,400
- I know what you mean.
- Team White told us...

4319
02:48:30,400 --> 02:48:31,470
to join hands and go after them.

4320
02:48:31,470 --> 02:48:32,900
We simply accepted their offer.

4321
02:48:32,900 --> 02:48:34,040
Right.

4322
02:48:34,170 --> 02:48:35,870
And we were guaranteed to lose.

4323
02:48:35,870 --> 02:48:38,540
The moment the weapons were issued,

4324
02:48:38,540 --> 02:48:39,910
there was nothing we could do.

4325
02:48:40,240 --> 02:48:42,050
Honestly, if Team White was...

4326
02:48:42,050 --> 02:48:43,780
any smarter,

4327
02:48:44,080 --> 02:48:46,580
they shouldn't have bought everything.

4328
02:48:46,720 --> 02:48:49,090
They were desperate to win,

4329
02:48:49,090 --> 02:48:50,520
so they bought all three.

4330
02:48:50,520 --> 02:48:53,260
Right now, our economy
is completely broken down.

4331
02:48:53,260 --> 02:48:55,690
I don't think they would've bought
all of them...

4332
02:48:55,690 --> 02:48:57,960
if they had even a bit of reason left.

4333
02:48:57,960 --> 02:49:00,430
- But we already started the war.
- Yes, we already did.

4334
02:49:00,430 --> 02:49:02,430
We already started the war,
so they couldn't trust us.

4335
02:49:02,430 --> 02:49:04,670
We did push them into a corner.

4336
02:49:04,670 --> 02:49:06,670
- Right.
- They...

4337
02:49:06,670 --> 02:49:09,740
We can't criticize them
for buying every weapon.

4338
02:49:09,740 --> 02:49:10,740
- You're right.
- Yes.

4339
02:49:10,740 --> 02:49:11,780
We definitely can't criticize them.

4340
02:49:11,780 --> 02:49:14,610
- It was life or death for them.
- Exactly.

4341
02:49:14,710 --> 02:49:17,150
I'm saying I would've at least
discussed it with us.

4342
02:49:17,150 --> 02:49:18,780
- Why would they, though?
- Exactly, why would they?

4343
02:49:18,780 --> 02:49:19,950
We started the war.

4344
02:49:19,950 --> 02:49:21,320
- To kill them.
- Exactly.

4345
02:49:21,650 --> 02:49:23,550
- We were out for their lives, so...
- But in the end,

4346
02:49:23,550 --> 02:49:25,920
they didn't think at all
about the whole team.

4347
02:49:25,920 --> 02:49:28,960
If I were them, I would've
thought about it a bit more deeply.

4348
02:49:28,960 --> 02:49:30,730
But think about it this way.

4349
02:49:30,730 --> 02:49:34,230
If one of us were put at risk
of getting eliminated,

4350
02:49:34,230 --> 02:49:36,100
would you let one of us get eliminated...

4351
02:49:36,100 --> 02:49:38,000
because you're worried
about the overall prize?

4352
02:49:38,000 --> 02:49:40,840
Because we currently don't know
the currency value.

4353
02:49:40,840 --> 02:49:42,970
But they do know the value.

4354
02:49:42,970 --> 02:49:45,280
- I wish they would've at least...
- So I...

4355
02:49:45,280 --> 02:49:47,880
I'm a bit worried about this.

4356
02:49:47,880 --> 02:49:50,850
Are you the kind of person
who will save your team members,

4357
02:49:50,850 --> 02:49:54,990
even if the total prize becomes zero?

4358
02:49:54,990 --> 02:49:56,720
- I got a bit scared about that.
- Me?

4359
02:49:56,720 --> 02:49:58,490
But we're a team of three.

4360
02:49:58,490 --> 02:50:01,430
If we were a team of six like them
and I was the leader,

4361
02:50:01,430 --> 02:50:04,300
I think I would've
at least discussed this beforehand.

4362
02:50:04,730 --> 02:50:06,460
The other teams
are teams of three, three, and one.

4363
02:50:06,460 --> 02:50:07,630
But the thing is,

4364
02:50:07,630 --> 02:50:09,200
even you were saying...

4365
02:50:09,200 --> 02:50:10,330
you became attached to Team Red.

4366
02:50:10,330 --> 02:50:12,170
- Those six must be so close.
- Exactly.

4367
02:50:12,170 --> 02:50:14,440
- That's true.
- Even losing one person...

4368
02:50:14,440 --> 02:50:16,170
- would be super sad for them.
- Exactly.

4369
02:50:16,170 --> 02:50:19,440
It would be wrong of the leader...

4370
02:50:19,440 --> 02:50:22,010
not to do their best
to save that one person...

4371
02:50:22,010 --> 02:50:23,380
just because they know...

4372
02:50:23,380 --> 02:50:26,120
- the total prize will become zero.
- Exactly.

4373
02:50:26,120 --> 02:50:28,150
Exactly. That's true.

4374
02:50:28,150 --> 02:50:31,220
At this point now,

4375
02:50:31,220 --> 02:50:33,620
everyone probably thinks
it's better to go home...

4376
02:50:33,620 --> 02:50:35,160
with just 500 dollars than to...

4377
02:50:42,870 --> 02:50:45,500
I mean, to be honest,

4378
02:50:45,500 --> 02:50:48,170
I'm only thinking this way
because I'm not them.

4379
02:50:48,370 --> 02:50:50,110
Hold on. What is it?

4380
02:50:50,810 --> 02:50:54,010
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

4381
02:50:54,050 --> 02:50:56,180
The leader negotiation...

4382
02:50:56,180 --> 02:50:58,750
and life submission will be held soon.

4383
02:50:58,750 --> 02:51:02,020
All team leaders,
please gather necessary resources...

4384
02:51:02,020 --> 02:51:04,920
and head to the Community Center.

4385
02:51:06,560 --> 02:51:09,960
During today's leader negotiation,

4386
02:51:09,960 --> 02:51:13,430
if Black goes,
"I won't give you any lives..."

4387
02:51:13,630 --> 02:51:14,730
Blue will all die too.

4388
02:51:14,730 --> 02:51:16,330
Exactly. Blue will all die.

4389
02:51:16,530 --> 02:51:18,400
We won't go home today, right?

4390
02:51:18,740 --> 02:51:21,540
Black won't deny us lives, right?

4391
02:51:21,540 --> 02:51:23,440
I know that won't happen,
but I just said so...

4392
02:51:23,440 --> 02:51:24,580
because I'm scared.

4393
02:51:24,580 --> 02:51:27,010
Don't do that.

4394
02:51:27,550 --> 02:51:29,510
If so, only the two of us will go home.

4395
02:51:30,280 --> 02:51:31,380
Why?

4396
02:51:31,380 --> 02:51:32,450
You're the leader.

4397
02:51:32,920 --> 02:51:34,820
What? Is that how it works?

4398
02:51:34,820 --> 02:51:36,620
Do I not also die
if I don't stick mine in?

4399
02:51:36,990 --> 02:51:38,060
You don't.

4400
02:51:38,690 --> 02:51:41,390
One person from each team
will always remain.

4401
02:51:41,390 --> 02:51:45,360
- If only one person is left...
- I'd rather go home together...

4402
02:51:45,360 --> 02:51:46,730
- than that happens.
- But...

4403
02:51:46,730 --> 02:51:48,100
How would I do
the productive activities alone?

4404
02:51:48,230 --> 02:51:49,800
That would be so sad.

4405
02:51:52,100 --> 02:51:53,440
I got it.

4406
02:51:55,540 --> 02:51:57,240
- I'll be back.
- Okay.

4407
02:51:57,880 --> 02:52:00,780
This might be an unpopular opinion,

4408
02:52:01,050 --> 02:52:02,880
but I think it's right
for whoever is needed to stay.

4409
02:52:02,880 --> 02:52:04,250
It's hard to find three.

4410
02:52:04,250 --> 02:52:05,550
Someone to send? Me.

4411
02:52:05,880 --> 02:52:07,590
- You.
- I can go too.

4412
02:52:07,590 --> 02:52:08,590
Let's go together, then.

4413
02:52:08,790 --> 02:52:10,960
- Okay.
- But you don't have to go.

4414
02:52:10,960 --> 02:52:13,190
Instead of just thinking, "I should go,"

4415
02:52:13,190 --> 02:52:15,230
I want us to be very objective...

4416
02:52:15,230 --> 02:52:16,460
But we already did...

4417
02:52:16,460 --> 02:52:18,260
- our part for today.
- This is all that's left.

4418
02:52:18,260 --> 02:52:19,400
One of you two has to live.

4419
02:52:19,400 --> 02:52:20,460
- No.
- Look.

4420
02:52:20,460 --> 02:52:22,200
Instead, I want us to do this.

4421
02:52:22,200 --> 02:52:23,630
I think you're so kind, Luna.

4422
02:52:23,630 --> 02:52:25,270
What I'm worried about...

4423
02:52:25,270 --> 02:52:26,640
is that you can't be tough.

4424
02:52:26,640 --> 02:52:28,570
This is what I think.

4425
02:52:28,570 --> 02:52:30,610
I think Siseon, Leia, and I...

4426
02:52:30,610 --> 02:52:32,780
are similar types of people.

4427
02:52:32,780 --> 02:52:35,150
If so, we should keep the two people...

4428
02:52:35,150 --> 02:52:37,650
who are good at solving problems
and being persuasive,

4429
02:52:37,650 --> 02:52:39,850
and we need one person
who can do something else,

4430
02:52:39,850 --> 02:52:41,720
like take action...

4431
02:52:42,250 --> 02:52:43,650
for Team White.

4432
02:52:44,190 --> 02:52:47,190
The strategies I came up with...

4433
02:52:47,190 --> 02:52:48,760
have been well used already.

4434
02:52:58,770 --> 02:53:00,770
Then I think it would be good for us...

4435
02:53:00,770 --> 02:53:03,740
to discuss which three
would make the dream team.

4436
02:53:03,740 --> 02:53:04,780
I...

4437
02:53:05,280 --> 02:53:06,980
In about an hour,

4438
02:53:07,510 --> 02:53:10,250
I'll go last for the life submission,

4439
02:53:10,250 --> 02:53:11,750
so if you feel frustrated,

4440
02:53:11,750 --> 02:53:12,750
- come out.
- Okay.

4441
02:53:12,750 --> 02:53:14,020
- I'll come out in a bit.
- Okay.

4442
02:53:14,020 --> 02:53:15,820
You'll have to wait a while.

4443
02:53:30,400 --> 02:53:32,870
This is going to be a bit awkward
for everyone.

4444
02:53:32,870 --> 02:53:34,140
Let's go together, Maillard.

4445
02:53:35,040 --> 02:53:36,140
But...

4446
02:53:36,640 --> 02:53:37,680
do you trust Black?

4447
02:53:38,340 --> 02:53:40,210
If Black gives the lives to White...

4448
02:53:41,050 --> 02:53:42,880
If Black betrays us here...

4449
02:53:42,880 --> 02:53:44,680
If so, I'll be left alone.

4450
02:53:44,880 --> 02:53:47,690
Imagine me doing
productive activities alone.

4451
02:53:48,120 --> 02:53:51,420
The community won't function.

4452
02:53:51,420 --> 02:53:56,760
But I think my team
is starting to break apart.

4453
02:53:56,760 --> 02:53:57,830
Why?

4454
02:53:58,900 --> 02:54:00,030
Who's having trouble with who?

4455
02:54:01,200 --> 02:54:02,530
Me and the other two?

4456
02:54:04,970 --> 02:54:08,140
I might go home tomorrow.

4457
02:54:08,140 --> 02:54:09,210
Why?

4458
02:54:10,540 --> 02:54:11,810
Kill them all today.

4459
02:54:13,880 --> 02:54:15,180
Look.

4460
02:54:16,180 --> 02:54:18,150
Kill them all. Then you don't need lives.

4461
02:54:18,520 --> 02:54:19,750
Then sell all of the lives.

4462
02:54:20,220 --> 02:54:21,390
Get paid in diamonds.

4463
02:54:22,020 --> 02:54:23,750
Then keep eating pork belly...

4464
02:54:23,750 --> 02:54:25,060
for the rest of the time.

4465
02:54:26,090 --> 02:54:27,220
It's perfect.

4466
02:54:27,560 --> 02:54:28,730
That sounds so nice.

4467
02:54:31,630 --> 02:54:34,300
Did you do some monitoring, Black?

4468
02:54:34,300 --> 02:54:36,600
- No.
- I see. You must've been bored, then.

4469
02:54:36,800 --> 02:54:38,040
I just ate dinner alone.

4470
02:54:38,040 --> 02:54:39,840
Really? At least you ate dinner.

4471
02:54:40,070 --> 02:54:43,270
I did want to talk to you about something.

4472
02:54:43,440 --> 02:54:44,510
Come here.

4473
02:54:45,910 --> 02:54:47,410
- One moment.
- Sure.

4474
02:54:48,880 --> 02:54:51,280
Before the leader negotiation,

4475
02:54:51,280 --> 02:54:53,250
Pitou and I were walking together,

4476
02:54:53,250 --> 02:54:56,020
and Pitou said, "I might die tomorrow."

4477
02:54:56,620 --> 02:54:57,960
That means she doesn't want to die.

4478
02:54:57,990 --> 02:55:00,760
I told her that there was a way
for her to not die.

4479
02:55:00,760 --> 02:55:01,890
She was interested.

4480
02:55:04,060 --> 02:55:05,600
- It's strange.
- Why?

4481
02:55:05,760 --> 02:55:06,960
My team members...

4482
02:55:07,900 --> 02:55:10,300
- don't seem to trust me right now.
- Why?

4483
02:55:10,630 --> 02:55:14,100
I said earlier, "Because Team White
spent too much money on weapons,"

4484
02:55:14,100 --> 02:55:16,210
"the prize we'll get in the end..."

4485
02:55:16,210 --> 02:55:18,440
"became almost meaningless."

4486
02:55:18,440 --> 02:55:22,080
"Would I have made that decision
if I were their leader?"

4487
02:55:22,080 --> 02:55:23,150
"I'm honestly a bit disappointed."

4488
02:55:23,150 --> 02:55:24,450
- I said so.
- Oh, Team White...

4489
02:55:24,450 --> 02:55:27,990
I was just annoyed
because it was another team.

4490
02:55:27,990 --> 02:55:30,750
If it was my team,
I would've made the same decision.

4491
02:55:30,750 --> 02:55:32,460
But the girls said,

4492
02:55:32,460 --> 02:55:34,830
"What you said really scares me."

4493
02:55:34,830 --> 02:55:36,990
Genie started saying so.

4494
02:55:36,990 --> 02:55:39,030
"That sounds like you would..."

4495
02:55:39,030 --> 02:55:41,700
"give up a team member for money."

4496
02:55:41,700 --> 02:55:42,900
That's what she said.

4497
02:55:42,900 --> 02:55:45,270
I mean, I would've done the same.

4498
02:55:45,270 --> 02:55:47,440
But I was just saying so...

4499
02:55:47,440 --> 02:55:48,970
because I wasn't in that position.

4500
02:55:48,970 --> 02:55:50,040
But...

4501
02:55:50,270 --> 02:55:52,210
they were making it sound like that.

4502
02:55:52,340 --> 02:55:55,010
So I felt a bit like, "What?"

4503
02:55:57,850 --> 02:56:00,680
It sounded like they were saying
I wasn't fit to be a leader.

4504
02:56:01,220 --> 02:56:02,320
That's how I felt.

4505
02:56:02,790 --> 02:56:04,290
Their faces and tone.

4506
02:56:04,820 --> 02:56:06,390
You probably will lose
your leader position tomorrow.

4507
02:56:07,630 --> 02:56:08,760
That might happen.

4508
02:56:08,760 --> 02:56:10,190
You'll keep all of them alive
for today, right?

4509
02:56:15,870 --> 02:56:17,500
If I don't, the system won't function.

4510
02:56:17,500 --> 02:56:18,540
You're a bit mad, aren't you?

4511
02:56:19,700 --> 02:56:21,470
If I can't stay in the leader position,

4512
02:56:21,470 --> 02:56:24,240
I feel like I'll definitely get out.

4513
02:56:26,010 --> 02:56:27,810
For now, you have enough lives.

4514
02:56:27,810 --> 02:56:29,510
You can survive for at least two days.

4515
02:56:29,580 --> 02:56:31,380
Yes, but...

4516
02:56:32,520 --> 02:56:34,990
- You could even survive for four days.
- But I don't know...

4517
02:56:34,990 --> 02:56:36,620
if they'll keep me alive until then.

4518
02:56:39,660 --> 02:56:41,590
Why wouldn't they
when you have enough lives?

4519
02:56:43,160 --> 02:56:44,230
You never know.

4520
02:56:44,330 --> 02:56:46,530
Because it's better for one person
to take all the diamonds for themselves?

4521
02:56:46,700 --> 02:56:47,730
Yes.

4522
02:56:47,830 --> 02:56:49,230
Will they keep me until the end?

4523
02:56:50,170 --> 02:56:52,070
I even thought this on the way here.

4524
02:56:53,000 --> 02:56:54,410
"Should I just act like..."

4525
02:56:54,840 --> 02:56:57,540
"I didn't get any lives from Black?"

4526
02:56:58,110 --> 02:56:59,740
Because at least one person
from each team lives...

4527
02:56:59,740 --> 02:57:01,050
even if you don't give them a life.

4528
02:57:01,710 --> 02:57:04,450
If this is your last day as a leader,
you need to make the first move.

4529
02:57:04,650 --> 02:57:06,520
Does Genie solve lots of problems?

4530
02:57:07,690 --> 02:57:09,020
Who did the most?

4531
02:57:10,520 --> 02:57:11,690
It wasn't me, for sure.

4532
02:57:12,890 --> 02:57:14,290
Then they'll cut you.

4533
02:57:14,530 --> 02:57:15,560
That's what I'm saying.

4534
02:57:16,360 --> 02:57:17,760
That's why I'm saying so.

4535
02:57:19,060 --> 02:57:20,860
If you want to be selfish,

4536
02:57:20,860 --> 02:57:23,030
you have to think about yourself,
not other teams.

4537
02:57:24,100 --> 02:57:27,100
Look at Team White change
in front of death.

4538
02:57:27,100 --> 02:57:29,740
I'm just telling you this
because you might regret it tomorrow.

4539
02:57:31,580 --> 02:57:32,640
Think it through.

4540
02:57:36,580 --> 02:57:37,780
(Occupied: Please wait.)

4541
02:57:37,780 --> 02:57:40,750
The leader negotiation will now begin.

4542
02:57:41,420 --> 02:57:43,090
All team leaders,

4543
02:57:43,090 --> 02:57:45,760
please stand in your designated positions.

4544
02:57:46,060 --> 02:57:48,790
First, here's the pollution index...

4545
02:57:48,790 --> 02:57:50,630
for the entire Community Town.

4546
02:57:51,130 --> 02:57:55,900
The total pollution index
accumulated over the past 4 days is 33.

4547
02:57:55,900 --> 02:57:58,000
- I see.
- Please note that once...

4548
02:57:58,000 --> 02:58:01,310
the pollution index reaches 100,
the town will be considered saturated.

4549
02:58:01,440 --> 02:58:04,910
In a moment,
we will announce the next agenda item.

4550
02:58:04,910 --> 02:58:05,910
Thirty-three...

4551
02:58:06,240 --> 02:58:08,680
Did you use five credits today?

4552
02:58:08,980 --> 02:58:10,880
Us? Yes. We only had five.

4553
02:58:10,880 --> 02:58:12,050
We used two. Today...

4554
02:58:12,050 --> 02:58:13,620
We probably used the rest.

4555
02:58:13,620 --> 02:58:14,620
- You used some today, right?
- Yes.

4556
02:58:14,620 --> 02:58:16,120
- You used two today, right?
- Yes.

4557
02:58:16,120 --> 02:58:17,790
I think we used two today, yes.

4558
02:58:17,790 --> 02:58:18,790
Okay.

4559
02:58:18,790 --> 02:58:20,320
Did you all use weapons today?

4560
02:58:20,320 --> 02:58:21,830
- They used all the weapons.
- We used them all.

4561
02:58:21,830 --> 02:58:23,260
But it doesn't increase
because of weapons.

4562
02:58:23,260 --> 02:58:24,600
- Right.
- I see.

4563
02:58:24,600 --> 02:58:26,900
So the pollution index
isn't affected by that.

4564
02:58:26,900 --> 02:58:29,000
- It's safer than we thought.
- Right.

4565
02:58:29,000 --> 02:58:31,000
But something might change tomorrow.

4566
02:58:31,000 --> 02:58:32,470
- Because as of now...
- Next up...

4567
02:58:32,470 --> 02:58:35,540
is the decision
to provide aid or impose sanctions.

4568
02:58:35,540 --> 02:58:37,140
First is aid.

4569
02:58:37,140 --> 02:58:39,110
If the majority of leaders agree,

4570
02:58:39,110 --> 02:58:42,150
two teams may transfer resources...

4571
02:58:42,150 --> 02:58:44,310
between each other without using credits.

4572
02:58:44,310 --> 02:58:47,320
This is limited to the resources
that have been brought here.

4573
02:58:47,320 --> 02:58:50,720
Through a transfer, only one resource
can be moved...

4574
02:58:50,720 --> 02:58:52,720
from one team to another.

4575
02:58:52,720 --> 02:58:54,660
There is no limit
to the quantity of resources transferred.

4576
02:58:54,660 --> 02:58:56,860
However, when a transfer is decided,

4577
02:58:56,860 --> 02:59:00,030
the approval of the leader of the team...
providing the resource...

4578
02:59:00,030 --> 02:59:02,000
must be included.

4579
02:59:04,400 --> 02:59:05,400
Then,

4580
02:59:06,470 --> 02:59:09,370
Team Red's opinion is important.

4581
02:59:10,210 --> 02:59:11,810
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

4582
02:59:11,810 --> 02:59:12,810
Why is that?

4583
02:59:12,810 --> 02:59:15,780
It depends on which team
you wish to provide aid.

4584
02:59:16,150 --> 02:59:17,280
- Really?
- Yes.

4585
02:59:18,180 --> 02:59:19,950
- I'll explain it a bit more.
- Right.

4586
02:59:20,680 --> 02:59:22,850
- I have all the lives.
- Right.

4587
02:59:23,320 --> 02:59:24,860
Team Blue...

4588
02:59:25,360 --> 02:59:27,460
pawned those to me.

4589
02:59:28,190 --> 02:59:30,230
Let's say I wish to
return them to Team Blue.

4590
02:59:30,530 --> 02:59:32,060
If Team White does not agree...

4591
02:59:32,330 --> 02:59:34,160
along with Team Red,
I won't be able to return them.

4592
02:59:34,400 --> 02:59:35,670
I need majority consent to do so.

4593
02:59:35,670 --> 02:59:37,400
Isn't that two people?

4594
02:59:37,600 --> 02:59:39,570
- That's how I understood it as well.
- It's a bit confusing.

4595
02:59:39,570 --> 02:59:40,640
- Right?
- Yes.

4596
02:59:40,640 --> 02:59:42,010
If it's two,

4597
02:59:42,010 --> 02:59:44,510
the team giving and the team receiving
can give their approval.

4598
02:59:44,510 --> 02:59:47,080
I'll ask. When providing aid to a team,

4599
02:59:47,080 --> 02:59:50,150
does majority consent mean two teams?

4600
02:59:54,220 --> 02:59:57,420
Majority means over half.

4601
02:59:57,420 --> 02:59:58,720
Out of four leaders,

4602
02:59:58,720 --> 03:00:00,520
the approval of three leaders is required.

4603
03:00:00,520 --> 03:00:02,060
- It's up to three.
- Right.

4604
03:00:02,060 --> 03:00:03,560
Only one must disagree.

4605
03:00:03,560 --> 03:00:05,600
It's hard to provide aid to a team.

4606
03:00:06,360 --> 03:00:08,570
I have a question.

4607
03:00:09,030 --> 03:00:12,440
May a single team provide aid twice?

4608
03:00:13,970 --> 03:00:15,770
Providing aid is allowed one time a day...

4609
03:00:15,770 --> 03:00:18,210
for only one team.

4610
03:00:20,310 --> 03:00:22,750
That means Team Red's opinion
is really important.

4611
03:00:23,910 --> 03:00:26,120
Team White has three lives.

4612
03:00:26,920 --> 03:00:27,950
Team Blue has none.

4613
03:00:34,860 --> 03:00:36,060
What are you waiting for?

4614
03:00:36,060 --> 03:00:37,660
Are you waiting for Maillard's decision?

4615
03:00:37,660 --> 03:00:40,300
Yes. And as for the number,

4616
03:00:42,230 --> 03:00:44,500
you should provide three lives.

4617
03:00:44,900 --> 03:00:46,400
- What?
- And...

4618
03:00:46,400 --> 03:00:47,840
can we talk more about this tomorrow?

4619
03:00:48,470 --> 03:00:49,970
- No.
- No?

4620
03:00:49,970 --> 03:00:50,970
That's not possible.

4621
03:00:51,610 --> 03:00:53,280
This is my plea.

4622
03:00:53,980 --> 03:00:55,780
There's a team
that will need lives tomorrow.

4623
03:00:56,250 --> 03:00:58,420
Could you offer...

4624
03:00:58,780 --> 03:01:01,820
the minimum number of lives for them?

4625
03:01:01,820 --> 03:01:04,520
The number of lives
that can be distributed...

4626
03:01:04,520 --> 03:01:05,990
is only two in total.

4627
03:01:05,990 --> 03:01:09,330
As you all know,
we failed to collect lives.

4628
03:01:09,330 --> 03:01:11,130
The maximum we can offer is two.

4629
03:01:11,130 --> 03:01:13,500
Are you willing to sell these lives...

4630
03:01:13,500 --> 03:01:16,000
to the team we want to sell them to?

4631
03:01:16,000 --> 03:01:18,100
I'm asking for lives...

4632
03:01:18,800 --> 03:01:22,140
to be able to distribute them
to the community.

4633
03:01:22,670 --> 03:01:24,540
I'm not planning to make money
off of them.

4634
03:01:24,540 --> 03:01:26,040
- Right.
- Right.

4635
03:01:26,040 --> 03:01:29,110
- Then, the number of lives...
- But instead,

4636
03:01:29,110 --> 03:01:30,380
- Yes?
- I will promise to give...

4637
03:01:30,380 --> 03:01:32,780
a reasonable amount of diamonds.

4638
03:01:33,280 --> 03:01:34,820
- So you want us to sell them, right?
- Right.

4639
03:01:35,220 --> 03:01:36,690
I hope Vector wins.

4640
03:01:36,690 --> 03:01:39,960
It's safer for us
if Vector has more of the lives.

4641
03:01:39,960 --> 03:01:41,830
Team Blue will never share their lives.

4642
03:01:41,830 --> 03:01:43,530
They will try to keep
their lives to themselves.

4643
03:01:43,530 --> 03:01:46,860
"Just give up, Pitou."

4644
03:01:46,860 --> 03:01:48,400
"We lost a lot as well."

4645
03:01:49,200 --> 03:01:51,340
Can it be four?

4646
03:01:51,670 --> 03:01:52,900
- Four?
- Yes.

4647
03:01:54,940 --> 03:01:56,970
I wished for five.

4648
03:01:56,970 --> 03:02:00,010
- We'll go with 4.
- If it's 4,

4649
03:02:01,040 --> 03:02:03,550
that's not a safe number.

4650
03:02:03,550 --> 03:02:06,150
We're in great danger right now.

4651
03:02:06,150 --> 03:02:09,850
The maximum we were willing to offer
was two.

4652
03:02:10,490 --> 03:02:13,660
I can't allow more bloodshed.

4653
03:02:13,660 --> 03:02:14,660
That is why.

4654
03:02:17,460 --> 03:02:19,730
If we can go out
for productive activities tomorrow,

4655
03:02:19,730 --> 03:02:21,800
we would be totally fine with that.

4656
03:02:21,800 --> 03:02:23,870
We would definitely be okay with
offering four lives, but...

4657
03:02:23,870 --> 03:02:25,100
But Team Blue...

4658
03:02:25,670 --> 03:02:27,570
I think we have to pretend
that we can't produce a lot.

4659
03:02:27,570 --> 03:02:28,670
We were able to produce a lot.

4660
03:02:28,670 --> 03:02:29,840
We did a terrible job.

4661
03:02:29,840 --> 03:02:31,610
They can't even produce lives.

4662
03:02:32,180 --> 03:02:34,750
Even if we use our credits,
we have to have basic knowledge.

4663
03:02:34,750 --> 03:02:36,680
Team Blue didn't produce many lives.

4664
03:02:36,680 --> 03:02:37,920
They only produced two.

4665
03:02:38,880 --> 03:02:39,880
Kill them.

4666
03:02:41,890 --> 03:02:45,790
But we don't think that will be possible
in this situation.

4667
03:02:46,060 --> 03:02:47,690
If the productive activities
go well tomorrow,

4668
03:02:48,090 --> 03:02:49,690
I will pay you that much more
for how many you produce.

4669
03:02:50,190 --> 03:02:52,060
I just want you to offer four for now.

4670
03:02:52,330 --> 03:02:53,330
- Okay, then.
- Who knows how things will go?

4671
03:02:53,330 --> 03:02:54,800
We'll go with four.

4672
03:02:54,800 --> 03:02:55,900
I promise you.

4673
03:02:56,130 --> 03:02:58,270
- I...
- How is this promise made?

4674
03:03:01,610 --> 03:03:04,010
There's nothing else we can do
besides trusting each other.

4675
03:03:04,010 --> 03:03:06,040
- Then...
- What must we produce, then?

4676
03:03:06,380 --> 03:03:07,380
Lives.

4677
03:03:08,180 --> 03:03:09,950
Then, credits...

4678
03:03:09,950 --> 03:03:11,480
- Credits must be bought.
- Credits must be bought.

4679
03:03:11,480 --> 03:03:13,120
- Credits must be bought,
- Do you have credits?

4680
03:03:13,120 --> 03:03:14,220
but we don't have credits to sell.

4681
03:03:14,220 --> 03:03:16,520
- Why are there credits?
- Credits must be produced tomorrow.

4682
03:03:16,520 --> 03:03:17,960
- Credits must be produced tomorrow...
- Right.

4683
03:03:17,960 --> 03:03:22,390
for our community to have over 30 credits.

4684
03:03:22,390 --> 03:03:26,260
We can survive only if we produce lives.

4685
03:03:26,260 --> 03:03:27,930
"If we produce credits,"

4686
03:03:27,930 --> 03:03:30,930
"they'll sell two lives to us, right?"
If we produce credits tomorrow...

4687
03:03:30,930 --> 03:03:32,900
with that thought,

4688
03:03:32,900 --> 03:03:34,740
- we might...
- So...

4689
03:03:34,740 --> 03:03:36,740
that is why I'm trying to secure lives
in advance as a guarantee...

4690
03:03:36,740 --> 03:03:38,240
as the middleman.

4691
03:03:38,240 --> 03:03:40,510
But that's not a guarantee.

4692
03:03:40,510 --> 03:03:42,510
- It's a verbal contract.
- It's a verbal contract.

4693
03:03:42,910 --> 03:03:44,380
If lives don't get sold to us tomorrow,

4694
03:03:44,380 --> 03:03:45,850
- we will...
- That will lead to death.

4695
03:03:45,850 --> 03:03:47,320
have one survivor left.

4696
03:03:47,320 --> 03:03:49,750
This team will have one survivor left.

4697
03:03:49,750 --> 03:03:51,960
That team will have one survivor left.

4698
03:03:51,960 --> 03:03:53,690
Will we gain eternal life after that?

4699
03:03:55,430 --> 03:03:57,960
Some people must disappear...

4700
03:03:57,960 --> 03:04:00,400
for the rest to feel happy.

4701
03:04:00,400 --> 03:04:01,930
If there's one survivor left in a team,

4702
03:04:01,930 --> 03:04:04,070
lives aren't needed.

4703
03:04:04,070 --> 03:04:05,570
The sacrifice of the few for the many.

4704
03:04:05,970 --> 03:04:07,170
A sacrifice is needed.

4705
03:04:08,170 --> 03:04:10,840
Don't you want eternal life on your own?

4706
03:04:11,840 --> 03:04:12,840
What?

4707
03:04:13,810 --> 03:04:14,950
- Me?
- Yes.

4708
03:04:15,180 --> 03:04:16,180
No.

4709
03:04:16,180 --> 03:04:17,980
- Why not?
- Without my team...

4710
03:04:18,320 --> 03:04:19,980
You must consider this.

4711
03:04:19,980 --> 03:04:22,990
If I am to think selfishly...

4712
03:04:22,990 --> 03:04:24,420
- and survive on my own,
- Yes?

4713
03:04:24,420 --> 03:04:27,520
the four of us here
will be the only ones left.

4714
03:04:27,860 --> 03:04:28,990
- Right.
- Yes.

4715
03:04:28,990 --> 03:04:30,430
Doesn't that sound exciting?

4716
03:04:33,360 --> 03:04:35,400
That's when a new game begins.

4717
03:04:35,400 --> 03:04:37,800
What did you say outside
before we came in?

4718
03:04:37,800 --> 03:04:41,200
You said that it felt like
two others would stab you tomorrow.

4719
03:04:41,640 --> 03:04:44,640
I'm making such a good offer right now.

4720
03:04:44,640 --> 03:04:46,410
- But...
- I'll be clear about this.

4721
03:04:46,410 --> 03:04:48,580
My team members suspected me
before I came.

4722
03:04:48,580 --> 03:04:50,580
- I see.
- That I might abandon them.

4723
03:04:50,580 --> 03:04:52,580
I said that I was being falsely accused...

4724
03:04:52,580 --> 03:04:55,020
and started defending myself.

4725
03:04:55,020 --> 03:04:56,790
I had to come out in the middle of that
because of the time.

4726
03:04:56,790 --> 03:04:58,860
I felt so uncomfortable about it.

4727
03:04:58,860 --> 03:05:00,960
These two were left behind,

4728
03:05:00,960 --> 03:05:02,660
and I came out on my own.

4729
03:05:02,660 --> 03:05:04,260
The last thing they said
before I left was,

4730
03:05:04,260 --> 03:05:06,030
"Then, does that mean..."

4731
03:05:06,030 --> 03:05:09,100
"she can abandon us for money?"

4732
03:05:09,100 --> 03:05:13,340
It felt like a ball of fire
was placed on my head.

4733
03:05:13,340 --> 03:05:15,770
I came out in the midst of that.

4734
03:05:16,340 --> 03:05:21,010
She suddenly started talking about
the distrust in her team.

4735
03:05:21,010 --> 03:05:23,350
"If this opportunity gets used well,"

4736
03:05:23,350 --> 03:05:25,920
"it will be a way
to wipe out the members of Team Blue."

4737
03:05:25,920 --> 03:05:28,350
I started getting this thought.

4738
03:05:29,320 --> 03:05:31,690
But if that happens,

4739
03:05:31,690 --> 03:05:34,160
only two of you have to agree
to change the leader.

4740
03:05:34,160 --> 03:05:36,160
That means there can be
a change of leader tomorrow.

4741
03:05:36,160 --> 03:05:39,100
That might mean the end of someone
will come tomorrow.

4742
03:05:39,100 --> 03:05:40,730
- That's what I'm saying.
- Luna!

4743
03:05:40,730 --> 03:05:43,130
We can make that happen
if you don't agree.

4744
03:05:43,130 --> 03:05:44,500
They're going to lose numbers anyway.

4745
03:05:44,500 --> 03:05:46,240
Let's reduce the number of members today.

4746
03:05:46,240 --> 03:05:47,470
I won't agree.

4747
03:05:47,470 --> 03:05:48,940
Right. Let's bring down the numbers
from here.

4748
03:05:48,940 --> 03:05:50,570
Three will be removed here.

4749
03:05:50,570 --> 03:05:52,410
Lives won't be needed anyway.

4750
03:05:52,410 --> 03:05:54,180
It's Mounjaro. Simple and effective.

4751
03:05:54,410 --> 03:05:55,410
Mounjaro.

4752
03:05:55,480 --> 03:05:57,180
No!

4753
03:05:57,180 --> 03:05:58,580
- That can't happen!
- Check this out.

4754
03:05:58,580 --> 03:06:01,920
This was a mistake by your members
who voted you as leader today...

4755
03:06:01,920 --> 03:06:03,690
in my opinion.

4756
03:06:03,690 --> 03:06:04,790
Think about this.

4757
03:06:04,790 --> 03:06:06,860
If we don't produce lives,

4758
03:06:06,860 --> 03:06:08,430
we will all get wiped out.

4759
03:06:08,430 --> 03:06:09,660
You won't be able to produce a lot anyway!

4760
03:06:09,660 --> 03:06:11,460
You produced two lives
starting from the first day.

4761
03:06:11,460 --> 03:06:13,530
How am I supposed to trust you?

4762
03:06:13,530 --> 03:06:15,770
Listen to this.
Let's say Team Red won't agree.

4763
03:06:16,400 --> 03:06:18,900
"I don't want to give
Team Blue any lives."

4764
03:06:18,900 --> 03:06:20,600
She will survive on her own,

4765
03:06:20,600 --> 03:06:22,540
- and her members will die.
- But if that happens,

4766
03:06:22,540 --> 03:06:24,770
- This is a crazy game.
- the system here...

4767
03:06:24,770 --> 03:06:26,580
will completely break down.

4768
03:06:26,580 --> 03:06:28,180
Will it really break down?

4769
03:06:28,180 --> 03:06:30,110
Listen to this.

4770
03:06:30,380 --> 03:06:31,480
Team Blue...

4771
03:06:31,820 --> 03:06:33,480
won't have to spend more lives.

4772
03:06:34,420 --> 03:06:36,520
You can sell it to Team White or me.

4773
03:06:36,520 --> 03:06:38,020
- Or you can sell it to Team White only.
- Team White and Team Red will use them...

4774
03:06:38,020 --> 03:06:40,190
until one survivor is left.

4775
03:06:40,190 --> 03:06:41,560
Right. Because there are enough lives.

4776
03:06:41,560 --> 03:06:43,830
Team Blue doesn't need to spend
more lives anyway.

4777
03:06:43,830 --> 03:06:45,760
Then, you should produce credits tomorrow.

4778
03:06:45,760 --> 03:06:47,500
I'll give this in return.

4779
03:06:47,500 --> 03:06:49,200
- Buy as many lives as you want.
- Right.

4780
03:06:49,200 --> 03:06:50,800
- What do you want to do?
- It's a win situation for me.

4781
03:06:50,800 --> 03:06:53,340
It won't even be your fault.

4782
03:06:53,340 --> 03:06:55,470
"That crazy Maillard didn't agree!"

4783
03:06:55,470 --> 03:06:56,540
Will you do that?

4784
03:06:56,540 --> 03:06:58,510
- No.
- She has a smile on her face.

4785
03:06:58,510 --> 03:06:59,610
- Right!
- No!

4786
03:06:59,610 --> 03:07:01,280
- She looks really happy.
- Why are you being like this?

4787
03:07:01,280 --> 03:07:03,010
How nice is that? If we don't agree,

4788
03:07:03,010 --> 03:07:04,310
we can get them killed!

4789
03:07:04,310 --> 03:07:05,880
What percentage are you at
to make this happen?

4790
03:07:05,880 --> 03:07:07,550
Are you all being serious about this?

4791
03:07:07,550 --> 03:07:09,450
It will become serious
if you make a decision.

4792
03:07:09,450 --> 03:07:10,620
Do you wish to do that?

4793
03:07:10,620 --> 03:07:11,820
Or do you want to stay
as a team of three...

4794
03:07:11,820 --> 03:07:13,390
and get stabbed and sent home?

4795
03:07:13,660 --> 03:07:15,290
Let's say I decide to survive on my own.

4796
03:07:15,290 --> 03:07:17,290
Will you share the prize money with me?

4797
03:07:17,290 --> 03:07:19,930
I'll give you some of the diamonds
in return.

4798
03:07:21,030 --> 03:07:24,470
All right. This amazing new world.

4799
03:07:24,830 --> 03:07:26,070
Are you ready to make it happen?

4800
03:07:35,680 --> 03:07:37,350
I agree to provide aid.

4801
03:07:37,680 --> 03:07:39,320
I wish to transfer my lives.

4802
03:07:39,520 --> 03:07:40,750
- I disagree.
- I disagree.

4803
03:07:40,750 --> 03:07:42,850
It's over. Negotiation failed.

4804
03:07:42,850 --> 03:07:45,490
Negotiation failed. Talks are over.

4805
03:07:45,490 --> 03:07:47,190
(Provide aid or impose sanctions)

4806
03:07:56,730 --> 03:07:58,670
Negotiation failed.

4807
03:07:59,100 --> 03:08:02,340
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)

4808
03:08:37,440 --> 03:08:39,140
(The Community 2: Invisible Hand)
